  <graph edgedefault="undirected">
    <node id="PRINCE">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Prince is a role addressed by Thuvia, suggesting a figure of importance and possibly leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title for a character who is involved in planning an escape, indicating a leadership or noble role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title given to a character who is expected to command an expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title referring to the character who is leading the fleet and is eager to get underway before the next day.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title referring to the person being addressed by Thuvia, suggesting a position of nobility or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title referring to the protagonist, who is facing a dangerous situation and is aware of the potential fatal consequences of being scrutinized by higher powers.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is a title used to address the narrator by Thuvia, indicating a position of nobility or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince is the title held by John Carter, indicating a position of nobility and leadership within Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Prince refers to the protagonist who is being disguised to infiltrate the realms of the therns, showing his role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a character addressed by Thuvia, witnessing the conflict and gaining understanding of the strategic importance of the warriors guarding the therns' domains.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a character who is addressed by Thuvia and is implied to have a significant role in the unfolding events, potentially posing as a priest.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a character who is regarded with deep respect and devotion, seen as a figure of authority and admiration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a leader within the party, being woken up by Thuvia to address a potential danger.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a leadership role responsible for making strategic decisions regarding battleship formations and defense.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a role of authority, as Xodar addresses him and requests items to reveal the corpse's identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is a title or role held by an individual involved in the mission to escape the stronghold of the Holy Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is addressed by Tars Tarkas, indicating a position of authority or nobility.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is the protagonist being advised by Phaidor to flee, indicating his leadership and central role in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is the protagonist whom Phaidor addresses, implying a position of nobility or leadership and centrality to the story.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b7e17d68c274e247f9a92e0dfa7535a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e51e1d8477880f7c52ccf46556e3c955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f212e50e14d429100cb7544cff0cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-123857b6c478330f85bc333d9a7eeab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36134f2c86fa620f5fc1afeb5c999e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4bd851a51f2718867c4b20dce63ae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff22eddd150fa9c82e1ebf3269b9831a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ff627f7e5d376dfb488b33baf21c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e8b4e5cb9fe7b6998ce2d6e059f797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6716a4317005ca2adb5fd451d6df6352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37d0a9a9b921ab61d9d45cce2805441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd3d00f92506b4a248933f3150a7352a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c11cfbe8d63489be093b9a14d65fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535538235eb01dfcd216bab7a901ead5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5387a5bebe527b5c1302cedb859b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d979802dde723cae7cce270dec2ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d663ab5c94c0659d8703cfef78b68e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebd37ffff0b33a7e235d87ed7805fbdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75779c31636c7f365a9d05b913893782</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIGHTING SPIRIT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fighting spirit refers to the narrator's renewed vigor and determination in the face of overwhelming odds.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bcc97b8466964e5aa69bc08566713a40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GARDENS OF THE CRUEL THERNS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The gardens of the cruel therns are the location where the narrator is fighting against the black men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bcc97b8466964e5aa69bc08566713a40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EARTHLY MUSCLES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Earthly Muscles refer to the physical capability of the narrator, which reacts differently under Martian conditions.</data>
