    </node>
    <node id="DATOR">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A Dator is a role or position associated with strength, as indicated by the mention of having the muscles of a dozen Dators.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator appears to be a title or rank associated with Torith, indicating his position of authority among the guards.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a high-ranking position among the First Born, associated with honor and authority, which Xodar held before his demotion.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a role held by Xodar, indicating a position of authority within the First Born of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a role or title associated with a proud individual who is defeated in a physical confrontation.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a role or title associated with fighting prowess and honor, used as a compliment in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a role or title held by Xodar, indicating a position within a specific hierarchy or organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a term used to describe a fighting style or characteristic associated with the First Born of Barsoom, indicating honor and skill in combat.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a title held by members of the First Born, akin to a prince, indicating a position of high status.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a title or position of power and respect, likely within a structured hierarchy or organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a title or role associated with Xodar, indicating a position of authority or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a title or role associated with leadership, specifically of the guards of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is a title or role held by Zithad, indicating a position of command or authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Dator is referred to as the first ancestor, a noble figure to whom respect is paid by the character raising his hands in salute.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64c0b713387801e1b22b06d3b9a3cc46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4a2f8784f599bc94defce14beef7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3964e585dee08446ad325587a718d0b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ae9b01eadc7f407e1d5bca34640588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-66576286b6b59d927ed315878d08d4a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68427a98a52f5c6bfa5aa4f4e34e079f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56d13213c1e66414a1713c9fa5cfdfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6935c77e3f98e0a9662defff47ba72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8888a7351a2f9284fdc4f2cc1a25d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5c0c969b2aa049ae080527d08909391&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5754b925c9ad697b90bdd239dbbb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cb52c113425589d349e2479393d8cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-11af4f76d96fedbeae481784201590d3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HASTOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Hastor is a Heliumetic city located far to the south-west, where the battleships are to be remodelled.&lt;SEP&gt;Hastor is a geographical location that serves as a destination for the expedition, significant in the strategic plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Hastor is a location that serves as a strategic point for the characters preparing for an air battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Hastor is a location where the fleet is stationed and whose people are questioning the purpose of the fleet.&lt;SEP&gt;Hastor is the location of the great docks where a fleet of battleships is stationed, ready to execute plans.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d663ab5c94c0659d8703cfef78b68e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb37188960dc17c3a250c133cc1d830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887</data>
    </node>
