      <data key="d2">chunk-196465999312ca6d83f3f81d85944eb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AIR VESSEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The air vessel is a ten-man cruiser mentioned in the text, which plays a role in the altercation by its anchor striking the narrator and others.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f6935c77e3f98e0a9662defff47ba72</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COURTIER">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Courtier is a richly trapped individual who emerges to lead the characters to Issus, indicating a role within the temple's hierarchy.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4a4c2a87c1f4e9cc424db7febe61149a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SPEAKER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Speaker is a character who acknowledges the protagonist's past actions and offers assistance to make their life more bearable, suggesting knowledge of the societal structure and fate of others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is a character who challenges Xodar's beliefs about Issus and suggests that they can control their own fate.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is a character who devises a plan to escape from Shador and reassures the boy about their safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is a character who encourages hope and freedom, and challenges the beliefs surrounding Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is a character who expresses gratitude towards another character for their courtesy and consideration, and offers a token of appreciation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is a character who reflects on the perceptions of weakness in relation to women and children, but demonstrates strength in other aspects of life. They also express love and concern for The Mother, which is recognized by The Boy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Speaker is an individual who has fought often in the arena and takes pride in their fighting prowess, maintaining family traditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac21fdcaba1072d7aae816bc5a5b7e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbf790c243f3e5d0d4de29cc208b1cfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6ace98e19b610b29e0db6de816d265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a22c0c45b96f211a7e6f3fec2419c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5883e77d0d77b28ad24e56e3db4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fe46f35811b518242ee5704c45d9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca4fd0f96467b5e870a8b2eb9b2d163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SECRET CELL">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Secret Cell is a dark, isolated place where the protagonist is imprisoned and threatened with dire consequences by Issus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4160da7474498abfc4e11860fbca61ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWORDSMANSHIP">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Swordsmanship refers to the skill and ferocity in using a sword, which is a significant attribute of The Speaker and contributes to their perceived stature and manner.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9ca4fd0f96467b5e870a8b2eb9b2d163</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MISSION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mission involves organizing a large military force to man battleships and transports for an operation centered around Omean.&lt;SEP&gt;The mission involves remodelling ships, assembling warriors, and targeting strategic locations for a planned assault.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db711ffa750bb33d7442d11412d8e06</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RANGE OF HILLS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Range of Hills is a geographical area where the young red woman was captured by the Black Pirates, suggesting strategic or tactical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Range of Hills is a geographical feature located several miles ahead of the protagonists, representing a potential point of escape from the Green Martians.&lt;SEP&gt;The Range of Hills is a geographical feature that was crossed by the characters on their journey to the Deserted City.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ce70b57630199d1d4144e52c899cfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fae3b8c057c10806b8855546fa2a43e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a999462c51c933f54b7da03b7f1fa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IRS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The IRS, or Internal Revenue Service, is the U.S. government agency responsible for tax collection and tax law enforcement. The Project Gutenberg Literary Archive Foundation aims to maintain its tax-exempt status with the IRS.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d2d0966e5a5e9985ffe55d85642aa4da</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEAD SEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Dead Sea is a geographical area that the protagonists have been crossing during their escape from the Green Martians.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7ce70b57630199d1d4144e52c899cfd0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CLIFFS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cliffs are a geographical feature offering potential shelter and defense against pursuing creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliffs are a massive, towering pile of rocks, characterized by a rough ascent formed by fallen debris and scattered boulders. They are noted for their lack of footholds and their imposing presence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliffs are described as a towering, gleaming face that rises nearly five thousand feet above the narrator and the cave.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliffs are described as rising perpendicularly from the valley's sward, presenting a potential sanctuary and strategic location for the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliffs are part of the landscape that the forest abuts, playing a role in the setting of the chase and battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a11c3e8c3e0a41f033f65d169562fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d66578f685f96545725c6926095d5777&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559d0add4d492cb1c4809fb59a95e633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a969533c3173ec88c8dc881084a5075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264ac3c16fad75dd9c5d97bf8e4b4ec5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEMPLE OF THE SUN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Temple of the Sun is a location where Dejah Thoris, Thuvia, and Phaidor are said to meditate for a year.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of the Sun is a significant location in the narrative, currently on fire and a central point of the unfolding crisis.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of the Sun is a significant structure consisting of six hundred and eighty-seven circular chambers, each accessible only once a year due to its rotation with Barsoom's revolution around the sun. It is used by Issus for imprisoning and punishing individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of the Sun is a smaller temple within the inner court of the Temple of Issus, notable for its thin spire and the many circular chambers beneath it.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c800b530f2a9aa4ac941241f419bdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae83a9d328abc751e8b03536497faf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46817f0e5364d880844af125e330b888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ROOM">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Room is a location that the narrator and others are led into, where the presence of Issus is encountered.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-46834d00b98b366f113489159b3f44a7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RESCUE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Rescue initially refers to the mission's objective to save Dejah Thoris, which has since shifted due to time constraints.&lt;SEP&gt;Rescue refers to the act of saving Dejah Thoris from the peril she faces within the Temple of Issus, representing a faint hope in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46817f0e5364d880844af125e330b888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PITS OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Pits of Issus are connected to the Temple of the Sun by a corridor through solid rock, indicating a subterranean aspect of the temple complex.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-46817f0e5364d880844af125e330b888</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROFESSOR MICHAEL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Professor Michael is mentioned in the context of Project Gutenberg, possibly involved in its activities or governance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6dc693d1fcbcbe36d61c6da9ecf262f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CEMETERY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cemetery is a location visited by the narrator and Captain John Carter, where Carter has a vault, marking a place of personal significance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-73f568e5559307a47b8b95fa17fa316c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOLLOW VOICE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Hollow Voice is an eerie and disembodied voice that chants a message of hopelessness and the impossibility of resurrection.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f7606a8748ac4d1fd0774bd9cf2a0ae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCORT">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Escort is responsible for halting the characters and conveying commands, indicating a position of authority.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd54938ae10297f91951e3dc08c03318</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FELLOW">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fellow is a character who exhibits furtive behavior, stealing glances and carrying the dead body with a cunning smile of triumph.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fellow is a skilled swordsman who engages in a battle, demonstrating agility and strategic prowess.&lt;SEP&gt;The fellow is the antagonist who used a ruse to put the narrator down and attacked with a gleaming blade.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32c5346403a0228de4126cc4c68535f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c0106b92cb6f20d3c3acb7b5cdb78cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3ad1e6cc14ff3d9d3bc55ad5d809034</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VOICE">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Voice is described as thin and wavering, yet accustomed to command, indicating a high level of authority and experience.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bd54938ae10297f91951e3dc08c03318</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CORPSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Corpse is the dead body of the enemy's fellow, which plays a crucial role in the narrator's fall and subsequent survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corpse represents the aftermath of a previous battle, serving as a reminder of the stakes involved in the current conflict.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f3ad1e6cc14ff3d9d3bc55ad5d809034&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63657b9d58bb2174ebfae1cd060b738a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISLE OF SHADOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Isle of Shador is a location described as having a small stone prison guarded by several individuals, suggesting a place of confinement and isolation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Isle of Shador is a distant island that houses a small stone prison and is guarded by half a dozen blacks, marking the end point of the described journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Isle of Shador is a geographical location mentioned as lying against the northern shore of the Sea of Omean.&lt;SEP&gt;The Isle of Shador is a geographical location mentioned as part of the escape plan, indicating it as a point of confinement.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da397bcf9850c3ba624363a75bf205f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd54938ae10297f91951e3dc08c03318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13123e8cc4e42bf2ebd1e6c36837aab2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE AIR VESSEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Air Vessel is a fair-sized airship, possibly a ten-man cruiser, that plays a crucial role in the protagonist's escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ef623f12c679dc785f41e5221408210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVINITY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Divinity is the belief in the deity status of Issus, which is ultimately shattered.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac8c4010c210dcbb6da5ccd528fdf874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PROTAGONIST">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Protagonist is a character experiencing fear and exhaustion as they are tormented by an unknown threat, constantly on guard to avoid an attack.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is a character imprisoned in Barsoom, experiencing isolation and receiving an offer from Zat Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is an individual attempting to navigate through a room of sleeping soldiers, demonstrating stealth and caution.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is an individual who is actively engaged in the struggle, attacking the blacks from the rear and fighting for Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is an individual who spared the Speaker's life and is now facing an uncertain fate determined by Issus, indicating a complex relationship with other characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is an unnamed individual who seizes the opportunity to escape by grabbing onto the anchor of an air vessel.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is engaged in a life-and-death struggle with the pirate, demonstrating quick reflexes and determination to survive.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is the central character involved in a combat scenario, fighting against pirates and experiencing intense action.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is the character who is captured and threatened by Issus, and is described as being unharmed after a descent into a dimly lit apartment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is the individual whose vessel collides with the battleship and is subsequently captured by the pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Protagonist is the narrator and main character involved in a combat situation, demonstrating skill and strategy in disarming and defeating opponents.&lt;SEP&gt;The protagonist is described as having wondrous beauty and prowess, capable of defeating seven of the First Born and taking Xodar captive with his bare hands.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0070ef1f1167082da565bcee6e79fbca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-452d661ef0dc01933f992e1f4cbb0181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c39c37bc3b545fc1976766cc4848db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5ed91aa2b973e3d2eacc4120957f423b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f514df6e2b51d4d8e31680e6f4a8cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b4e2984506fbfdf5c917bb3682edfbcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36f83701ff3cac994524405a183c1f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03e5883e77d0d77b28ad24e56e3db4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcd8c23863f19567a47b0d338bf750a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ef623f12c679dc785f41e5221408210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e982d0a53cb2c3721cfd5378e4bffd76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4160da7474498abfc4e11860fbca61ad</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROPITIOUS MOMENT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Propitious Moment refers to the opportune time for escape from Issus's control.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac8c4010c210dcbb6da5ccd528fdf874</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ANCHOR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Anchor is a trailing part of the air vessel that the protagonist uses to make his escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ef623f12c679dc785f41e5221408210</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POWERFUL MEN">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Powerful Men are unidentified individuals who have forcibly restrained the protagonist, indicating a potentially antagonistic role.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-170c5e513d0cfc27ab31c4132ea9d143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MY MOTHER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">My mother is described as a beautiful and beloved figure who is often sad and wistful, thinking of her lost love, and is cherished by her people in Helium.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0645e6d28537e5c8127826ee111f4dbf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FARTHER MOON">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Farther Moon is described as casting brilliant beams, contributing to the atmosphere and setting of the scene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-170c5e513d0cfc27ab31c4132ea9d143</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MY FATHER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">My father is portrayed as a man deeply in love with my mother, whose memory is worshipped as the savior of Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0645e6d28537e5c8127826ee111f4dbf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROFESSOR MICHAEL S. HART">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Professor Michael S. Hart is the originator of the Project Gutenberg-tm concept, dedicating thirty years to producing and distributing free eBooks.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-19f8d06d2291e3e24665b567daf90f0b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE HILLS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Hills are a geographical feature mentioned as being close to the escaping party, possibly offering refuge or a strategic location in their escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The hills represent a place of safety that John Carter and his companions are trying to reach.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49f2e6f0fef68b5f0a7f5923018ebed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e76d233bd322e66f43582e5859013c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PARTY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Party is a diverse group of individuals from different countries, colors, races, religions, and even worlds, united in their effort to escape a common threat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Party refers to a group of individuals whose faces are covered with silk, making them unrecognizable. They appear to have a secretive agenda and knowledge of hidden passages.&lt;SEP&gt;The Party refers to the group of individuals who landed on the sward and were subsequently attacked by the plant men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a7a4fe2b5df5b2ed0fabd95ff2a65a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d025c2fdd21d7a956f2705f12f6b69a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e76d233bd322e66f43582e5859013c2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOOMIAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Soomian is a character who terminated his pilgrimage and was devoured upon the banks of the Lost Sea.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOST SEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Lost Sea is a geographic location where Soomian was devoured, and where he had sought love, peace, and happiness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXECUTIONER">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Executioner is a role played by individuals who may be imprisoned with the condemned to ensure death occurs in a specific manner on a predetermined day.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eae83a9d328abc751e8b03536497faf5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="E. R. B.">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">E. R. B. is the author of the manuscript, who left notes about the story in his room at the hotel in Richmond.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLASPHEMY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Blasphemy is the act for which Soomian was killed, and which John Carter and Tars Tarkas fear being accused of if they escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRINCESS OF HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Princess of Helium is the title held by Dejah Thoris, indicating her royal status and importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess of Helium is the title held by Dejah Thoris, indicating her royal status and significance in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess of Helium is the title held by Dejah Thoris, indicating her royal status in the city of Helium on Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess of Helium is the wife of John Carter and a royal figure in Helium, experiencing sorrow due to the calamities that have befallen Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess of Helium is a central figure in the narrative, presumably of high status and importance, and is in danger of being attacked.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess of Helium is a significant figure who has been kidnapped by the black pirates of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess of Helium is related to the Jeddak and also concerned with the search for the missing person, highlighting her importance and connection to the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess of Helium is the title held by Dejah Thoris, signifying her royal status and importance to John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess of Helium, Dejah Thoris, is a key figure whose potential demise impacts the expedition's objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;The title held by Dejah Thoris, indicating her status and position.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c530bc2d8a3e5ffa6e7e1b615b196ddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ce6762a4b2ba2df84440f6782a029bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9313680f9284277c6d0068f59907d106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f65b8a5a48d5153729a3de1ec4ca4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c780b2690f7d5702006bb65b02e4811b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef83a1bb59d0a6160845638665b9ef6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5ed703fd05231acae40dc9a78f48c3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEVIL AND THE DEEP SEA">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Devil and the deep sea is an idiom used by John Carter to describe their difficult situation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRISON">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Prison is a place of confinement, mentioned in relation to the Isle of Shador.&lt;SEP&gt;Prison refers to the place where Xodar and the narrator are held, representing confinement and the need for escape.&lt;SEP&gt;Prison refers to the place where the narrator and Xodar are held, representing confinement and security.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prison is described as a confining space with solid rock walls that present challenges for escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The prison is a location with several chambers, each containing minimal furniture, specifically stone benches.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f3a6677c685c5edfb6994caf71b433ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9348949c540111a72093dbdd3189e57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d378cc6dcca5a19ea2b10af50a96bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04159352b966552000df8cf4feecf682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad069d3e03018513afb20c39dd315bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIGHTING VIRGINIAN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fighting Virginian refers to the protagonist of the story, known for his adventures across Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE NOBLE HUDSON">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Noble Hudson refers to the Hudson River, described as flowing like the grey and silent spectre of a dead river.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE LEADER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Leader is the head of the group who confidently leads the way to a secret panel and demonstrates knowledge of the hidden passageways beneath the palace.&lt;SEP&gt;The leader is a person who performs the action of knocking on the wall with the hilt of his sword to gain entry to a chamber.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68f1a6e31899408aeeec6a28a06f7b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d025c2fdd21d7a956f2705f12f6b69a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE COUP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Coup is the clever maneuver by the enemy intended to incapacitate or kill the narrator, which almost succeeds.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63657b9d58bb2174ebfae1cd060b738a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PASSAGE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Passage is a secret route that leads to the pits beneath the palace, accessible through a hidden panel in the wall.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d025c2fdd21d7a956f2705f12f6b69a8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PAIN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Pain is the sensation experienced by the narrator upon hitting their head, which paradoxically clears their mind and incites anger.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63657b9d58bb2174ebfae1cd060b738a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN NOBLE">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A Martian Noble is a person of high status on Mars who maintains a secret service for private security and intelligence.&lt;SEP&gt;A Martian noble is a high-ranking individual on Mars, maintaining a personal secret service to ensure security and gather intelligence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-682cfb3dc6d02c7c2e7994c7caa7c551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLD METAL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cold Metal is the object the narrator's hand touches while recovering from the fall, symbolizing a turning point in their struggle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63657b9d58bb2174ebfae1cd060b738a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECRET SERVICE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The secret service refers to the intelligence and security operations conducted by Martian nobles to protect against espionage and threats.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOLDEN CLIFFS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Golden Cliffs is a geographical location beneath the gardens of the Holy Therns, associated with the Chamber of Mystery and feelings of hopelessness.&lt;SEP&gt;Golden Cliffs is a geographical location mentioned as the vantage point from which Phaidor plans to watch a gruesome event.&lt;SEP&gt;Golden Cliffs is a high balcony location from which one can watch events unfold, specifically the great white apes tearing someone asunder.&lt;SEP&gt;Golden Cliffs is a rock-bound location mentioned in the text, where the chamber within its bowels is situated.&lt;SEP&gt;The Golden Cliffs are a geographical feature at the foot of which are gorgeous forests.&lt;SEP&gt;The Golden Cliffs are a geographical feature mentioned as a landmark in the narrative, over which the protagonist travels.&lt;SEP&gt;The Golden Cliffs are described as a landmark that, along with the templed gardens of the Holy Therns, represents a destination of safety or sanctuary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Golden Cliffs of the Mountains of Otz are described as a dangerous and challenging terrain to navigate.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-04a29095babe1a2ff500039fc4979ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ae3d51c8ed57d43c6b8f4465dfd95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89113c4da6f11aefb8678fe8526edbf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732154b0f5db90ca8982ebe025221f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0fb47cc5ccb52b699a384237e299809c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd96469a4962b32b193a14b2cae95e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WEB SITE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Web site refers to the online platform where users can access Project Gutenberg-tm's resources, search for eBooks, and find information about the organization.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29460a2778acd4b1b5cd5ba224e48c7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMAIL NEWSLETTER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The email newsletter is a communication tool used by Project Gutenberg-tm to inform subscribers about new eBooks and updates regarding the organization.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29460a2778acd4b1b5cd5ba224e48c7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VALLEY DOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Valley Dor is a fair valley on Barsoom that, if opened to the red men, would be a significant accomplishment for the expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical area encircled by the domain of the therns, often under attack by the black pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical area that lies beneath the Golden Cliffs, described as part of the landscape in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location associated with the strange shapes and reincarnation cycle, adding a mystical element to the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location described as a place where strange shapes walk, suggesting a mysterious or ominous environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location from which Phaidor, Tars Tarkas, and Thuvia are fugitives.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location mentioned as part of the sacred precincts associated with ancient customs and religion.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location on Barsoom where plant men are found in large dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location on Mars, situated far south of the equator, whose exact position is difficult to determine without precise instruments.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location that is part of the legend, described as wondrous but inhabited by horrid brutes.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location that the characters overlook from an opening in the cliff.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location that the narrator and the black pirate have left behind many miles astern.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a geographical location where victims are claimed by the Holy Thern, and where the subterranean passage of the Iss flows for a thousand miles.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location along the shores of the Lost Sea of Korus, where the beautiful Dejah Thoris awaits.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location associated with Issus and the concept of life and death, from which it is implied that escape is nearly impossible.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location associated with an age-old precedent of harsh punishment for fugitives.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location associated with the River Iss and is considered a final destination, indicating its importance in the story's mythology.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location from which Tars Tarkas and Thuvia are fugitives, associated with superstition and danger.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location mentioned as a place where loved ones join after death, indicating a cultural or spiritual significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location mentioned by John Carter as part of his recent travels.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location where John Carter is thought to roam care-free.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location where individuals are preyed upon by plant men and apes, and their belongings are claimed by the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a location where the tiny plant men, a result of the evolutionary process from the Tree of Life, are now found in large dimensions.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a place where the Barsoomians have been lured, associated with a terrible fate.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a region on Barsoom where the Tree of Life once flourished.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is a target location for the assembly of warriors and the fleet's strategic plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is another important location associated with the Princess's journey, possibly linked to the Sacred Iss.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is another location mentioned alongside the River of Mystery and Lost Sea of Korus, indicating its importance in the context.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is described as a care-free place associated with love, peace, and rest, a destination for pilgrimage.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is described as a land of false hope, torture, and death from which John Carter has escaped.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is described as a place of love, peace, and rest, considered Heaven by Barsoomians, where they long to pilgrimage at life's end.&lt;SEP&gt;Valley Dor is described as a significant place from which John Carter has returned, and is associated with sacred entities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9313680f9284277c6d0068f59907d106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eff6289e379a5bbb6ce19b0dc88aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdc154afb97906f6c0d9be300b69e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f45050d6a20b8b55e7285b8bb22a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9582d5fbcd0fec18f551d2401616b736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f6195017cf2ed0308d928aeccda715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec0c5c3f38231c4a87625db9626c95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c401d24eec318e7dd6ff9a98117d860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70f2bbb44eb678dedfd2d193e527d2bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a6342d219ff9538b029d45a991c42a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ff8e74ae364f7c74333f82d747443b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa250e31c575970c17ded33f099e84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9502067fd0cb8fc03f8323bae38b4131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96eb2a40b66ea789f0a4cd3f2ec63e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c3bee92a592b4fa42f49fe8b29d697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-633e94a7e73d5790348d90518684dac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7842012554cda4bb9f52354216e4a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5387a5bebe527b5c1302cedb859b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f651ea5c605f9f3d54a95f1c90c89a0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0958c186ba3135c1e8cf7f85bf340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6ecb83005b0a3ed19af31b7dc7a307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6337d09fdc42bf43f4adbf33b0f37655&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91388cfb9b19f81432eafb4bca1d653b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77544c11bdeae685d5cc57de932d4153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LOST SEA OF KORUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Lost Sea of Korus is a sea mentioned in the text, located near Valley Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Lost Sea of Korus is a significant geographical feature connected to the Valley Dor and River Iss.&lt;SEP&gt;Lost Sea of Korus is mentioned as a location associated with mystery and possibly danger.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a body of water located in the exact center of the Valley of Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a body of water located six thousand feet below the Golden Cliffs, depicted as shimmering in the moonlight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a geographical location connected to the sacred precincts and ancient religious beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a geographical location in the Valley Dor, associated with the Barsoomian pilgrimage at the end of life.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a geographical location mentioned in the ancient legend, associated with the end of the pilgrimage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a legendary location near the south pole, associated with adventure and exploration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a location where the narrator thought the woman awaited him.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a sacred place against which John Carter has allegedly blasphemed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is a sea where the river from the mountains empties, and is part of the setting described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The Lost Sea of Korus is located in the exact center of the Valley of Dor, adding to the mystique and isolation of the region.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-33f4de7021681b138c6572d77b66c4fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f45050d6a20b8b55e7285b8bb22a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7842012554cda4bb9f52354216e4a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9582d5fbcd0fec18f551d2401616b736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87b2173e6bc1dc31b41308980db1e72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6ecb83005b0a3ed19af31b7dc7a307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6337d09fdc42bf43f4adbf33b0f37655&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa250e31c575970c17ded33f099e84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26ef0b24e731f9a32cfb495e4f895d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNSEEN HAND">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Unseen hand refers to the mysterious force that caused the door to close with a sharp click.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb47cc5ccb52b699a384237e299809c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PIRATES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Pirates are mentioned as a group that might pose a threat, suggesting their involvement in conflict or battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pirates are a group that overwhelms the protagonist's vessel, led by Xodar, and capture the crew without causing harm.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pirates are depicted as a group involved in hostile activities, potentially capturing or threatening individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;The pirates are a group of attackers using small fliers to engage the therns, demonstrating reckless and fierce combat tactics.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d22f942245f43a066705ca39e7afcb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-452d661ef0dc01933f992e1f4cbb0181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d81037675f5b075ca39bbd7280bffb81</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNSEEN LIPS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Unseen lips refers to the source of the cruel and mocking peal of laughter that rang through the desolate place.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0fb47cc5ccb52b699a384237e299809c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROTAGONIST">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Protagonist is the central figure experiencing mental and physical strain while facing the threatening creatures, determined to fight and survive.&lt;SEP&gt;The protagonist is the narrator of the story, who finds themselves hanging by one hand from a vessel's anchor and contemplating the situation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f54e6e134d03ff91769cb5e4edbaeba6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GARDENS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gardens are a location where green warriors are engaged in an activity, indicating a place of strategic or combative significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gardens are mentioned as a location to which the narrator and Xodar return, suggesting a place of retreat or significance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2cc67bf329b29478328d22700eef5657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4953262a187c7f088ce754bc536a798</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VESSEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Vessel is a mode of transportation that proved difficult to navigate, causing its occupants to drift aimlessly for two days before being abandoned.&lt;SEP&gt;The vessel is an airship or flying craft that the protagonist is hanging from, which moves away from the scene of a previous battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a999462c51c933f54b7da03b7f1fa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THRONE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Throne represents the seat of power associated with the Martian deity Issus, a symbol of authority and control.&lt;SEP&gt;The Throne symbolizes authority and power, around which the society of the First Born is structured, with masses of people on both sides.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6bbfb90b7b84328adaa1e46f68731fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a027e972d7eb768695014c7c960f5758</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRANDFATHER'S PEOPLE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The grandfather's people are a group that loves and mourns with the narrator and his family, honoring John Carter's memory.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REMARKABLE CREATURE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Remarkable Creature is described as having a unique physical appearance, with a round body tapering to a thin blade and tiny replicas hanging from its armpits.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-528e772d9803ac855585b403871a1f86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TINY REPLICAS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tiny Replicas are small, six-inch-long versions of the Remarkable Creature, connected by a stem from their heads to the adult creature's body, possibly young or parts of a composite creature.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-528e772d9803ac855585b403871a1f86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MIGHTY POWER OF LIFE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mighty Power of Life refers to the secret behind a portal that John Carter unlocked, bringing life to millions on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREAT FESTIVAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Great Festival is an annual event held in honor of John Carter's achievements, marked by thanksgiving and remembrance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HERD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Herd refers to a group of creatures of varying sizes and stages of development, from tiny buds to fully formed adults, observed feeding together.&lt;SEP&gt;The Herd refers to a group of creatures, some of which have smaller specimens dangling from them, indicating a variation in the physical characteristics among members.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c70d613534f24ec10a67a59c4f2fe02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-528e772d9803ac855585b403871a1f86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEFEAT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Defeat refers to the potential outcome of the battle, which the characters are trying to avoid.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3cdc7ca0ada626816a0c812ad9e1df01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HILLS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Hills are a geographical feature representing safety and a destination for John Carter and Thuvia as they flee from the Warhoons.&lt;SEP&gt;The hills are a lofty range located directly north, offering concealment opportunities from potential pursuers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c843602d278a489f52282444efd5b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7a16642255b39659c194a76a94b26b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARIZONA CAVE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Arizona Cave is a location associated with a transformative experience for the narrator, where their body lay in a state resembling death.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0399b1611c31391a38e23605c6a4cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TREE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tree is a geographical location that serves as a temporary retreat for the characters during the battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3cdc7ca0ada626816a0c812ad9e1df01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BONDAGE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Bondage represents the state of captivity or restriction that the protagonist is facing, subject to the whims of Issus and the societal structure.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03e5883e77d0d77b28ad24e56e3db4f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARCH NIGHT 1886">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">March Night 1886 marks a significant moment for the narrator, rekindling their connection to Mars and their past experiences.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0399b1611c31391a38e23605c6a4cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONTHLY RITES OF THE TEMPLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Monthly Rites of the Temple are events where individuals are pitted against each other or beasts, serving as entertainment and reflecting cultural practices.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03e5883e77d0d77b28ad24e56e3db4f1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARCH NIGHT 1866">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">March Night 1866 is a pivotal event where the narrator stood outside the Arizona Cave, feeling a powerful attraction to Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-da0399b1611c31391a38e23605c6a4cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RELIGION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Religion is a system of beliefs that influences the customs and laws within the society, impacting John Carter's sentencing.&lt;SEP&gt;Religion is depicted as a belief system based on superstition and lies, manipulated by those in power for personal gain.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2dceb1683460906a1f380e987a784c31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEAD MAN'S REVOLVER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The dead man's revolver is a weapon that became available to the narrator when it fell from the grasp of a deceased individual.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32c5346403a0228de4126cc4c68535f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CUSTOM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Custom refers to the traditional practices and edicts that guide the society's actions and legal proceedings.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHAMBER OF MYSTERY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Chamber of Mystery is an event or location associated with feelings of hopelessness experienced by the narrator, indicating a place of significance and emotional impact.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber of Mystery is a location mentioned in the text, suggesting an enigmatic or secretive place where significant events occur.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber of Mystery is a location where the narrator heard the cruel and mocking laughter of the fellow.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6cb353d9a9d5f4be9cf6efd243bf6dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32c5346403a0228de4126cc4c68535f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMPARTIAL COURT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Impartial Court is a judicial body that has delivered a verdict against John Carter, indicating a legal authority within the society.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE DEAD COMPANION">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The dead companion is the individual whose revolver was used by the narrator to kill the fellow.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32c5346403a0228de4126cc4c68535f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LITTLE FELLOWS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Little Fellows are the smaller creatures within the herd, some still attached to their parents, and others feeding independently, indicating a growth and development process.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c70d613534f24ec10a67a59c4f2fe02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK PIRATE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black Pirate is an individual who exhibits hostile intent towards the narrator, characterized by a fierce demeanor and armed with a revolver.&lt;SEP&gt;The Black Pirate is an individual who narrates a strange tale and is aware of the approaching battleship, influencing the protagonist's actions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d22f942245f43a066705ca39e7afcb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9878ed9daf1be8baa0b54fae98e5e4a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PARENTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Parents are the adult creatures in the herd to which some of the smaller creatures are attached, suggesting a nurturing or protective role within the group.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c70d613534f24ec10a67a59c4f2fe02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BATTLE SCENE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Battle Scene refers to a conflict or skirmish from which a vessel is retreating, indicating a possible encounter between opposing forces.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d22f942245f43a066705ca39e7afcb84</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONTHLY RITES">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Monthly Rites are ceremonies held in the temple of Issus where men are pitted against each other and beasts for sport.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RAY TANKS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ray Tanks refer to components of a vessel that are affected by damage, impacting its ability to maintain course.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e2cb6922d0bff95becbc89209d302ce</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OMNIPOTENCE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Omnipotence refers to the single, all-powerful force that dictates actions in the heaven described.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHIVALRY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chivalry is exemplified by Carthoris's actions to help Thuvia and John Carter, showing noble and self-sacrificing behavior.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49f2e6f0fef68b5f0a7f5923018ebed4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FANATICISM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fanaticism refers to the narrow and extreme religious zeal exhibited by the Holy Therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARIZONA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Arizona is referenced as the location of a ghostly cave where the narrator experienced horrors and fearsome encounters.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d976a8fa9e1f5518efefe5f34b3de197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SELF-WORSHIP">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Self-worship is the practice of adoring oneself, exhibited by the Holy Therns, leading to their eradication of humanitarian instincts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GHOSTLY CAVE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ghostly Cave is a terrifying place in Arizona that left a lasting impression on the narrator, associated with horror and fear.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d976a8fa9e1f5518efefe5f34b3de197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FEARSOME THING">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fearsome Thing is an ominous entity that lurked in the dark recesses of the ghostly cave, instilling fear in the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d976a8fa9e1f5518efefe5f34b3de197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FAMOUS BLACK WARRIOR">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A Famous Black Warrior is a notable figure who may participate in the rites, representing a high level of skill and status.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b852a9d3367f81e14d5fe18d854c6494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONTHLY RITES OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Monthly Rites of Issus are recurring events involving combat, where participants' loyalty and purity are judged based on their survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The Monthly Rites of Issus are ceremonies involving bloodshed, where black men cleanse their souls, highlighting the ritual's significance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbe8483a1bbc19b7757cade3ab93f3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b852a9d3367f81e14d5fe18d854c6494</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STRANGE POWER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Strange Power is a mysterious force that has twice drawn the narrator through space, representing a significant and enigmatic influence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d976a8fa9e1f5518efefe5f34b3de197</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENTENCE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sentence refers to the judicial decision of condemnation that can be reprieved under certain conditions.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMPANION">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Companion is a character who, despite being dead, plays a role in the story through the bullet from their revolver.&lt;SEP&gt;The Companion is with John Carter, sharing the resolve to fight bravely and displaying a warrior's demeanor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6cb353d9a9d5f4be9cf6efd243bf6dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d728a27adf87f0a7a11d641afb689063</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THOAT OIL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thoat Oil is a substance used by Xodar to aid in the identification of a spy, suggesting its utility in security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoat Oil is used by Xodar to reveal the true skin color of a corpse, indicating its significance in uncovering hidden identities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-682cfb3dc6d02c7c2e7994c7caa7c551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebd37ffff0b33a7e235d87ed7805fbdd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REALITIES OF LIFE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Realities of Life refers to the awakening and awareness of the protagonist, triggered by the surrounding conflict.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6cb353d9a9d5f4be9cf6efd243bf6dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PIRATE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Pirate is an antagonist in the scene, characterized by his ebony hand, revolver, and intent to kill the protagonist, referred to as a "thern."</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b4e2984506fbfdf5c917bb3682edfbcf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE HERD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Herd refers to a group of creatures on Mars that move in remarkable leaps, resembling kangaroos in their locomotion.&lt;SEP&gt;The Herd refers to a group of creatures with single eyes in the center of their heads, pursuing the Green Warrior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Herd refers to a group of creatures with snake-like hair that react collectively to a strange shrieking wail, indicating their sentient nature.&lt;SEP&gt;The Herd refers to a group of plant men charging together, representing a formidable force that the Great Warrior confronts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-325b26f02d17fd6347079d1ba4fad726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-559d0add4d492cb1c4809fb59a95e633&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b274f937a3dc2f41dc46c714db0e1c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a293ca63ae749e20ee10ccd0b69b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SENTRY">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Sentry refers to a person or entity responsible for guarding or watching, mentioned in the context of the escape plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-784db098c3a71d77244da6e31d175ceb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RADIUM ILLUMINATOR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Radium Illuminator is a minute light source located in the center of the chamber's roof, providing dim illumination throughout the space.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cce81745da273c6b721f4e683db4bc6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCAPE PLAN">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Escape Plan is the planned attempt to leave the location near Shador, involving strategic timing and observation.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape Plan is the strategy devised by Xodar and the narrator to break free from their prison.&lt;SEP&gt;The Escape Plan is a coordinated effort by the narrator and companions to flee the prison and reach the shore.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-04159352b966552000df8cf4feecf682&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-784db098c3a71d77244da6e31d175ceb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885bf7dbe26f685a917110c8c81cfc01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE LAUGH">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Laugh is a recurring, cruel, and mocking sound that creates an atmosphere of fear and tension within the chamber.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cce81745da273c6b721f4e683db4bc6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DIVINE PRINCESS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Divine Princess is a significant figure to the protagonist, symbolizing love and longing.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VOICE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Voice is a hollow sound that chants from a far corner of the chamber, adding to the sense of mystery and hopelessness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cce81745da273c6b721f4e683db4bc6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHOSEN VOCATION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Chosen Vocation refers to the narrator's pursuit and role, which is significant enough to leave discourse for future generations.&lt;SEP&gt;Chosen Vocation refers to the protagonist's role or duty, which they aim to fulfill admirably even in the face of adversity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2417d5af6bb8ebfe1906e22eaeea4d53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED BARSOOMIANS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Barsoomians are another group on Mars, whose flesh is also considered suitable for consumption by the higher orders.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f38682fe044a197c2cdd15af662eef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAINTIES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Dainties refer to the additional delicacies consumed by Issus, hinting at the luxurious and possibly cruel nature of their diet.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5f38682fe044a197c2cdd15af662eef5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OFFICER">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">An Officer is a member of the group who observes changes in the water level, indicating strategic awareness and vigilance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Officer is a character of high rank, adorned in elaborate attire, who welcomes Xodar aboard the ship.&lt;SEP&gt;The Officer is a character who stands beside the protagonist, providing information to Issus about the protagonist's actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The role of an Officer in the Heliumite Navy involves navigation and the use of instruments to chart courses for vessels.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e0844027fa3550189a9d270364e85674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5c0c969b2aa049ae080527d08909391&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-67ff8e74ae364f7c74333f82d747443b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95bfe57ab079b1e2ed63627fb04566e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUBMARINE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Submarine is a craft moored with an uncovered hatch, indicating its readiness for use or exploration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Submarine is a vehicle used by the group, floating on the waters, and potentially pursued by another submarine.&lt;SEP&gt;The Submarine is a vessel mentioned in the context of a potential deception or strategy related to its location and status.&lt;SEP&gt;The Submarine is a vessel used to navigate through the underwater environment beneath the surface of Mars, equipped with powerful lights for visibility.&lt;SEP&gt;The Submarine is an empty vessel located at a wharf, central to a concoction or plan that is described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The submarine is a mode of transportation used to travel beneath the surface world through a tunnel, highlighting its role in the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The submarine is a vehicle that, if reached undetected, could allow escape to the sea and islands beyond Omean.&lt;SEP&gt;The submarine is a vessel from which the troops are exiting, indicating it is either sinking or has been compromised.&lt;SEP&gt;The submarine is a vessel used for underwater navigation, capable of moving through narrow passages and rising to the surface.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d28c03324ce7391ecbcf6ecd8eb6f962&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da397bcf9850c3ba624363a75bf205f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fb847572b8f4cd9bcb5e21934d38337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2dc607190379cdec50d1c32f9a6cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11bf730f5cfa3d77405e7d734e74488&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7407e663d0639c538204a4f83f2475d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61dacafb7778f4b0ffdd11993b73432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34a9e3055f88da17653657badc062d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95bfe57ab079b1e2ed63627fb04566e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLANT MEN OF BARSOOM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Plant Men are hostile entities on Barsoom known for their gruesome appearance and aggression.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Men of Barsoom are described as hideous creatures with snake-like hair that serve as ears, representing a strange race from the original Tree of Life.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-40e7a2060e2c27b443e01d4c73c7f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09006b13030957e1aa7f0ee75bbcb7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEADER OF THE HERD">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Leader of the Herd is a large member of the Plant Men of Barsoom, who initiates movement and is followed by the entire herd.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b09006b13030957e1aa7f0ee75bbcb7c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="QUEST">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Quest is the group's mission to attack the temple and navigate through tunnels on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a95bfe57ab079b1e2ed63627fb04566e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANAESTHESIA">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Anaesthesia is described as a strange state that binds the narrator, implying a loss of sensation or consciousness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a22e1ad1f3af901591bbdf5e3b5957aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUDIENCE CHAMBER OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Audience Chamber of Issus is a location where Issus meets with the protagonist, suggesting its importance in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c36f83701ff3cac994524405a183c1f9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GUARDS OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Guards of Issus are a group tasked with protecting Issus, engaging in battle against the narrator and the prisoners.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79bfaa16b39934f8800e01535bdd4dac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VOID">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Void refers to the vast emptiness into which the narrator travels, characterized by cold and darkness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a22e1ad1f3af901591bbdf5e3b5957aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED MARTIAN WOMAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Martian Woman is a young, intelligent member of a race known for their beauty and copper-colored skin. Her warning helped save the narrator's life.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6f1743e5cfa11d0a744fab2a0b4abb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE NOBLES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Nobles are influential figures who are part of the audience and are called upon to join the battle, indicating their allegiance to Issus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-79bfaa16b39934f8800e01535bdd4dac</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRISONERS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Prisoners are individuals chained in the chambers of the underworld, who sometimes turn against the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Prisoners are individuals held captive who engage in a fierce battle against Issus' guards in the arena.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prisoners are individuals held under guard in an enclosure beneath the seats of the amphitheatre, showing their subjugation and fear.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prisoners are individuals securely chained within the chamber, suggesting their captivity by the terrible creatures inhabiting the place.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prisoners are individuals who break free during the uprising, taking part in the battle against Issus' forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The prisoners are individuals held in chains, displaying emotions ranging from curiosity to hope. Their presence suggests a context of captivity or conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The prisoners are individuals who live under the control of the thern, sometimes turning against their oppressors.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-42f063e8c8fb8dc754a765041b551fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a027e972d7eb768695014c7c960f5758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202ae065926466ff564e922828d8ca62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ecb74cf43adde900703ca6804345ebe0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f1743e5cfa11d0a744fab2a0b4abb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b7627f226c0cffd3d7951ab5750969&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ae29e0662e7c7df5e1c335a0ba53d41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARENA OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Arena of Issus is a place associated with horror and danger, potentially linked to the fate of Dejah Thoris.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1ad7db4f246beb4b819a8f0994ae7c1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SAVAGE BRUTES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Savage Brutes are described as grim beasts in chains, contributing to a threatening atmosphere within the chamber.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c6f1743e5cfa11d0a744fab2a0b4abb0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EARTH MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Earth Man is an athletic individual from Earth, whose physical abilities are enhanced by Mars' lesser gravity and air pressure.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f09a293ca63ae749e20ee10ccd0b69b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHAMBER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Chamber is a fair-sized underground location beneath the city of Helium, containing chains and human skeletons, indicating it may have been used as a prison or place of confinement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is a location that is slowly revolving, posing a time-sensitive challenge for the characters involved.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is a location where Tars Tarkas is fighting against the monsters, suggesting a confined and challenging environment for the combat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is the setting where the narrator experiences a tense encounter, housing prisoners and savage brutes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-155a520841f1f147eaf186dab64b63b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6f1743e5cfa11d0a744fab2a0b4abb0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ce01b1948513d143cbcd4b1eddaaeda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea85a61fc6af15c21b035b16ff189849</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED MARTIAN YOUTH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Martian Youth is a character who appears at the doorway, showing curiosity about the narrator's situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Red Martian Youth is a fellow prisoner with whom the narrator feels a strange attraction, providing insight into their character and situation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49c756f350a29d8f5307a56d2cfe02e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe8483a1bbc19b7757cade3ab93f3d9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE STRUGGLER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Struggler is a person engaged in a life-and-death struggle, attempting to free themselves from a choking hold.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0534c79feeadfbc465eaaaa38c21aeba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREEN MEN AND WOMEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Green men and women are members of the wild hordes that populate the dead sea bottoms and deserted cities of Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17e1d860411b2b13228387bd01459577</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE HOLY VISION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The holy vision refers to a divine or sacred image, likely of significant spiritual importance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE HOLDER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Holder is a person exerting a choking hold on The Struggler, determined to drag them to their death.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0534c79feeadfbc465eaaaa38c21aeba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE DECK">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Deck is the physical location where the struggle takes place, providing a surface for the confrontation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0534c79feeadfbc465eaaaa38c21aeba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HER RADIANT FACE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Her radiant face refers to a female figure whose appearance is described as holy and radiant, implying a spiritual or divine nature.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ANCHOR CHAIN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Anchor Chain is part of the ship's equipment, serving as a hold for The Holder during the struggle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0534c79feeadfbc465eaaaa38c21aeba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHALANX OF ARMED MEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">A solid phalanx of armed men is a group of soldiers or guards arranged in a tight formation, providing protection or defense.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DAIS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">A dais is a raised platform, typically used for a throne or high seat, indicating a place of honor or authority.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXPLOSION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">An explosion occurs above and behind the protagonists, leading to confusion and impacting the ranks of the Warhoons.&lt;SEP&gt;The Explosion is a loud event that caused confusion and panic among the ranks of the Green Men, leading to their retreat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bc2a40b4b5725576e6c332e92d2fc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2417d5af6bb8ebfe1906e22eaeea4d53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BENCH OF CARVED SORAPUS WOOD">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">A great bench of carved sorapus wood is a large, intricately carved wooden bench, likely used as a throne or seat of authority.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="INTERPLANETARY SPACE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Interplanetary Space refers to the vast, trackless expanse between planets, which the Narrator traverses with uncertainty and fear of being lost.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0a229c550121312c4db9f9bbe4adbb4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEMALE BLACK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The female black is an elderly woman with a striking and repulsive appearance, described in detail with physical attributes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee7298aa7719687caf7748ba690182d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANOTHER SOLAR SYSTEM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Another Solar System is a distant potential destination for the Narrator, representing the vastness and unpredictability of space travel.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0a229c550121312c4db9f9bbe4adbb4c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REBELLION AGAINST ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Rebellion Against Issus is a collective uprising led by the narrator and supported by prisoners and other followers, aiming to overthrow Issus and achieve vengeance.</data>
