    <node id="THURID">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Thurid is a character who attempts to kick Xodar, showing aggression and rage when thwarted.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is a character who attempts to physically kick Xodar, indicating hostility and aggression towards him.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is a character who is requested to be bound and taken before Issus, indicating a significant role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is a character who was easily accounted for by John Carter, indicating a conflict between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is another individual who has been bound and is to be taken before Issus, suggesting he is an adversary.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is described as a noble and gallant individual, adorned with ornaments and arms, who is involved in a confrontation with Xodar.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is portrayed as a powerful individual who was easily disposed of by the narrator, indicating their combat prowess.&lt;SEP&gt;Thurid is referred to as a noble Dator, suggesting a role of significance or power, and is suggested to face the protagonist in a challenge.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64c0b713387801e1b22b06d3b9a3cc46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad953db00d8c2abdbfeaba1f774adf47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac274835cf15fd4d19a41f986b75a81a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1602bdc35e6e17999a40b105c63f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4638e15286baadf00497251d2c1faa42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5754b925c9ad697b90bdd239dbbb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8888a7351a2f9284fdc4f2cc1a25d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbd0fd5cca73331a533757f7f594757</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NOBLE BLACKS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Noble Blacks are a group of individuals who are seen reviling and cursing Xodar, indicating their collective disapproval.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4638e15286baadf00497251d2c1faa42</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE YOUNG WHITE GIRL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Young White Girl is a captive on the cruiser, bound and displaying an expression of horrified anticipation, suggesting she is in distress and hoping for rescue.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf01106365a33c764d09e06d53df8b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TRIBUTE TO ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tribute to Issus is a ceremonial event marking the end of individuals who have seen the divine glory of the goddess for a year.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbe729ce46c2462fad11275ee94493b1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BLACK MEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black Men are individuals on the cruiser, described as being sprawled about in sleep, possibly guards or crew members.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf01106365a33c764d09e06d53df8b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MYSTIC JEWEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mystic Jewel is an object of significance, described as sparkling in the center of a stolen headpiece, potentially holding symbolic or mystical importance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf01106365a33c764d09e06d53df8b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JEDDAKS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Jeddaks are leaders or rulers from whose courts the splendid beauties are taken to become part of the Tribute to Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Jeddaks are rulers or leaders of mighty courts, from which individuals are selected to serve in the retinue of Issus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbe729ce46c2462fad11275ee94493b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3356245cc78413b113811e37a4b2050b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SELECTION OF A NEW JEDDAK">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Selection of a New Jeddak refers to the process of choosing a new leader, which is a critical issue in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5ec04b19f44e50aea83ee65f6472738</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE STOLEN HEADPIECE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Stolen Headpiece is an item worn by the narrator, notable for containing the mystic jewel, suggesting it has been taken from someone else or another place.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ecf01106365a33c764d09e06d53df8b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZODANGANS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Zodangans are the opponents of Helium's fighting-men, who are unable to withstand the attack.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad8def4f34b963a5737d3ed48d75d4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OUR LITTLE VESSEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Our Little Vessel refers to the craft or vehicle being described, which is experiencing difficulties in maintaining its horizontal position and is at risk of crashing.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4402bc0fee69b84388050c068b5a22f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BATTLE OF ZAT ARRRAS' SHIP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Battle of Zat Arrras' Ship is a conflict where Helium's fighting-men board and overpower the Zodangans, leading to Zat Arrras' confrontation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dad8def4f34b963a5737d3ed48d75d4f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CONTROLLING DEVICES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Controlling Devices are mechanisms within the vessel that are used to direct and manage its flight and position.&lt;SEP&gt;The controlling devices refer to the mechanisms that manage the direction and movement of the boat, specifically through the use of rays of repulsion.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5a7a16642255b39659c194a76a94b26b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4402bc0fee69b84388050c068b5a22f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIGHTING MAN">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fighting Man is a character who experiences a surge of battle joy and is marked by a distinct smile during combat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-325b26f02d17fd6347079d1ba4fad726</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SUN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sun is described as rising above the horizon, illuminating the scene and revealing the presence of the boarding party.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sun is the celestial body that rises, bringing light to the scene described, and signifies the transition from night to day.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sun represents a celestial body whose position and light reveal the hidden beauty and wealth of the cliff, creating an inspiring visual experience.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3572581c177d59bd25bf67c02d0373c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baf097d75b2e15406baf64c8aff8191f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4402bc0fee69b84388050c068b5a22f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BOULDER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Boulder is a large rock surrounded by the corpses of assailants, marking the starting point of the characters' retreat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boulder is a large rock that the Green Warrior uses as a defensive position against the herd.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-325b26f02d17fd6347079d1ba4fad726&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a11c3e8c3e0a41f033f65d169562fb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GROUND">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ground refers to the earth below, which the vessel is dangerously close to diving into.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4402bc0fee69b84388050c068b5a22f4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CALOT">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Calot is mentioned in the context of being spurned by Thurid, suggesting a negative perception or rivalry.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac274835cf15fd4d19a41f986b75a81a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AIR SCOUTS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Air Scouts are individuals dispatched by Hor Vastus to search for Thuvia, indicating a role in reconnaissance and search operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Air Scouts are one-man pilots launched from a vessel, demonstrating their role in reconnaissance and exploration.&lt;SEP&gt;The Air scouts are one-man aircraft launched from the battleship, likely serving a reconnaissance or combat role.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0461306cf04c98666dc40fbe77653113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b33af041481ac0fa8f2a1a4f22e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8656b4b6a355643abf13c112ecbaf810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECRET COUNCILS OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Secret Councils of Issus are meetings or gatherings where Issus's influence is exerted, and where conflicts or competitions are noted.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac274835cf15fd4d19a41f986b75a81a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TROOPS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The troops are a disciplined and brave group of soldiers moving through a flooded corridor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d28c03324ce7391ecbcf6ecd8eb6f962</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COWARDLY INJUSTICE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Cowardly Injustice refers to the unfair and cowardly treatment that Xodar faces from others, driven by his fall from favor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ac274835cf15fd4d19a41f986b75a81a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WATER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Water is a barrier in the Martian tunnel, creating a submerged gallery that must be navigated under challenging conditions.&lt;SEP&gt;Water is flooding the submarine and the corridor, representing a significant and menacing environmental challenge.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-541b0ea26f51fac0f91dc38e84f6e054&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d28c03324ce7391ecbcf6ecd8eb6f962</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ANCIENT PEOPLES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ancient Peoples are imagined as the inhabitants of a dying world, involved in labours, intrigues, mysteries, and cruelties.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f872648a390de3468a26f2e0d0becad8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLUMN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The column refers to the formation of troops moving through the corridor, indicating an organized and orderly progression.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d28c03324ce7391ecbcf6ecd8eb6f962</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZODANGAN CREW">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Zodangan crew is a group of individuals operating under Zat Arrras, engaged in a fierce naval battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b53d74848fe61ebd58b7de25870cddf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORRIDOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Corridor is part of the setting, leading to various entrances and ultimately to the temple above.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corridor is a physical location described as a passageway within which the protagonist hides from the approaching group.&lt;SEP&gt;The corridor is a narrow passage connected to the submarine, which is also flooded and challenging the troops' movement.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-de0224229a9afe630da210af9c6bd5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72812560e1ff7542f6388b33de0b70d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d28c03324ce7391ecbcf6ecd8eb6f962</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NAVAL BATTLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The naval battle is a fierce conflict involving fleets maneuvering and engaging in combat in a crowded, fiery sky.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b53d74848fe61ebd58b7de25870cddf1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sea is depicted as an open body of water on Mars, an unusual sight that contrasts with typical Martian landscapes.&lt;SEP&gt;The sea is a body of water beyond Omean, where there are many islands that are considered safe from the blacks.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a412d7e62e543df749e5efad982ac680&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fb847572b8f4cd9bcb5e21934d38337</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sun is mentioned as shining brazenly over the sea on Mars, contributing to the visual experience of the landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sun is the central star of the solar system, providing heat and light to Mars, though its effects are diminished due to Mars' thin atmosphere.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a412d7e62e543df749e5efad982ac680&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9da712a7c655f8901bdc9f3fb4a0cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHRILL, WEIRD CRY">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Shrill, Weird Cry is a recurring sound that previously summoned a herd to attack, indicating its significance in the ongoing battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bdbf2fc4303809c86bb51b044977592d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIERCE BEASTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fierce Beasts are creatures used to attack the characters, suggesting they are part of a hostile environment or system.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c3588057177584b3a0e8590d47a6b02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN CUSTOMS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Martian customs refer to the traditions and practices of the inhabitants of Mars, influencing the social and political structures on the planet.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c62fc6c1b0c8d44a0b390114bb7ef329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GUARD">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Guard consists of armed members responsible for security, reacting to unexpected events with vigilance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is a character responsible for overseeing the confinement of the prisoners and ensuring Issus' commands are followed.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is an organization involved in a conflict where they attempted to capture individuals, indicating their role in maintaining order or control.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is responsible for maintaining security and searching for the white slave, displaying authority in the situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is responsible for overseeing the cells and ensuring the prisoners are accounted for, showing a mix of rage and relief upon discovering the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is responsible for overseeing the prison, posing a potential threat to the narrator's plan of escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard is the individual approaching the Prisoner, unaware of the impending attack.&lt;SEP&gt;The guard is responsible for inspecting the prisoners and ensuring the security of the prison, although his discipline appears to be lax.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-28682fa788a26ee3b60113da3a1a2e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dec572fdc799700a73d7f10c92bbd990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad51ac4fc1824f7d9fecff7b3b450743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9348949c540111a72093dbdd3189e57c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6936386cb94820c7f5a584ca537f27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67b69095d5fb4eb3dbe97daae753305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828c13a969a4680fba443b671dee21b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MUSKETRY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Musketry refers to the use of muskets or firearms in the battle between the Black Pirates of Barsoom and the therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cb13d519a0b4f895198cfc2c98df8b98</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARSOOM">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Barsoom is the fictional representation of the planet Mars, serving as the primary setting for the narrative of John Carter's adventures. It is depicted as a dying world with a complex society, characterized by its thin air, dwindling resources, and ancient civilizations. The planet is home to various races and creatures, including the warlike red men, the therns, the green men, and the First Born. These inhabitants are engaged in tribal conflicts and fierce contests over the limited resources available.

Barsoom is known for its fantastical and vibrant landscapes, including scarlet swards and jewel-adorned temples, as well as unique geographical and technological features such as magnet-operated elevators. The narrative explores its diverse nations and communities, each with its own customs, laws, and superstitions, influenced by the planet's history of atmospheric challenges and the existence of an atmosphere plant.

The planet is also associated with mystery and superstition, with significant cultural and religious influences such as the Thern cult and the Holy Therns, who are considered gods by some inhabitants. Despite its challenges, Barsoom is a place of great importance, where John Carter is revered as a savior and warrior, having played a crucial role in the survival and happiness of its people.

Throughout the narrative, Barsoom's dying environment and harsh survival policies present unique challenges and adventures for the characters, who navigate its societal issues and complex social and political dynamics. The planet's history includes a tradition of seas that have become a cultural fear, and its environment features unique flora and fauna, contributing to its rich and immersive setting.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9ce6762a4b2ba2df84440f6782a029bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80b3d1ec56db5ef8672ef886c7145598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151c6925632d42abc6c6f08a41de7eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71af797a3da71bfc14e67053629a5b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41692485a75fafbf159b80ea98324da3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fdc3026e0bed9c169e49b431d71e5e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553265af22155e878e0c762c2ea5c1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3779ce2c27b4981b2df99e660baffbea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443e52a0d87636b2c7dc0fa86976141f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7842012554cda4bb9f52354216e4a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f890217e0a0643b024f03067d85c909c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c71c37ac9aea9f53b4337fdbaf8493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7747bf1bf113982bf92fc681219b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a221bcb1631084ef422a98443917c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78737f9e0a06b70a0bb9ae9555fd2498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95bfe57ab079b1e2ed63627fb04566e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f48c1d754d1ffb26016da528676dbc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbfd544a7666d71957424825d22b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ae9b01eadc7f407e1d5bca34640588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5207e2e583ab1153c0186e0f0fed81b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d75a8b07d711ce1eff0a8d3d37c746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2bc04d789e0440373c080f9bdaedb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23577b33daf3c193d9b0f1a6043134a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0645e6d28537e5c8127826ee111f4dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c530bc2d8a3e5ffa6e7e1b615b196ddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9313680f9284277c6d0068f59907d106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-339c906257b62f16b009c25aebb93a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a7a16642255b39659c194a76a94b26b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7f8d28a3e30c0766661860b398aad13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5c0c969b2aa049ae080527d08909391&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6ace98e19b610b29e0db6de816d265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf22396435379360201facb4abd270f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0153c5f50c46a4640a510682675ea05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e8b4e5cb9fe7b6998ce2d6e059f797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0224229a9afe630da210af9c6bd5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e1d860411b2b13228387bd01459577&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510dc6fe133b57e406d839f11db76440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8b04ae7b15b144bbaef0ad0fbf97c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a77f4314bc84a07f13a448593fb7d076&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ed8f8e8bb759705aa097dff1c2324ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-307cb64b5b7a6a0c626a6d904683a8b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5ed703fd05231acae40dc9a78f48c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8c4010c210dcbb6da5ccd528fdf874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54ae772b882a5b23dec9acd964a9f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c1b239e85ba6e45a8d3cfd5dd89d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c06efaf0405e791fc4f6f9af3b7624b3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7f7d474fe7101bd33e5c6418f6481220&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5cf45af5e3799da900db83fcb3ff56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ff701e90f02ebbdfe223f97c8789b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-378619143a33f83383e8a418b9f9c820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c865b073d24996a602f890b25765e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b74b5b67f66c6890acf203d7c8111324&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c39c37bc3b545fc1976766cc4848db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369e6763ac9a08c733a8e0483dbb2cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214f06aa11fe94cd8053753efc32c5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43de1e21bfa0068e5a696fbdd9d723aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3ab8dbfde418bf4917b6e144180ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de56aca17cfbd4ba48408133a07edc2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77544c11bdeae685d5cc57de932d4153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f568e5559307a47b8b95fa17fa316c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db711ffa750bb33d7442d11412d8e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3842a58eeaf8cd4c18a171bd149f0da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad91ced17fd76f9b7fb848f010f12b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef83a1bb59d0a6160845638665b9ef6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fadccafc99ba487f1ebdc2a44e91a284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e89417178bd5f0cae70e639617e8707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e6e909540039e4b0a0732f451c6013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8f314a9085fecdc7786aee01217512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d066fee844e2d8100274ab66d09c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-170c5e513d0cfc27ab31c4132ea9d143&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c1c1de3605517ea048c08675a03df17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae83a9d328abc751e8b03536497faf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-633e94a7e73d5790348d90518684dac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-473a795cf653b75021d5abd79e52d085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cebd2d10250f3f1708ab616c25dcf6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-628891acbda1427e7518f177398758d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0091b7eec20ccaadf8476aa83db095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75779c31636c7f365a9d05b913893782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4bea953f1bd40bf6d9a85e314fdbeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c1de3b9f0e7f1ea967106856be68ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18db334173655996e9e3de660f3dfeb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155a9ae6f189508e5e1a54b15041b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-547ddb0ab69ae5538d65ac67924e4a67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WARHOONS OF THE SOUTH">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Warhoons of the South are a group or community on Mars, likely part of a larger horde with distinct societal roles and customs.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c62fc6c1b0c8d44a0b390114bb7ef329</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE OFFICER OF THE GUARD">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Officer of the Guard is responsible for overseeing security and is vigilant, quickly assessing potential threats.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-25d09049fb095c6edf0153c6f72e085a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLEET OF BATTLESHIPS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fleet of Battleships is an assembly of a thousand battleships equipped for navigation and warfare, central to the plans discussed.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AIR CRAFT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Air craft refers to the various flying machines present in the garden, symbolizing a means of freedom and escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GREAT THARK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Great Thark is a being that is initially secured with chains and is encountered by the warriors and the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great Thark is a leader who commanded the savage tribesmen that overran Zodanga, contributing to its defeat.&lt;SEP&gt;The great Thark is a prominent figure on Mars, potentially significant in the context of the story, with implications for rescue efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;The great Thark refers to Tars Tarkas, emphasizing his status and prowess as a warrior leader among his people.&lt;SEP&gt;The great Thark refers to Tars Tarkas, suggesting his stature and significance among the Tharks.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c62fc6c1b0c8d44a0b390114bb7ef329&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1cfa5959049998648fc259707cbe29c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88a169256ce5000de4b694a44baa4d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce58ae175da8c88d32eed4fe4dc295b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE REVOLVERS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Revolvers represent a means of protection or aggression, crucial for the character's sense of safety during the escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-25d09049fb095c6edf0153c6f72e085a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECRECY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Secrecy is crucial to the plans being carried out, as it helps prevent the plans from being discovered by Zat Arrras' spies.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCAPE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Escape is a concept discussed in the text, referring to the possibility of overcoming certain death and achieving freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape is the act of leaving the current situation, planned by the narrator using the air crafts as the avenue to freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape is the miraculous event where the characters successfully evade their enemies and leave the land of the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the act of fleeing from the deceptive Valley of Dor and the oppressive rule of the Holy Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the action of fleeing from pursuing enemies, facilitated by the fog on Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the narrator's plan to avoid detection and confinement, relying on agility and the element of surprise.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the planned action by John Carter and his companions to flee from captivity or danger.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the potential action of fleeing from the Black Pirates, indicating a pivotal moment or objective in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the protagonist's plan to kill the jailer by a ruse and trust to fate to lead them to safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Escape refers to the rare and challenging act of leaving the Valley of Dor and the Land of the First Born, typically involving the use of an airboat.&lt;SEP&gt;The Escape refers to the group's successful departure from the city without being pursued, marking a significant moment of relief and safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f48c1d754d1ffb26016da528676dbc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80eb9f50e883e48730129bb2c24b1228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c1b239e85ba6e45a8d3cfd5dd89d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec0c5c3f38231c4a87625db9626c95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5090242f995a0ee5e8500bf6ef94eed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26ef0b24e731f9a32cfb495e4f895d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad4c9898bf8ce3eb60abe1ad94ff5f73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2b778334955e9ced7c09bfb06c6e52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828c13a969a4680fba443b671dee21b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BLACK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black is a character who reacts with a fleeting grin to the conversation about immortality and the therns, suggesting some hidden knowledge or insight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Black is an individual who becomes unconscious during a challenging situation but eventually regains consciousness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e7f8d28a3e30c0766661860b398aad13&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1ccf749f2b30c16f4cc985a93939e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE OPEN WINDOW">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Open Window symbolizes a potential escape route, offering a direct path to freedom and safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-25d09049fb095c6edf0153c6f72e085a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LAND OF LOST SOULS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Land of Lost Souls is located between the Mountains of Otz and the ice barrier on Barsoom. It is an area with fertile lands that require no irrigation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE OUTER WORLD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Outer World refers to a place that is unreachable for the protagonist, symbolizing freedom and the unknown beyond their current confines.&lt;SEP&gt;The Outer World represents a goal or destination that the narrator is determined to reach, symbolizing freedom or escape from current circumstances.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-03e5883e77d0d77b28ad24e56e3db4f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd21470cebb00b207669a678b79f42d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MASTER OF LIFE AND DEATH">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Master of Life and Death is a significant figure on Barsoom, likely a position of great power and authority, and is related to Phaidor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Master of Life and Death is a title indicating a powerful and influential position related to themes of life and mortality.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-65cbfd544a7666d71957424825d22b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1ccf749f2b30c16f4cc985a93939e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THRONE OF RIGHTEOUSNESS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Throne of Righteousness is a significant place within the temple, possibly symbolizing authority or justice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Throne of Righteousness is a symbolic platform where judgment takes place, representing fairness and justice.&lt;SEP&gt;The Throne of Righteousness symbolizes authority and leadership, serving as a place where allegiance is sworn and power is recognized.&lt;SEP&gt;The Throne of Righteousness symbolizes the rightful or moral authority held by the protagonist and his allies.&lt;SEP&gt;Throne of Righteousness is a symbolic place of authority and justice where people rally in support of John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Throne of Righteousness refers to the platform where John Carter and others are halted during the trial.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a356f2ca641af882f4389e64c1cfe156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3806151a083dd701c29455b3a3f12e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-290349b66f441c7882b44da1cd267609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b99744d09aa8c4015948f8dc5e7f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5e144173f5e450941ba6b94f86ebf0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIERCE BRUTES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fierce brutes refer to the dangerous creatures inhabiting the productive areas of Barsoom, preventing others from accessing its resources.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THOATS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Thoats are creatures associated with Green Martian Life, known for their distinctive squealing and grunting sounds.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are creatures or animals that are part of a herd within the city, indicating their role in the ecosystem or as a resource.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are creatures that form part of the herd in the courtyard, known for their restlessness and potential noise when alarmed.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are fierce beasts used for transportation, crucial to the escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are large creatures ridden by the Green warriors, playing a significant role in their combat strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are large, fierce beasts native to the described environment, characterized by their wild nature and ferociousness. They are controlled through cruelty and brute force, standing ten feet tall at the shoulder with a distinctive dark slate color on their backs and sides, shading to yellow on their feet, and having a pure white belly.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are large, glossy creatures used as mounts by Tars Tarkas and the narrator during their escape.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are mighty beasts ridden by the green warriors of Thark, contributing to their battle capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are the mounts of the Green Martians, described as sleek, hairless creatures with a dark slate color, vivid yellow legs, and a broad flat tail. They are controlled through telepathic means.&lt;SEP&gt;Thoats are the riderless creatures that plunged among the dead and dying during the chaos following the explosion.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f50f91d9820d10c6c913902753e753a2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eab17c76d340b78e7d04b4ce3014258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc2a40b4b5725576e6c332e92d2fc23e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe80414646c50a040ed7d24329e8df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f38d06d8db25fac8950d2837736775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2bc04d789e0440373c080f9bdaedb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cadceeac04df930779a49bf86b28cc7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87cf36f7152da08268ab8ec68bf17938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0edd1e7012585beb90063a964c7516bd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE OTZ">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Otz refers to foothills that are part of the geographic setting where the events take place.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae1ccf749f2b30c16f4cc985a93939e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGH PRIEST">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The High Priest is a high-ranking noble involved in the events taking place within the temple.&lt;SEP&gt;The High Priest is the highest noble of the realm, serving as the religious leader who invokes Issus to act against blasphemers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f3602317d23520f84b00ad6d7b914819&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aa86d78f2bb2e5145ff9051abc850f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WICKED REMNANTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Wicked remnants are the remains of two once mighty races on Barsoom that bar others from accessing the fertile lands.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE NARRATOR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Narrator is a character experiencing fear and excitement while being guided through unknown depths by the boy, demonstrating a sense of adventure.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a character who experiences a near-death encounter and a moment of clarity and rage after being attacked and falling onto a corpse.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a character who follows the youth onto the submarine, participating in the stealthy operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a character who formulates a plan to rescue Tars Tarkas and is prepared to take violent action to ensure their escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a character who is more inclined towards fighting and similar arts rather than romantic pursuits, and he expresses his love for Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a character who plans a discreet action involving his son, Carthoris, and assures that it is harmless.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is a father who reflects on his son's resemblance to his mother and expresses deep emotions upon reuniting with his son.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is an experienced combatant who admires the boy's fighting skills and sees a reflection of his own fighting style in the boy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is an individual engaged in a fierce battle against numerous creatures, demonstrating exceptional combat skills and endurance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is an individual involved in a fierce battle, who describes the actions of the Green Warrior and their shared combat against adversaries.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is an individual who acts impulsively, driven by admiration and the thrill of battle, to assist the Great Warrior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is an individual who has a profound connection to Mars and a longing to return to a significant experience, reflecting a deep personal journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is following the trail of the three warriors, observing their actions and movements through the corridors.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the central character who has angered the mob by affronting Issus and subsequently falls into a black abyss with a boy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the central figure contemplating the need for swords and planning a perilous trip with companions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the character recounting the events, expressing exhaustion and the need to engage in a battle for survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the father of Carthoris, who experiences a profound moment of horror upon realizing he has harmed his son.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the individual devising a plan to counter the threat, demonstrating strategic thinking and leadership in a dangerous situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the person describing the events, expressing a negative opinion about the woman's appearance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the person trying to escape captivity and contact Carthoris, showing determination and resourcefulness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Narrator is the protagonist of the story, facing numerous challenges and adversaries in the search for their lost love.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator has close-cropped black hair and a thern complexion, and is recognized for their fighting ability and strange origin.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is a captive who observes the situation and notes the ineffectiveness of the bindings on their wrists, suggesting they are not Martian.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is a character who is addressed by the black pirate and experiences a sense of hope followed by apprehension upon seeing a battleship.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an adventurer who embarked on a journey to find the Lost Sea of Korus and encountered the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an individual involved in intense combat, experiencing both defensive and offensive moments, armed with a Martian sword.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an individual who has experienced loneliness and imprisonment, expressing disbelief and hope upon hearing about the return to Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is an individual who is balancing on a partition wall and interacts with another character, demonstrating agility and curiosity.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is deeply affected by the disappearance of Dejah Thoris, experiencing intense emotions and a sense of urgency.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is the central character engaged in a combat scenario, skillfully using a Martian sword to fend off multiple attackers.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is the individual trying to avoid detection by the men and navigating through the dark corridors with caution.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator is the protagonist who used the dead man's revolver to defend himself against the fellow's attack.</data>
