      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Orgies of Sacrifice refer to the horrific rituals performed by the mysterious beings, involving sacrifice and cannibalism.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7f7d474fe7101bd33e5c6418f6481220</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GIRL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The girl is a character who is present during the attack, as indicated by her shriek.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7965e5a361b23156242ad340f4031ff6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NORTHERN WARHOON">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Northern Warhoon refers to a geographic area associated with the Warhoons, indicating a specific region known for its harsh conditions and possibly the location of their dungeons.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-df11c982435f95e861fc0dd91fde9b5d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEMPLES OF THE THERNS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Temples of the Therns are geographical landmarks, visible in the sunlight, towards which the transports are heading.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temples of the Therns are part of the stronghold's defenses, indicating a sacred or significant area within the fortified location.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temples of the Therns are sacred places associated with the Therns, where severe punishment is meted out to those who entertain sacrilegious thoughts.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-efd3e0d93de6c86499fed72eef65713e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1de80424c9643aa139d17b7a371aed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36134f2c86fa620f5fc1afeb5c999e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN FLIERS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Martian fliers are swift vehicles used on Mars, capable of reaching speeds of approximately two hundred miles an hour.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9327b914c391d3c6243870a0c7d7b802</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNDERGROUND DUNGEON">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Underground Dungeon is a place of imprisonment associated with the Warhoons, significant for its role in holding prisoners.</data>
