    </node>
    <node id="RIVER OF MYSTERY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">River of Mystery is a geographic location from which returning individuals are traditionally killed as blasphemers.&lt;SEP&gt;The River of Mystery is a geographical feature associated with a voluntary pilgrimage that leads creatures to an unknown end.&lt;SEP&gt;The River of Mystery is a location associated with a voluntary pilgrimage undertaken by individuals seeking unknown outcomes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4946b446ccff9fda170ff24c30ed8581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6527f91419b819bb445cd47f8d793fe4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CITY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The City is a location described as dead and from which the group is escaping, indicating a place of danger or abandonment.&lt;SEP&gt;The City is a location where the narrator is attempting to move undetected, suggesting it is under some form of control or surveillance.&lt;SEP&gt;The City is an ancient metropolis built upon rolling foothills, with its architecture reflecting a barbaric splendour turned to silver by moonlight.&lt;SEP&gt;The City is the inhabited area where the protagonist navigates through shadows and intersections to avoid detection.&lt;SEP&gt;The City is the location that the protagonist intends to infiltrate to confirm information about the Warhoons.&lt;SEP&gt;The City is the setting from which Tars Tarkas and the narrator are attempting to escape, heading toward its southern boundary.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7eab17c76d340b78e7d04b4ce3014258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-307cb64b5b7a6a0c626a6d904683a8b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87cf36f7152da08268ab8ec68bf17938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25b54582b37bd689e9944f79dbc5d866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad4c9898bf8ce3eb60abe1ad94ff5f73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0edd1e7012585beb90063a964c7516bd</data>
    </node>
