      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The conflict within the palace refers to a battle or struggle that the narrator hears, indicating a significant event occurring nearby.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe5cf45af5e3799da900db83fcb3ff56</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLAVE MAIDENS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Slave Maidens are individuals who surround Issus, adorned in jeweled trappings and colorful cloths.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fb8bd9971e54ccc028230b4d13bef281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GREAT GATES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Great Gates are barriers that Tars Tarkas opens to facilitate their escape from the city.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7eab17c76d340b78e7d04b4ce3014258</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BLACK PIRATE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black Pirate is a character who is present during a high-altitude flight, closely observing the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The black pirate is a character who kept the narrator engrossed with a tale, sensing the approach of a battleship.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0c401d24eec318e7dd6ff9a98117d860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3535289447cafe1e19cf3c11eed02d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HIGH DIGNITARIES">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">High Dignitaries are individuals of elevated rank among the First Born, distinguished by their precious stones and gold insignia, symbolizing their authority and status.&lt;SEP&gt;High Dignitaries are individuals of high rank, gleaming with precious stones and insignias, who stand in front of the soldiery.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e6bbfb90b7b84328adaa1e46f68731fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fb8bd9971e54ccc028230b4d13bef281</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ATMOSPHERE PLANT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Atmosphere Plant is a facility mentioned in the text, which John Carter hoped to reach to save Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;The Atmosphere Plant is a crucial facility on Barsoom that maintains the planet's air supply, and John Carter saved countless lives by reopening it.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THARK">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Thark is a character present with Thuvia and the narrator during the battle scene, observing the combatants.&lt;SEP&gt;The Thark refers to a group or race known for their distinct characteristics, such as being relentless and not relishing flight.&lt;SEP&gt;The Thark refers to a group or species, possibly associated with Tars Tarkas, indicating a warrior culture.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d7cb29c22be9d31a0a3156fe8cf8b734&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78737f9e0a06b70a0bb9ae9555fd2498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094a963e57ebb31d9da4dd213eabadfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MEN OF HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Men of Helium are the audience and judges to whom John Carter presents his case, seeking justice and support.&lt;SEP&gt;Men of Helium refers to the collective group of sailors and soldiers who are loyal to the Prince of Helium and participate in the naval engagement.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fec090a1531505a82f52e76f197bd709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18db334173655996e9e3de660f3dfeb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK-HAIRED PRINCESS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black-haired Princess is a significant character related to John Carter, possibly his love interest, whom he dreams of reuniting with in the royal gardens of Tardos Mors.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c</data>
    </node>
