    </node>
    <node id="MEN OF ZODANGA">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Men of Zodanga are implied to be unjust, as John Carter does not expect justice from them.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-18db334173655996e9e3de660f3dfeb6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLENDER SON">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Slender Son is a character imagined to be with Princess in the royal gardens, symbolizing youth and potential kinship.&lt;SEP&gt;The Slender Son is John Carter's child, whom he dreams of being with the Black-haired Princess in the royal gardens of Tardos Mors.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BOTTOM OF KORUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Bottom of Korus is mentioned as a potential destination, suggesting a place of significance or peril.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-094a963e57ebb31d9da4dd213eabadfb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARSOOMIAN LION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Barsoomian lion is a terrifying creature with tiny ears, enormous protruding green eyes, and a powerful tail. It emits a terrifying roar that can momentarily paralyze its prey.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-37de92ea295356665d5a7b1eb1ea03a4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE WHITE MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The White Man is a character who is sought after by the guard of Xodar, indicating a position of interest or importance within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The White Man is the protagonist who engages in a sword fight with the enemy, demonstrating considerable skill despite not having practiced for ten years.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20b2378fb16755bb8ab3dfb8a663431e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a292b6d7aae5528de2d633ec624a151c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TREE OF LIFE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tree of Life is a concept describing the evolutionary process where life forms transition from plant life to a combination of plant and animal, eventually developing independent thought and movement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree of Life is a dead entity that once played a significant role in the reproduction and existence of plant men on Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree of Life is a legendary plant in the Valley Dor on Barsoom, from which the First Born trace their lineage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree of Life is mentioned as a place where one can find a quick end to suffering, implying it has significant importance or power.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree of Life is the origin from which the strange race of Plant Men of Barsoom sprang.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89113c4da6f11aefb8678fe8526edbf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-633e94a7e73d5790348d90518684dac7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b09006b13030957e1aa7f0ee75bbcb7c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MYSTERIOUS RIVER ISS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mysterious River Iss is a geographical feature used in the doctrine of the Therns to persuade people to undertake pilgrimages.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SWORD FIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sword Fight is a close and intense battle between the protagonist and the enemy, showcasing their skills and endurance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-20b2378fb16755bb8ab3dfb8a663431e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PALACE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Palace is a location occupied by Zat Arrras, with pits beneath it where guards are stationed, and the destination for the narrator's return journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Palace is a location where the Speaker's guard-room is situated, and it contains many fine trappings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Palace is a location where the events are unfolding, including the influx of people and the presence of a dining hall with a view of the main gates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Palace is the destination for the protagonist and his allies, indicating a place of significance and possibly power.&lt;SEP&gt;The Palace is the location from which Dejah Thoris attempted to escape and where the events involving Sola and her father take place.&lt;SEP&gt;The Palace is the location where the conflict is taking place and is a central setting for the events described.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dbf790c243f3e5d0d4de29cc208b1cfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3806151a083dd701c29455b3a3f12e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d66810adef7e94054186f17a12de861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150a32741024f15fa5faa16e08c5f878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8917f33ca9393e6e40d34847a0b96e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288dab7b4222c07f01804ee7228c46ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE LOST SEA OF KORUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Lost Sea of Korus is a mythical or historical geographical location that plays a role in the religious teachings of the Therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MY PRINCE">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">My Prince is a title indicating a position of leadership or nobility, likely referring to the protagonist.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0491417d3b1d17dbd4f6570ef17e2cd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CARTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Carter is a leader among a group of individuals attempting to escape from a dangerous situation within a mountain chamber.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WIVES AND DAUGHTERS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Wives and daughters are referred to as individuals who need to be saved from various atrocities and dangers on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOUTH POLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The South Pole is a region on Mars experiencing summer, resulting in melting ice caps and cloud formation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5090242f995a0ee5e8500bf6ef94eed3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CHAMBER OF DEATH">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Chamber of Death is a location within a mountain, described as a perilous place from which escape is being attempted.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREAT WHITE APES OF DOR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The great white apes of Dor are described as dangerous creatures with fangs that threaten the people of Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="NATURE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Nature is depicted as a powerful force, represented by an impenetrable curtain that separates the characters from their enemies.&lt;SEP&gt;Nature is described as creating a condition that allows for escape by hanging a curtain of fog above the planet.&lt;SEP&gt;Nature refers to the natural world and its phenomena, which the creature is described as a travesty of.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-459aa866f94fbb1f816c19ab635af138&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5090242f995a0ee5e8500bf6ef94eed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c1b239e85ba6e45a8d3cfd5dd89d08</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ESCAPE PLAN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Escape Plan is a coordinated effort to break free from captivity, involving multiple individuals and requiring careful timing and preparation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Escape Plan is a strategy devised by the prisoners, including Carter and the girl, to escape from the chamber and the therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed0051afe0d62a248a398dfeca58557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THRONE ROOM">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Throne Room is a significant location where the confrontation occurs, featuring a carved door, a throne, and ranks of soldiers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ee174a5fe26d1ed437fbeaaf534da837</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREEN JEDDAK">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Green Jeddak is a title or role indicating a leader among the green Martians, who is introduced to Xodar.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ad4c9898bf8ce3eb60abe1ad94ff5f73</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ANCIENT SUPERSTITION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ancient Superstition refers to a long-standing belief that the group is opposing, despite its known fallacy through cruel experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Ancient Superstition refers to the beliefs held by the therns, which the prisoners are challenging by attempting to escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c768a4ea224d8da779e3818ab95c45f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COLD, DEAD ISS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The cold, dead Iss is described as a force that carries individuals away from homes of love and life to danger and death.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRINCESS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Princess is a black-haired woman imagined to be in the royal gardens of Tardos Mors, associated with dreams of companionship and royalty.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess is a character who is referenced in a moment of reflection, suggesting her importance to the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess is the role held by Dejah Thoris, who is central to the rescue plan and political conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess refers to Dejah Thoris's role, highlighting her importance and the motivation for the rescue mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess refers to Dejah Thoris, who holds a noble position and is admired for her virtues and sacrifice.&lt;SEP&gt;Princess refers to Dejah Thoris, who is described as having a slender form, indicating her status and importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a beloved leader who embarks on a journey, followed by her loyal guards and a hound named Woola.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a central figure who suffered greatly due to the loss of her lord and her son, and is deeply mourned by Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a character who is concerned for her son and the soldiers of Helium, and encourages John Carter to fulfill his duty.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a key figure in the narrative, described as incomparable and central to the protagonist's actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a key figure whose safety and survival are central to the narrative, inspiring hope and courage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a significant figure who is the target of a rescue mission, underscoring her importance in the unfolding events.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is associated with John Carter, representing personal sacrifice and happiness that he gave up for the greater good.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is the individual that the narrator is determined to reach, rescue, and seek revenge for, indicating her significant importance in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ea85a61fc6af15c21b035b16ff189849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214f06aa11fe94cd8053753efc32c5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-86c3bee92a592b4fa42f49fe8b29d697&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb66e3143c3d99b7ed3016c869442dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8b04ae7b15b144bbaef0ad0fbf97c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a524faa9db11b6d8e0ba78bffed85d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60721b3b1ff8467dd26b0e1844246065&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906dc67c04c5c3c54cafff91f6bf6a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9202971a6c9b597c032f8fde2a01d35a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a221bcb1631084ef422a98443917c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CELL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cell is a chamber from which Tars Tarkas is removed, indicating its function as a place of confinement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cell is a physical location where the white man is held, separated by partition walls, highlighting themes of confinement and escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cell is the physical location where the characters are confined, representing a barrier to freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;The cell is a location where Tars Tarkas is chained, indicating a place of imprisonment or containment.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a292b6d7aae5528de2d633ec624a151c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-28682fa788a26ee3b60113da3a1a2e96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06aa4fa22af57c68012d4559518b9942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88a169256ce5000de4b694a44baa4d8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TEMPLE OF THE SUN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Temple of the Sun is a significant location in the narrative, described as a golden temple with intricate designs and precious stones.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b24d0bed8f7d9763208b3080b3ddeb2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EARTH">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Earth is the home planet of John Carter, where he spent ten years before returning to the planet he loves.&lt;SEP&gt;Earth is the home planet of the narrator, associated with familial ties and nostalgia.&lt;SEP&gt;Earth is the planet where the Uncle has returned after his experiences, and it represents the broader context in which his discoveries are considered revolutionary yet incomprehensible.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33062da99c0918b07863c96eb6751bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-700a9ecf3a90c20ff6154b43291d211a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE XAVARIAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Xavarian is a group or entity with officers who appear divided into factions during the journey to Helium.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8de0958c186ba3135c1e8cf7f85bf340</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GODDESS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Goddess is a figure who was worshipped as divine but is now betrayed and facing the vengeance of her people.&lt;SEP&gt;The Goddess is portrayed as a powerful being who, despite her usual demeanor, is currently overwhelmed with emotion and vulnerability.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5b24d0bed8f7d9763208b3080b3ddeb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7407e663d0639c538204a4f83f2475d4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Ben is the narrator's body servant who delivers a telegram, playing a role in the communication process.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="IMPRISONMENT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Imprisonment refers to the captivity of Dejah Thoris, which is the cause of the approaching conflict and John's demand for accountability.&lt;SEP&gt;Imprisonment refers to the narrator's confinement, during which they have been treated with courtesy and consideration by the visitor.&lt;SEP&gt;Imprisonment refers to the state of being held captive, which is a situation the narrator finds themselves in.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-489a23f49738517554abf2da01fc7862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc762f5d59833da40830b39a8c156c55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5dcfae890412722c9137f3055bdbbb40</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN HOUND">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Martian hound, or calot, is a creature on Mars with jaws equipped with several rows of long needle-like fangs, similar to those of the Banth.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-949dc44a1a314c18156adec10cd85e90</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOTEL RALEIGH">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Hotel Raleigh is the location in Richmond where the narrator is meeting John Carter.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WEAPONS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Weapons include swords, daggers, and revolvers, which are crucial for the group's defense and were distributed among the followers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c768a4ea224d8da779e3818ab95c45f2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMBAT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Combat is the rapid fighting described in the text, involving the narrator and the boy as they face their adversaries.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-176e51cc1b67ba293d6f8fb29ef63b47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TELEGRAM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Telegram is a mode of communication used to arrange a meeting, reflecting urgency and formality.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WHITE APE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">White Ape is one of the creatures that originate from the buds of fruit trees, emerging from a specific section within the bud.&lt;SEP&gt;White Ape refers to a creature or adversary in the context, symbolizing danger and a formidable challenge.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5360ea6efbfef241b4593260b36361e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdc154afb97906f6c0d9be300b69e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ADVERSARIES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Adversaries refer to the foes that the narrator and the boy are fighting against, specifically mentioned as "blacks" in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-176e51cc1b67ba293d6f8fb29ef63b47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WHITE MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The White Man is an individual not native to Barsoom, characterized by a different skin color and involved in a confrontation with another character.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-923f3704592d0c1131d92378ee957a21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK MAN OF BARSOOM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Black Man of Barsoom is a primaeval creature that originates from the buds of fruit trees, emerging from a specific section within the bud.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1bdc154afb97906f6c0d9be300b69e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEMONS OF THE OUTER AIR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The demons of the outer air are described as having a malign lust for blood and engaging in battle with the therns, suggesting a fearsome and aggressive nature.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5e32f64cbf961c7ebe05d9308a82211c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARSOOMIAN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Barsoomian refers to someone or something originating from Barsoom, a fictional setting, implying a native identity or origin.&lt;SEP&gt;Barsoomian refers to the inhabitants of Barsoom, indicating a distinct cultural or racial group within the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Barsoomian refers to the inhabitants or concepts related to the planet Barsoom, also known as Mars in the fictional universe.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68427a98a52f5c6bfa5aa4f4e34e079f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd39baf5700bc8ce341598b693d045d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-923f3704592d0c1131d92378ee957a21</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIXTEEN-LEGGED WORM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sixteen-Legged Worm is one of the creatures that emerge from the buds of fruit trees, originating from a specific section within the bud.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sixteen-Legged Worm is an ancestral creature from which many forms of animal life on Barsoom are said to have evolved.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a54ae772b882a5b23dec9acd964a9f8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdc154afb97906f6c0d9be300b69e67</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE YOUTH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Youth is a captivating figure who breaks free from the cages, inspiring others with a call to action.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a character who actively fights alongside the narrator, ultimately saving them by killing an adversary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a character who demonstrates stealth and quickness, leading a silent infiltration onto a submarine and into its main cabin.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a character who is involved in the confrontation with Issus, nearly succumbing to a blow but saved by the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a character who may deliver a message to Carthoris and is associated with wearing a harness and sword, indicating a role of a messenger or warrior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a charismatic and influential individual who inspires others to rise up and fight against their captors, demonstrating leadership and bravery.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a companion of the narrator and Xodar, involved in a plan to remain hidden in the water during a perilous trip.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is a young man who delivers food to the narrator and conveys messages from Zat Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is an individual standing beside the narrator, notable for being the first to vocally support the rebellion against Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Youth is engaged in battle alongside the narrator, indicating bravery and involvement in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The youth is a character who provides information about Zithad and expresses hope for the downfall of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;The youth is a character who pursued the guards closely behind the great apes.&lt;SEP&gt;The youth is described as handsome and dignified, possibly a noble character with shabby trappings, suggesting a disparity between appearance and status.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0a705f5ca3ac7586de6280ecff5dabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe97f250482c686ce435b237250ec83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef78295a9a43f2e8c84cc7df716c9614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-45e4a46e4701cf657ddb82656fd17c60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b513f985e87889370807eaddbed6a7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af15d56fdb26a152438c0fb85843479f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1061c20e9da039c1ef6d01a5f9f830bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b50f9fffc90e373e4a1484b4a92e8928&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0700c43fe3a98521053c4539ff16e766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cb52c113425589d349e2479393d8cbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f804d99b0560937dece663ce5c7f98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c70f842786039ef907bfc03bffe9b7d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9676c4c8b41ff0b49d14a71ae70361aa</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EARTHLY STRENGTH">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Earthly Strength refers to the narrator's superior physical abilities compared to the warriors on the planet, giving them an advantage in combat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8426378e0c6a6a09748fb71be6bb2857</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The men are a group carrying a torch and moving through dark corridors, potentially pursuing or inadvertently following the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The men are part of a group carrying a torch, navigating the winding passageways of Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-521cf73d9e8446fc4ced3d3322249e47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RELIGIOUS FANATICS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Religious Fanatics are followers of Issus, portrayed as an infuriated mob, crazed by the affront to their goddess.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af15d56fdb26a152438c0fb85843479f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SECRET DOORWAYS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Secret Doorways are passages through which beasts are released, indicating a hidden mechanism of control or attack.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5c3588057177584b3a0e8590d47a6b02</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TORCH">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The torch is a source of light that provides faint radiance, allowing navigation through the dark passages.&lt;SEP&gt;The torch provides faint radiance, allowing navigation through the dark passageways.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-521cf73d9e8446fc4ced3d3322249e47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK GULF">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black Gulf is a mysterious opening in the flooring, symbolizing a potential escape or doom for those who enter.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-af15d56fdb26a152438c0fb85843479f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RED MARTIANS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Red Martians are a group known for manufacturing curious and deadly revolvers.&lt;SEP&gt;Red Martians are a group of people with specific customs and character traits, who value acts of loyalty and honor.&lt;SEP&gt;Red Martians are a group of prisoners, suggesting they are a distinct race or group in the narrative, associated with the main characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Red Martians are described as individuals unaccustomed to large quantities of water, indicating a cultural or physiological trait.&lt;SEP&gt;Red Martians are inhabitants of Mars, associated with the red grasslike vegetation and great waterways.&lt;SEP&gt;Red Martians are one of the races present in the underworld, part of the heterogeneous collection of hybrids.&lt;SEP&gt;The Red Martians are a group of men and women who are prisoners and decide to join the escape plan despite their misgivings.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a5c94f3b5e290f5c1cd4a83a590d5a6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e6b03456b9b45383978573633205507&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c3588057177584b3a0e8590d47a6b02&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ff17997572867abd4f76f4d654adda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad91db0cfa902f227c8f42d4fc8ec3f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c768a4ea224d8da779e3818ab95c45f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CORRIDORS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The corridors are dark, winding passages beneath the dead cities of Mars, filled with potential dangers and unknown creatures.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-521cf73d9e8446fc4ced3d3322249e47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BATTLESHIPS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Battleships are advanced war vessels taken by the First Born from the Red Men to be copied, as the First Born do not invent or create themselves.&lt;SEP&gt;Battleships are large naval vessels with watchful guards, responsible for monitoring surrounding activities during the night.&lt;SEP&gt;Battleships refer to large military ships used in strategic operations, significant in the context of defense and warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;Battleships refer to large warships, indicating a significant military presence and the capability of the black pirates.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3eee5f1ac2c6536f462bf6d2d2fb2ff7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3568b50dc95db579dd850d006b0923f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e5e5b39a52fe718335f8e9d6edf39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535538235eb01dfcd216bab7a901ead5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE AIR BATTLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Air Battle is the upcoming conflict for which the characters are preparing, involving a fleet of battleships.&lt;SEP&gt;The Air Battle suggests a conflict or combat occurring in the air, involving aerial tactics or vehicles.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5122be51fbf9687e6937b89f972a742f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE DEAD CITIES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The dead cities are ancient, possibly abandoned locations on Mars, under which the corridors run.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-521cf73d9e8446fc4ced3d3322249e47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LUXURY AND IDLENESS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Luxury and Idleness are the lifestyles of the First Born, who pride themselves on their non-productiveness and depend on the labor of lower orders.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-85e5e5b39a52fe718335f8e9d6edf39f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DYING MARS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Dying Mars refers to the planet Mars, which is depicted as a place with decaying or deteriorating environments.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-521cf73d9e8446fc4ced3d3322249e47</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TRIBUNAL">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tribunal consists of thirty-one judges who deliver a unanimous verdict of death against John Carter for blasphemy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tribunal is a body that delivered a verdict against Helium's hero, representing judicial authority.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a68ab2d56f3a58dae0859abb96ba81f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddabfd0bd8bf6b02e156424ff9c407b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE JAILER">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Jailer is responsible for guarding Tars Tarkas's cell and is a potential obstacle to the escape plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a32b81d30df31b9838bdc61e632ce4e5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARSOOMIAN YEAR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">A Barsoomian year refers to a time measurement specific to the world of Barsoom, impacting the timing of events in the narrative.</data>
