    <node id="WARRIORS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Warriors are individuals located within the buildings who could be alerted by the noise from the herd.&lt;SEP&gt;Warriors are individuals who have taken a prisoner and are navigating through corridors, indicating their role as captors or guards.&lt;SEP&gt;Warriors are the opponents faced by the narrator, characterized by their fierceness and skill in battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-98f38d06d8db25fac8950d2837736775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8d461891a972418eb14d1655c357ae53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8426378e0c6a6a09748fb71be6bb2857</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PRINCESS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Princess is a character condemned to a dire fate by Issus, evoking the narrator's rage and protective instincts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a character who is fearful of being discovered by a terrible creature and is emotionally attached to John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;The Princess is a character whose body is mentioned, indicating she is deceased or in a perilous condition, deeply affecting the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-410b3ad1e7dc881b5bb089cb806d3650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62e8976c797532ee7fe92a94f959fbbe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae579ef7acc06ef53410bc801d675e17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THORNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Thorns are a group deeply entrenched in superstition and religious practices, worshipping entities like the Great White Apes and plant men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1de80424c9643aa139d17b7a371aed4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KORAD">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Korad is a location on Mars, mentioned as being near the dead sea bottom where the Tharks reside.&lt;SEP&gt;Korad is referred to as a dead city with age-old marble halls where the narrator courted Dejah Thoris.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06c8b6e33f9e011b6bce4f39de022bf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd3df1ac8a7347e4d559c5ff38864ea</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TERRIBLE CREATURE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Terrible Creature is an entity known for its ferocious cruelty, causing fear and distress to those who encounter it.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae579ef7acc06ef53410bc801d675e17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SACRILEGIOUS THOUGHTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sacrilegious Thoughts refer to ideas that challenge or disrespect the religious beliefs held by the Therns, seen as extremely dangerous and punishable.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1de80424c9643aa139d17b7a371aed4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEMPLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Temple is a structure above the corridor where the narrator exits, indicating its significance in the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a location of unthinkable beauty, containing magnificent apartments and noble halls, serving as a significant setting in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a location under attack by the Black Pirates of Barsoom and defended by the thern forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant geographic location that the fleet aims to reach via a subterranean route.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant location in the narrative, serving as a target for the group's attack and central to their quest.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant location within the narrative, from where cries of alarm and warning arise.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant location, reachable by a subterranean route, indicating its strategic importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is the location where the conflict is occurring and where Dejah Thoris is currently situated.&lt;SEP&gt;The temple is a structure above the ancient system, connected to the corridors and chambers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-62abb1ac4cf24cfe818a8870240b9a6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4c2a87c1f4e9cc424db7febe61149a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb13d519a0b4f895198cfc2c98df8b98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fb847572b8f4cd9bcb5e21934d38337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-489a23f49738517554abf2da01fc7862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e88229e411ecdc345e27bf0ded33876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3076597b25663698d56a8907b5084439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-de0224229a9afe630da210af9c6bd5c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a95bfe57ab079b1e2ed63627fb04566e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OUR SON">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Our Son refers to the child of John Carter and the Princess, who is mentioned as being in a location where soldiers are present.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae579ef7acc06ef53410bc801d675e17</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIANS OF THE OUTER WORLD">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Martians of the Outer World are contrasted with the Therns, worshipping a hope for a life of love, peace, and happiness after death.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1de80424c9643aa139d17b7a371aed4</data>
