    </node>
    <node id="TEMPLES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Temples are located behind the ramparts, housing a million fighting-men, suggesting a place of military significance and strategic planning.&lt;SEP&gt;The temples are geographical locations targeted by bombs from the larger fliers, indicating their strategic importance in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The temples are locations above the corridors and chambers where the slaves come from.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b02017949859ea016f59b43ad5eeda2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d81037675f5b075ca39bbd7280bffb81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202ae065926466ff564e922828d8ca62</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BOY">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Boy is a character involved in the escape, positioned alongside Xodar and the narrator to minimize air resistance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who assists the narrator in finding the trap door and emphasizes the importance of not deserting friends.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who guides the narrator through a dark passageway, showing familiarity with the environment and taking cautious steps to ensure safety.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who has been courteous and considerate to the Speaker, prompting the Speaker to offer him a gift as a token of gratitude.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who identifies the "lighted way" and leads the advance towards the submarine.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who is being spoken to and is convinced of the identity of another person through their words and actions, particularly in relation to his mother.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who is concerned about leaving their swords behind and follows the speaker's lead.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who is saved from falling overboard during a collision on the vessel, indicating vulnerability and reliance on others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who is tightly clutched by the narrator as they fall into the abyss, indicating a close connection or protection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a character who provides guidance about safely navigating a drop into a dark pit.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a skilled and confident fighter, displaying a grim smile and taunting his adversaries during combat. His fighting style resembles that of the narrator, evoking a sense of pride and respect.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is a young character involved in the high-speed ascent, who laughs and makes a comment during the event.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is being carried by Xodar during the swim to the flier, requiring frequent surfacing for air.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is the son of John Carter, who expresses surprise and emotion upon hearing his father's name.&lt;SEP&gt;The Boy is the son of the narrator, displaying a mix of hope and uncertainty, and shares a strong emotional connection with his father.&lt;SEP&gt;The boy is a character who is being carried by Xodar, suggesting that he is an important figure in the escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f0c492fec7174d93acfd367ca61db0d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7e17d68c274e247f9a92e0dfa7535a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17f428c86f9c77692b7b7700645f08be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebe383ebeaef8c182ef68112da6f7629&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-176e51cc1b67ba293d6f8fb29ef63b47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34a9e3055f88da17653657badc062d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cb36162aba338e66b3b93a517a51f9f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbbe716988c944d1192d640b258ae3d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbf790c243f3e5d0d4de29cc208b1cfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9470c83ddd8e7e1b1a012ece31cb589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2c1456d3d47a31765ea1a0f63e5efd3d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d731e75e344e54d80aeee19cd043b4fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935472cc7fa86ac74d68d6972f9a98b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fe46f35811b518242ee5704c45d9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ca4fd0f96467b5e870a8b2eb9b2d163&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-921a093a9894a3c734cae70309767381</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE WARRIORS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The warriors are a determined group who sped to support the narrator and his companions.&lt;SEP&gt;The warriors are a group that has taken a prisoner and are navigating through the corridors on Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b513f985e87889370807eaddbed6a7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOLY LAND">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Holy Land is a mystical and revered location on Barsoom, accessible through a secret subterranean entrance known only to the First Born and their slaves.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Land is described as a subterranean location known only to the First Born and their slaves, considered a real heaven by those who worship it.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1fd4c188807a94298bfeb6bdc0fd055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c77572865c7949fb289c8ad54e38a34</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THUVIA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Thuvia is a beautiful girl who leads the procession and plays a significant role in guiding the group through the underworld.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character accompanying Tars Tarkas, also in danger as a fugitive from the Valley Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character in need of assistance during a perilous situation, showing vulnerability.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character involved in a perilous situation, displaying awareness of the dangers posed by the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character present during a battle scene on Mars, observing the events alongside the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character present during the situation but chooses to give privacy to the narrator and Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character present in the storeroom during the attack, who was asleep and thus avoided the initial gunfire.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character riding a mount that is showing signs of exhaustion during an escape from the pursuing Green Martians.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who appears to be under the influence of a master and experiences sadness. She is involved in a narrative about love and loyalty.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who appears towards the end of the passage, potentially intervening in the confrontation between Phaidor and John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who can command ferocious creatures with a low singsong voice, indicating a special ability or connection with these animals.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who explains cultural aspects of the thern race and suggests actions to be taken during the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who expresses deep love and loyalty towards the Prince, despite knowing he is married to the Princess of Helium. She wishes to serve him as a slave, considering it her greatest honor and happiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who expresses loyalty and willingness to stay and face danger alongside the protagonist.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who has been a prisoner for fifteen years and is knowledgeable about the conflict between the Holy Therns and the black pirates of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who identifies the attackers as the Black Pirates of Barsoom, indicating familiarity with the situation or the attackers.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who interacts with the narrator and commands the men to dispose of the bodies, suggesting a role of authority or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who interacts with the narrator, providing information about the fears of the therns and opening a doorway.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who intervenes in a dangerous situation, attempting to protect another character from harm.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who is guarded by two creatures as they walk alongside her, indicating her importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who is involved in the dialogue and actions within the dominions of the therns, showing a commanding presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who is involved in the narrator's plan for escape, indicating her significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who is lifted onto a creature, suggesting her importance or fragility within the group.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who is part of a diverse group trying to escape a pursuing threat. She initially rides her own mount but is later carried by another character due to her mount's exhaustion.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who leads others through a dangerous environment, showing an ability to control fierce beasts with a word of command.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who openly admits her affection for John Carter, indicating sincerity and candor in her feelings.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who participates in the journey and volunteers to remain during a halt, showcasing responsibility and involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides explanations about the hybrids and their condition in the underground world.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides guidance and information about the group's journey, indicating her role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides guidance on the escape route from a fortified location, indicating knowledge of the area's geography and defenses.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides information about the therns and the dangers of the underworld.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides insight into the actions and hierarchy of the Therns, suggesting strategies for escape.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides insight into the challenges of navigating the fortified area and was released from chains at midnight.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides insight into the events occurring, particularly the aftermath of the attack by the plant men and the arrival of the great white apes.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who provides insight into the strategic attacks of the black pirates and questions the Prince about the necessity of guarding the domains of the Holy Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who recognizes the resemblance between the Prince and the Holy Thern, and suggests using this resemblance for their advantage.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who respects John Carter's desire for privacy and steps aside during his farewell.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who sacrifices herself by slipping to the ground to lighten the burden of her mount, allowing her companion to escape from the pursuing Warhoons.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who seeks revenge and demonstrates courage by shooting the thern, indicating a personal vendetta and strong emotions.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who shares her experiences and expresses love for John Carter, playing a role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who shows deep affection and happiness upon discovering that the narrator is alive, indicating a close relationship or admiration.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who suggests carrying the body of the dead thern and carries keys that provide access to a storeroom.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who suggests using banths to distract attention and is able to call them with a singsong voice.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who was released from chains at midnight and leads the narrator through winding corridors to an opening overlooking the Valley Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a character who, like Dejah Thoris, is mentioned as having feelings for John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a companion of the narrator, who was asleep on the floor and escaped the initial attack.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a female character who expresses a desire to serve the Prince, showing loyalty and admiration. She is offered a future as an honored equal rather than a slave.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl believed to be the daughter of a proud Barsoomian house, and her whereabouts are unknown.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl who informed the narrator about the return to Barsoom, indicating her role in conveying important news.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl who informs Dejah Thoris of John Carter's return to Barsoom, playing a role in their reunion.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl who shows fear and seeks protection, likely a character of significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl who was first freed by the narrator and subsequently helped free others. She is armed with a revolver and acts as a guide through the maze of passages.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a girl whose fate is also uncertain, with concerns about her potential capture by red or green men.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a guide and ally who assists in navigating through dangerous areas, showing familiarity with the terrain and the risks involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a guide leading a group through a complex network of passages with the goal of reaching a storeroom with arms and ammunition.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a guide who leads others through roundabout passages to avoid detection.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a member of the party accompanying the narrator and Tars Tarkas.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a member of the party who volunteered to remain on watch while the others slept, demonstrating vigilance and responsibility.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a member of the party who went missing after Carthoris sent her thoat galloping toward the hills to escape danger.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is a person being consulted for advice or insight on the actions of another individual in a critical situation.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is an individual who was subjected to being a plaything for fifteen years, indicating a history of captivity and mistreatment.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is another character present in the scene, witnessing the aftermath of the death and the actions of the fellow.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is another individual expected to serve Issus and is central to the expedition's objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is described as a beautiful companion of Tars Tarkas, whose fate is also uncertain, highlighting her importance to the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is described as a beautiful companion, possibly accompanying the narrator or another character in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is introduced as a character in the narrative, potentially playing a significant role in the unfolding events.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is likely a character involved in the narrative, possibly with a key role or significance.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is mentioned as having been a plaything and slave for fifteen years, indicating a history of subjugation by the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is present with the Princess in the chamber, indicating her involvement in the situation.&lt;SEP&gt;Thuvia is the Princess of Ptarth, known for her beauty and her voluntary pilgrimage from her father's court, indicating her adventurous spirit.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c530bc2d8a3e5ffa6e7e1b615b196ddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808ddbe6ccdd93bf254656679b522a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-62abb1ac4cf24cfe818a8870240b9a6a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c8b6e33f9e011b6bce4f39de022bf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d708df29c7481f7f2727287063d43d2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8444ad2509b1d2679504e820feabb704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ff17997572867abd4f76f4d654adda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041ca20ade0f8736efede5678e381751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8ef909cf6cea9004f4cf2ca39dc840&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f7421e24bb6db8db2cf43cce33eb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-123857b6c478330f85bc333d9a7eeab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202ae065926466ff564e922828d8ca62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c0106b92cb6f20d3c3acb7b5cdb78cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0491417d3b1d17dbd4f6570ef17e2cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe5cf45af5e3799da900db83fcb3ff56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36134f2c86fa620f5fc1afeb5c999e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea85a61fc6af15c21b035b16ff189849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f063e8c8fb8dc754a765041b551fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940010d0056f8b8b43094bf27beeb53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e6e909540039e4b0a0732f451c6013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e93369af7ee026526581151dd43e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70f2bbb44eb678dedfd2d193e527d2bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c780b2690f7d5702006bb65b02e4811b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ff701e90f02ebbdfe223f97c8789b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96be56df7e782f9d519314ec83cc530c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff22eddd150fa9c82e1ebf3269b9831a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4946b446ccff9fda170ff24c30ed8581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5122be51fbf9687e6937b89f972a742f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67b69095d5fb4eb3dbe97daae753305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c6cb353d9a9d5f4be9cf6efd243bf6dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1403de9be5a8cd3ec91ce41c26a8925d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ff627f7e5d376dfb488b33baf21c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553265af22155e878e0c762c2ea5c1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a4fe2b5df5b2ed0fabd95ff2a65a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e8b4e5cb9fe7b6998ce2d6e059f797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6716a4317005ca2adb5fd451d6df6352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6453946479e0e828e52424d453708f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96eb2a40b66ea789f0a4cd3f2ec63e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7ce70b57630199d1d4144e52c899cfd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd3d00f92506b4a248933f3150a7352a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a73fbe62c4a019aaf786458159a47b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a31ee982c8901b257ed1089244c5a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cebd2d10250f3f1708ab616c25dcf6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5387a5bebe527b5c1302cedb859b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbe2b8a94bb223962e9bd344d6ec1889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad4c9898bf8ce3eb60abe1ad94ff5f73&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-58d979802dde723cae7cce270dec2ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8656b4b6a355643abf13c112ecbaf810&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e76d233bd322e66f43582e5859013c2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c843602d278a489f52282444efd5b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818231005769615743d6e44cf0d9b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f651ea5c605f9f3d54a95f1c90c89a0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78737f9e0a06b70a0bb9ae9555fd2498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75779c31636c7f365a9d05b913893782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baade9e995ad50662746a7b13183b0f4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83143cdd9a1d0eb60c6e662a220df1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb13d519a0b4f895198cfc2c98df8b98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c768a4ea224d8da779e3818ab95c45f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60721b3b1ff8467dd26b0e1844246065&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c22e4d87550fcfbcdf0c1e0d337db45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6527f91419b819bb445cd47f8d793fe4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b02017949859ea016f59b43ad5eeda2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70df0f7b7c4334f4d8af1b1558e02707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2e6f0fef68b5f0a7f5923018ebed4</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PRISONER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Prisoner is the narrator of the text, plotting an escape by feigning death and planning to attack an approaching person.&lt;SEP&gt;The prisoner is being escorted by the warriors through the corridors of Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dec572fdc799700a73d7f10c92bbd990&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLANT MEN AND APES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plant Men and Apes are considered by the Therns as manifestations of departed spirits, indicating a spiritual significance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a1fd4c188807a94298bfeb6bdc0fd055</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PASSAGEWAYS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The passageways are winding corridors beneath the dead cities of Mars, where the characters are navigating.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PRISON">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Prison is a location from which the characters are attempting to escape, featuring an outer wall and a sentry.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prison is a location where the narrator and others are detained, indicating a place of confinement.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prison is a roofless building with high walls, divided into several rooms, where the characters are located.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prison is the location from which the narrator and companions are attempting to escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prison refers to the stone structure on the Isle of Shador, symbolizing confinement and despair.&lt;SEP&gt;The prison is the facility where the narrator and others are held, with a grated window and heavy door.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-885bf7dbe26f685a917110c8c81cfc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e03da8ccb26edbf8fde791db77d403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8eb5e4ae34dcc2ce9d5542a4818bd332&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b836fd8868218c6690ae5715294518c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SOLDIERS OF HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
