      <data key="d2">chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GUARD-HOUSE">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Guard-house is a location containing swords that the narrator considers retrieving before embarking on the trip.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guard-house is part of the prison facility, filled with sleeping soldiers, and is a strategic point in the escape plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-885bf7dbe26f685a917110c8c81cfc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0a705f5ca3ac7586de6280ecff5dabe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE POWERFUL CREATURES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Powerful Creatures are formidable beings with strong paws and frightful fangs, engaged in a battle with the Therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16b92520aa86cd4fddd2580eca2b853a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DUTY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Duty refers to the moral or legal obligation that John Carter feels towards his son and the soldiers of Helium.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SHORE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Shore is the destination towards which the narrator and companions are heading as part of their escape plan.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-885bf7dbe26f685a917110c8c81cfc01</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE AIR CRAFT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Air Craft are numerous vehicles lying unguarded in the garden, representing a potential means of escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16b92520aa86cd4fddd2580eca2b853a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TERRIBLE FOREBODING">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Terrible Foreboding refers to the intense sense of dread and anxiety that John Carter feels when parting from the Princess.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ISLAND">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The island is the location where the prison is situated, surrounded by waters and nearby ships.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GARDEN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Garden is the location where the conflict between the Therns and the powerful creatures is taking place, surrounded by air craft.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-16b92520aa86cd4fddd2580eca2b853a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE JEWEL OF BARSOOM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Jewel of Barsoom is a unique and priceless stone, symbolizing significant cultural or historical importance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cebd2d10250f3f1708ab616c25dcf6b8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CRUISERS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The cruisers are smaller warships positioned between the battleship and the shore, indicating a layered defense or presence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIRST PARENT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">First Parent is a concept referring to the origin from which all animal life on Barsoom, including plant men, has sprung.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Parent refers to a primordial entity or concept from which other beings, specifically plant men, are derived.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8f314a9085fecdc7786aee01217512</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ONE-MAN SCOUTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The one-man scouts are small, individual vehicles used for surveillance or quick maneuvers, situated between the cruisers and the shore.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REPULSIVE RAYS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Repulsive Rays are a critical component of the vessel's operation, essential for maintaining its horizontal course and speed.&lt;SEP&gt;Repulsive Rays are a form of technology used to ascend a shaft, which has implications for speed and vulnerability to pursuit.&lt;SEP&gt;Repulsive Rays are a technology used to propel the cruiser far into space, indicating advanced navigational capabilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c7b23c5166102d5a9fca07fc36cb1ef1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1014144b11d6bc9183b660092a58e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cf99ba93703b4f07b83d74558ee9671</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRISONER">
