      <data key="d1">The Prisoner is an individual captured by the warriors, highlighting their vulnerable position in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d461891a972418eb14d1655c357ae53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TUMULT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Tumult refers to the chaos and fighting among black, red, and green men at the Temple of Issus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORRIDORS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Corridors refer to the passageways that the characters are navigating, representing the setting and complexity of their journey.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d461891a972418eb14d1655c357ae53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SOUTH POLAR ICE CAP">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The South Polar Ice Cap is a vast region of snow and ice on Mars, visible from the vessel as it passes overhead.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44530add08352b8b880eb7edb777f7be</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DARKNESS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Darkness is a condition affecting visibility and navigation, contributing to the suspense and difficulty of movement.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d461891a972418eb14d1655c357ae53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OTZ VALLEY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Otz Valley is a geographical area located in a mighty depression at the south pole, characterized by its vast size and depth, and is associated with the domains of the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Otz Valley is a geographical feature on Mars that the vessel will be skirting during its journey.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-44530add08352b8b880eb7edb777f7be&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f4de7021681b138c6572d77b66c4fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FLEET">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fleet consists of about twenty large battleships and several smaller cruisers, involved in capturing individuals and searching for fugitives.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet consists of battleships and transports organized for the air battle, showcasing a strategic military operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of great ships that are part of the expedition, moving at a rate of one per second to form a line toward the south.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of ships that sailed thousands of feet above the ground, involved in an incident where they grazed the surface of a mountain range.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group or force that Yersted mentions, indicating that they are expected to return to Omean and change the situation for John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is an organized group with a flagship, involved in delivering messages and executing commands within the narrative's setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is commanded by Zat Arrras and is actively searching for Dejah Thoris, indicating its organizational role in the quest.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet refers to the group of ten ships that initially retreated from the mouth of the shaft due to the overwhelming forces of the First Born.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-55a19eca534e1c90722bcaba6bf0d0c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4bea953f1bd40bf6d9a85e314fdbeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8fae3b8c057c10806b8855546fa2a43e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f52f078afdf87c4aea647dd81d1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f05633c09d904df84e543d1d5aa51c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SILENCE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Silence is a state that enhances the suspense and challenges in detecting the presence of others in the corridors.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8d461891a972418eb14d1655c357ae53</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIVIL WAR">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Civil War is a potential outcome of the rescue plan, indicating significant political and military conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Civil War is a potential outcome of the tensions in Helium, which John Carter is attempting to prevent.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a524faa9db11b6d8e0ba78bffed85d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133710c37757094f24b32287cf6f3044</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TEMPLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Temple is a location mentioned as a strategic point of attack from the valley side, important for the rescue mission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a location that has fallen before the assault of men from the outer world, symbolizing a loss of power and control for its inhabitants.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a previously witnessed location connected to the throne of Issus and significant events in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant landmark located above the pits that Carthoris is familiar with, indicating its strategic importance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant location where a fierce struggle is taking place, possibly holding religious or strategic importance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a significant location where the search for Issus takes place, indicating its importance in the storyline.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a specific area within the palace precincts where the battle is occurring.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple is a structure located above the upper pits, indicating a place of significance and possibly refuge.&lt;SEP&gt;The temple is a significant location that serves as a point of reference or potential destination for the group trying to escape the flood.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cacbf0b16743300060afa11c4c73b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aa86d78f2bb2e5145ff9051abc850f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e96546a836d85558a443f79415ac1818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee174a5fe26d1ed437fbeaaf534da837&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d66810adef7e94054186f17a12de861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f52f078afdf87c4aea647dd81d1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a3eae58bb1b31a20484bd7491decba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcd8c23863f19567a47b0d338bf750a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RELIGION OF THEIR FATHERS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">This refers to the traditional religious beliefs held by the people, which are being challenged by new ideas or experiences.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90f4870643c7b80fc79a5ab9ab123487</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE KEEPER OF THE KEYS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Keeper of the Keys is a deceased individual whose keys are missing, impacting the group's ability to escape or resolve the crisis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5221b49e5ededb6977aa59a29710dee0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VESSEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Vessel is a large, presumably mechanical object or craft that is capable of hovering and moving into a large pit, suggesting advanced technological capabilities.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vessel is a means of transportation involved in a collision, requiring skilled navigation to avoid disaster.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vessel is a ship that vibrates with the rhythmic purr of its machinery, indicating it is powered and capable of travel.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vessel is a smaller craft controlled by the protagonist, noted for its speed and maneuverability.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vessel is experiencing a critical issue with its forward ray tanks, leading to potential loss of control and speed.&lt;SEP&gt;The vessel is a ship or craft on which the black man is held captive and where the interaction takes place.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fd39baf5700bc8ce341598b693d045d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443e52a0d87636b2c7dc0fa86976141f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3572581c177d59bd25bf67c02d0373c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5c0c969b2aa049ae080527d08909391&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935472cc7fa86ac74d68d6972f9a98b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c7b23c5166102d5a9fca07fc36cb1ef1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLASPHEMERS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Blasphemers are individuals accused of disrespecting or rejecting the established religious beliefs, considered heretics by the society.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-90f4870643c7b80fc79a5ab9ab123487</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOOR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Door is a portal that opens into a dimly lit apartment on Mars, characterized by a button instead of a knob.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d7ac97eeeec2ca5930ab7f0b8f51909</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TARDOS MORS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tardos Mors is a Prince of a royal house, representing nobility and lineage, with expectations of honor and duty.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a Prince of the House of Tardos Mors and Jeddak of Helium, showing leadership and nobility.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a character mentioned as having a trusted man in his service, indicating his influence and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a character who appointed someone to a role after another person refused the honor, indicating a position of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a character who the narrator believes will be convinced of the truth and has the courage to act on his convictions.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a character whose return is awaited for resolving a dispute, indicating his importance in decision-making.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a location with royal gardens where Dejah Thoris was last seen.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a notable figure on Barsoom, whose influence is recognized in matters of consequence and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a person mentioned in relation to not returning to Helium as part of the conditions for reprieve.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a person whose safety is a concern, indicating a role of leadership or importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a royal location with gardens, linked to dreams of returning and reunion.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is a significant figure whose presence or absence affects political dynamics and allegiances in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is mentioned as a current or past leader, whose absence might lead to a change in leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is mentioned as a figure of authority or leadership, whose interests are considered by Kantos Kan in preventing conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is mentioned as a figure of authority whom the speaker is willing to oppose to rescue Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is mentioned as deceased, and his death seems to have significant implications for the leadership dynamics in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is mentioned as deceased, implying former importance, possibly a leader or ruler.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the Jeddak (leader) of Helium on Mars, a key figure in Martian politics.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the Jeddak (ruler) of Helium, a prominent character in the story, indicating a high-ranking position in Barsoomian society.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the Jeddak, or ruler, of Helium, and a significant figure in the social hierarchy of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the current Jeddak of Helium, holding a position of leadership and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the grandfather of Dejah Thoris, who took command of two expeditions to explore the northern hemisphere of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Tardos Mors is the grandfather of the Princess, who takes part in a major expedition, indicating his role in the family and community.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Tardos Mors is a noble family or organization to which John Carter belongs, indicating his royal lineage and status.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8920a88678918057bb141c7f9636c0d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e029e53f82ffdbeba2500285e859f464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba6fe6e7d6d25df18260ffbf7692d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5e144173f5e450941ba6b94f86ebf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2689f06a45abd5998519fb85220b9bd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e89417178bd5f0cae70e639617e8707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d77b7126508e140eb1d722ab80d440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70f2bbb44eb678dedfd2d193e527d2bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a524faa9db11b6d8e0ba78bffed85d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60a9da7e3358ae80aa0dde32a451ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5611c5f62cf8eed6262c37dc2e3a029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c1c1de3605517ea048c08675a03df17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203aa795181a9eb1397b2f84beb7f517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1589e9bc10a530649c9633fc000a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a77e7ac5150f49ecbdb4fdb4409a0642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300d991e887f6e7a94ba6084446b534d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133710c37757094f24b32287cf6f3044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b43139978dba5887d5c135e5174</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE RED MEN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Men are a group or faction engaged in a conflict with the blacks, attempting to reach the inner sacred precincts of the temple.&lt;SEP&gt;The red men are another group with a similar physical structure to the therns and the narrator, but they are distinct in skin color and identity.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5e32f64cbf961c7ebe05d9308a82211c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfcd8c23863f19567a47b0d338bf750a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="APARTMENT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Apartment is a dimly lit chamber on Mars, initially appearing unoccupied, entered by the narrator and Thark.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7d7ac97eeeec2ca5930ab7f0b8f51909</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SATOR THROG">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Sator Throg is a character amused by the sight of banths and involved in the training and handling of these creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a character from whom a circlet of gold set with a large gem was taken, indicating his possession of valuable items.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a character who has been taken away by the therns, suggesting involvement in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a character who holds a position of power and influence, capable of ordering punishments such as being thrown into a pit with banths.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a character who, along with his slaves, succeeded in killing one and capturing the other of the two sought individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a person from whom the narrator has taken the wondrous gem.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a person whose harness John Carter is wearing, indicating a possible connection or disguise.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is a significant figure who granted liberty to others and is described as mighty, indicating a position of power or influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is addressed by the narrator as potentially being threatened by his own vassals, indicating a position of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is described as a Holy Thern of the Tenth Cycle, indicating his significant status and influence within the infernal cult.&lt;SEP&gt;Sator Throg is mentioned as a previous owner of a similar circlet of gold, indicating a possible connection or rivalry with the thern.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6716a4317005ca2adb5fd451d6df6352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682cfb3dc6d02c7c2e7994c7caa7c551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e89417178bd5f0cae70e639617e8707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d68959082a690bb8c58c37751492f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83143cdd9a1d0eb60c6e662a220df1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e51e1d8477880f7c52ccf46556e3c955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e58012e53ec92e40f7c47c8c3805771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a31ee982c8901b257ed1089244c5a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67b69095d5fb4eb3dbe97daae753305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70df0f7b7c4334f4d8af1b1558e02707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6311329816ffebf6e549cded38827ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STRUGGLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Struggle refers to the fierce battle taking place between the blacks and the red men at the entrance of the temple.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-dfcd8c23863f19567a47b0d338bf750a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OTZ MOUNTAINS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Otz Mountains are a mountain range that circles the inner Valley of Dor and are located a hundred miles from the northern boundary of the Otz Valley.&lt;SEP&gt;The Otz Mountains form the northern boundary of the Valley of Dor, encircling it and contributing to the geographic isolation of the area.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26ef0b24e731f9a32cfb495e4f895d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f4de7021681b138c6572d77b66c4fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE WONDROUS GEM">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The wondrous gem is an object taken from Sator Throg, used as a tool to aid in the escape plan by sketching maps.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a6311329816ffebf6e549cded38827ab</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ATMOSPHERE PLANT">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Atmosphere Plant is a massive facility on Mars responsible for pumping artificial atmosphere to all parts of the planet, crucial for sustaining life.&lt;SEP&gt;The atmosphere plant is a significant structure in Barsoom, whose failure led to a critical event affecting the entire world.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9313680f9284277c6d0068f59907d106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c71c37ac9aea9f53b4337fdbaf8493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOLDEN TEMPLE OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Golden Temple of Issus is a notable structure located on the shore of the Lost Sea of Korus, within the Land of the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;The Golden Temple of Issus is a significant structure located on the shore of the Lost Sea of Korus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-26ef0b24e731f9a32cfb495e4f895d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f4de7021681b138c6572d77b66c4fe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE JEWEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Jewel is a priceless stone worn as an insignia of rank by those in charge of the atmosphere plant, known for its unique scintillation of nine distinct rays.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06c71c37ac9aea9f53b4337fdbaf8493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CIVIL STRIFE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Civil Strife refers to the potential conflict arising in Helium, which could lead to significant consequences.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5611c5f62cf8eed6262c37dc2e3a029</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OLD MAN">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Old Man is a role describing individuals in charge of the operation of the atmosphere plant, possessing the jewel as an insignia of their rank.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06c71c37ac9aea9f53b4337fdbaf8493</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JUDGMENT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Judgment refers to the decision-making process in the dispute, particularly the biased judgment of Zat Arrras.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b5611c5f62cf8eed6262c37dc2e3a029</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROJECT GUTENBERG LICENSE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Project Gutenberg License outlines the terms and conditions under which eBooks can be accessed, copied, distributed, and reused, emphasizing free and unrestricted use.&lt;SEP&gt;The Project Gutenberg License outlines the terms and conditions under which the eBook 'The Gods of Mars' can be used, shared, or modified.&lt;SEP&gt;The Project Gutenberg License outlines the terms under which Project Gutenberg works can be copied, distributed, and reused.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b38d8856480feab5752283bef0dbc3b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1cf4d481e792ef99973556a80dbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2f3648e3cf4dbbe3dbea6a4c8bce863</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GREEN MEN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Green Men are described as having naked feet, suggesting they are entities whose movement is silent and difficult to track in the corridors.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ed8eaa881de43df481740ee0848635e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MERCIFUL DEATH">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Merciful Death refers to the release from anguish, indicating a willingness to face death in a dire situation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2bb66e3143c3d99b7ed3016c869442dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEJAH THORIS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dejah Thoris is a central and significant character in the narrative, known as the Princess of Helium on Mars. She is the beloved wife of John Carter and the mother of Carthoris, and her royal status is crucial to the political landscape of Helium. Dejah Thoris is deeply connected to the protagonist, who holds her in high regard and affection, often referring to her as his long-lost love. Her beauty and nobility make her an incomparable figure, admired and desired by many.

Throughout the story, Dejah Thoris is a focal point of concern and action. She is often at the center of rescue missions and expeditions, highlighting her importance and the peril she faces. Her preservation is a primary goal for the protagonists, as her safety is constantly threatened by various adversaries, including Zat Arrras and the First Born. Dejah Thoris experiences significant mental and emotional turmoil, particularly due to her separation from John Carter and the potential danger posed by her son and husband’s actions against Issus.

Despite the challenges, Dejah Thoris remains a source of hope and inspiration for those around her. Her presence motivates the protagonist to undertake daring actions and face formidable enemies. Her disappearance and subsequent rescue efforts are central to the narrative, as they influence the protagonist’s decisions and emotions. Dejah Thoris’s character embodies courage and resilience, even contemplating desperate measures to maintain her dignity in captivity.

Her relationships with other characters, including John Carter and the narrator, are profound and impactful. She is portrayed as a figure of great emotional significance, whose well-being directly affects the morale and motivations of those who care for her. Dejah Thoris's story is one of love, danger, and political intrigue, making her a pivotal character whose fate is intricately tied to the unfolding events of the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f06165f12faf40faec1cab62f00bb8fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150a32741024f15fa5faa16e08c5f878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46817f0e5364d880844af125e330b888&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2689f06a45abd5998519fb85220b9bd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681e8c340ca9a7f2e14d3fcd3d71a3e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-41692485a75fafbf159b80ea98324da3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e9d5b5bb51756648e7a02983977bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87b6b9321f4f05f0578fcd6c878db520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43237e8924c3e87e804cbb4a0e2df875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3feecd7b55e6730b49c641bb5d5360b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3779ce2c27b4981b2df99e660baffbea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7842012554cda4bb9f52354216e4a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d66810adef7e94054186f17a12de861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f48c1d754d1ffb26016da528676dbc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5207e2e583ab1153c0186e0f0fed81b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d75a8b07d711ce1eff0a8d3d37c746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3eee5f1ac2c6536f462bf6d2d2fb2ff7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9762baf17f88ae161924df645bc3091f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89015e03c34ca60483685acd4b9fc408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c530bc2d8a3e5ffa6e7e1b615b196ddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a43c41b4e0cc30def80a6039700a0bca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5ec04b19f44e50aea83ee65f6472738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827fe0dc4cb1367d64ea93dc46b45f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165af99021c79dc0a6c523935a6d7b6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6453946479e0e828e52424d453708f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca06d2e5dc124b584060a61efedd5b65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d8b04ae7b15b144bbaef0ad0fbf97c4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ae3d51c8ed57d43c6b8f4465dfd95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e7a2060e2c27b443e01d4c73c7f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bcc97b8466964e5aa69bc08566713a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ad7db4f246beb4b819a8f0994ae7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba620ffc24b992c1aa22b35a87d8b250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f7421e24bb6db8db2cf43cce33eb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e401d5c5533e509190fb60ba8bfa478f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-288dab7b4222c07f01804ee7228c46ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bb66e3143c3d99b7ed3016c869442dc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d77b7126508e140eb1d722ab80d440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e93369af7ee026526581151dd43e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70f2bbb44eb678dedfd2d193e527d2bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b41c4f89a372b142a32bb11bf4f3a03f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4dd3df1ac8a7347e4d559c5ff38864ea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b74b5b67f66c6890acf203d7c8111324&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a6cf5a549fe9fa939ec322caa01cf9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a773a771531534f350f32a0bab74d10c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f804d99b0560937dece663ce5c7f98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f65b8a5a48d5153729a3de1ec4ca4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-60721b3b1ff8467dd26b0e1844246065&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef83a1bb59d0a6160845638665b9ef6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4f865b074dfa38019a0b7368edf0f019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fadccafc99ba487f1ebdc2a44e91a284&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07aa86d78f2bb2e5145ff9051abc850f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e6e909540039e4b0a0732f451c6013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a524faa9db11b6d8e0ba78bffed85d25&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60a9da7e3358ae80aa0dde32a451ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5380aaece7d51c8e33df868c8f3f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906dc67c04c5c3c54cafff91f6bf6a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe235097b6a7bc40f0991d5558167a0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83fa3ad9e9d77a8f079c91c9d9b7717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a6b409ade844047226580d5ff59b532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461306cf04c98666dc40fbe77653113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbe2b8a94bb223962e9bd344d6ec1889&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300d991e887f6e7a94ba6084446b534d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be809390aed5cbcb14d9c180568ae323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46834d00b98b366f113489159b3f44a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04adf1d3a5ce992fde59f92432650b96&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-489a23f49738517554abf2da01fc7862</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SIDE ARMS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Side Arms refer to weapons or equipment that produce a clanking sound, indicating their presence in the middle corridor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ed8eaa881de43df481740ee0848635e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PRISON CELL">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Prison Cell is the location where characters are trapped and trying to prevent smoke from reaching them.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2bb66e3143c3d99b7ed3016c869442dc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PRISONERS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Prisoners are individuals initially held captive but are now participating in the rebellion against Issus, tasked with protecting the Maidens.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prisoners are individuals who have been captured and are now being organized by the narrator into a formation for battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prisoners are red Martians who are chained to the wall in a chamber, indicating their captivity and lack of freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;The prisoners are individuals who have broken free and are attacking their captors in the arena.&lt;SEP&gt;The prisoners are individuals who were released from their cages and were armed with swords to fight.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ef78295a9a43f2e8c84cc7df716c9614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79bfaa16b39934f8800e01535bdd4dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a648d5f699056f4919135718d634cd3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b513f985e87889370807eaddbed6a7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e73ce07604d42f9c6e9b21c0f5f3b1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MIDDLE CORRIDOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Middle Corridor is a location within a network of passageways, associated with the faint sound of side arms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ed8eaa881de43df481740ee0848635e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOONLIGHT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Moonlight is mentioned as the setting in which the narrator was standing upon the banks of a broad river, adding to the atmosphere and emotional tone.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b74b5b67f66c6890acf203d7c8111324</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BEAST">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Beast is a large creature that is revealed when the wall and floor sections rotate, indicating it was hidden behind the partition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Beast refers to a fierce creature that was previously positioned on the opposite side of a revolving floor and is associated with the notion of danger and threat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6885d08319ecf502c70443aab4891a50&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a648d5f699056f4919135718d634cd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THREE DIVERGING CORRIDORS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Three Diverging Corridors are part of a complex maze, adding to the difficulty of navigation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ed8eaa881de43df481740ee0848635e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BROAD RIVER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Broad River is a geographical feature mentioned in the context of the narrator's experience in the moonlight, contributing to the scene's setting.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b74b5b67f66c6890acf203d7c8111324</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VAULT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Vault is a concept referring to a secure place within the cemetery where Captain John Carter enters, symbolizing a form of departure or seclusion.&lt;SEP&gt;The Vault refers to a secure location with a huge door controlled by a mechanism accessible only from the inside, indicating high security.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-300d991e887f6e7a94ba6084446b534d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-73f568e5559307a47b8b95fa17fa316c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIVE PASSAGEWAYS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Five Passageways are a junction point in the narrative, serving as a key location where decisions must be made.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5ed8eaa881de43df481740ee0848635e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUARD-HOUSE">
      <data key="d0">LOCATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The guard-house is a building where guards are stationed, containing the sleeping quarters and weaponry of the guards.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-88123f1b59edf123c3166b0b5885525c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GOVERNMENT OF HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Government of Helium is the ruling body represented by Zat Arrras, holding significant power over political affairs.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8920a88678918057bb141c7f9636c0d0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWORDS AND FIREARMS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Swords and firearms represent the weapons held in the guard-house, essential for the guards' duties and defense.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-88123f1b59edf123c3166b0b5885525c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIRST BORN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The First Born are a group depicted as noble and divine, with no peasantry among them. Even the lowest soldier is considered a god and has slaves to serve them.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group on Barsoom, known for their strength, as indicated by the narrator's feat of besting eight of them single-handedly.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group or society in whose land the Sea of Omean and the prison of Shador are located.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group who secretly dug a tunnel from the temple of Issus to the temple of Matai Shang and utilize the Therns to gather wealth and labor.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are another group from whom the characters are escaping, similar to the Warhoons.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are another group involved in the narrative, possibly with their own set of beliefs or cultural practices that are controversial or conflicting.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group associated with the goddess Issus, implying a structured hierarchy and religious or cultural significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group of high dignitaries and nobles who reinforce the guards to protect Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or domain where individuals enter and are not permitted to leave, suggesting a restrictive or imprisoning nature.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or entity that resides on Barsoom and is associated with the secret fleet and the Sea of Omean.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or faction that poses a threat to the narrator and Xodar, requiring them to plan an escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or society that enforces the domains where these rites take place, suggesting a powerful and controlling organization.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that has stolen naval technology from the ships of Helium, indicating a history of conflict or competition.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that holds the narrator and others as prisoners, suggesting their authority and control.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that is portrayed as inescapable, suggesting their formidable nature and control over others.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that opposes the protagonist, having ten thousand members within their domains.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that the protagonist defeated, indicating their role as adversaries in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group with a navy that harbours beneath the surface of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a naval force that engaged in battle with the narrator's fleet, emerging from the mouth of the shaft.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is an entity described as having a great fleet, suggesting a formidable opponent in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is an organization or group that holds prisoners, suggesting a controlling or authoritative role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is an organization that patrols cruisers, causing fear among others who do not venture from their domains due to the presence of these cruisers.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is described as possessing a mighty navy, indicating a powerful and possibly hostile group within the story.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is implied to be a group or society with a culture or practices that include the events described, such as the selection for meals and the arena activities.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born refers to a group or land on Barsoom, indicating a significant societal or cultural aspect.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-06c8b6e33f9e011b6bce4f39de022bf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d708df29c7481f7f2727287063d43d2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80b3d1ec56db5ef8672ef886c7145598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f212e50e14d429100cb7544cff0cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4ad2a6244781aedab72c9923705b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e4b09129997fb7a91db72baa774cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c6ace98e19b610b29e0db6de816d265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5075c6c6334565039e84371f24903659&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c1c1de3605517ea048c08675a03df17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553265af22155e878e0c762c2ea5c1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b852a9d3367f81e14d5fe18d854c6494&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-15499bc9bc2128fc6cca8592889ba35c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6bbfb90b7b84328adaa1e46f68731fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535538235eb01dfcd216bab7a901ead5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd6426cafa5e0838a5fd65d263895518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8d42e26d2ebe98d69db21c6b82ea8c5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90f4870643c7b80fc79a5ab9ab123487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c36f83701ff3cac994524405a183c1f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7cf352dbadda3cde2de75b1e9945ac7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46834d00b98b366f113489159b3f44a7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ed8f8e8bb759705aa097dff1c2324ba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f52f078afdf87c4aea647dd81d1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e73ce07604d42f9c6e9b21c0f5f3b1c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE REDS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The reds refer to the group of warriors who fight alongside John Carter against the black men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-628891acbda1427e7518f177398758d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ESCAPE ATTEMPT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Escape Attempt involves scaling a wall to reach a shaft that leads from the dome of the sea to the outside world, planned for nighttime when vigilance is low.&lt;SEP&gt;The escape attempt is the act of trying to leave a location stealthily, as described in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-47d378cc6dcca5a19ea2b10af50a96bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88123f1b59edf123c3166b0b5885525c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JOHN CARTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">John Carter is a central and influential figure in the narrative, known as the Prince of Helium and the Jeddak of Helium. His character is marked by bravery, loyalty, and a strong moral compass. He is deeply connected to the royal family of Helium, being the husband of Dejah Thoris and father of Carthoris, and is revered for his leadership and dedication to his people.

John Carter's adventures span both Earth and Barsoom (Mars), where he is celebrated as a legendary warrior and savior. He has demonstrated exceptional combat skills and a warrior's spirit, often fighting alongside notable figures like Tars Tarkas. His actions have earned him the respect and loyalty of powerful individuals in both land and air forces of Helium, and he is regarded as a leader whom many would follow against any adversary, divine or mortal.

Throughout his journey, John Carter has been involved in significant events, such as defeating Zodanga, opening the atmosphere plant on Barsoom to save millions, and challenging ancient customs and religious beliefs upon his return from the Valley Dor and the Land of the First Born. He is also known for his daring escape from Issus, being the first mortal to do so, and his efforts in interrupting the cruel practices of the Holy Therns.

John Carter's character is further enriched by his deep affection and devotion to Dejah Thoris, whom he is determined to protect and reunite with despite the chaos around him. He is also a figure of honesty and sacrifice, prioritizing the lives of others over his own and influencing societal structures on Barsoom through his ideas.

As a citizen of two worlds, John Carter embodies the qualities of a noble leader, warrior, and devoted family man, making him a pivotal figure in the narrative and a symbol of hope and resilience on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8920a88678918057bb141c7f9636c0d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc7b3f5722e07fd67a65e8fb1be7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9269232f99d91f950b2e2e1efcd036d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddabfd0bd8bf6b02e156424ff9c407b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3779ce2c27b4981b2df99e660baffbea&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7842012554cda4bb9f52354216e4a765&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d66810adef7e94054186f17a12de861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a221bcb1631084ef422a98443917c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133710c37757094f24b32287cf6f3044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495092be397283589740233519b5dcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d75a8b07d711ce1eff0a8d3d37c746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e6c74f70eb14cd86afae56d8763706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae579ef7acc06ef53410bc801d675e17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c530bc2d8a3e5ffa6e7e1b615b196ddc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eff6289e379a5bbb6ce19b0dc88aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5360ea6efbfef241b4593260b36361e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55a19eca534e1c90722bcaba6bf0d0c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4df2b18cd1896c0096f54e469a17bed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dfc552f7d0b3a308de82eacc193e6164&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81350d8cbbd6d8b5e2fa84130eea4bb5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3aa250e31c575970c17ded33f099e84c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6453946479e0e828e52424d453708f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33062da99c0918b07863c96eb6751bba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22e1ad1f3af901591bbdf5e3b5957aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-094a963e57ebb31d9da4dd213eabadfb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23432f8130c334a06bbe7cfa9957ad64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d64ab0385ad3464fbc5ca8002c6cc1e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5009e631aba3ff94894fe4081e86897a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5ed703fd05231acae40dc9a78f48c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2e6f0fef68b5f0a7f5923018ebed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7e17d68c274e247f9a92e0dfa7535a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d728a27adf87f0a7a11d641afb689063&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ad7db4f246beb4b819a8f0994ae7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba620ffc24b992c1aa22b35a87d8b250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40f45050d6a20b8b55e7285b8bb22a8c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba6fe6e7d6d25df18260ffbf7692d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98242f5ba56160f01ff92873f61bfe8a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbd0fd5cca73331a533757f7f594757&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07e93369af7ee026526581151dd43e2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-378619143a33f83383e8a418b9f9c820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c9fa2f165189b2177ca5c0e4a0b033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c800b530f2a9aa4ac941241f419bdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5324db2140e850349d16bd6636e59321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-290349b66f441c7882b44da1cd267609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aa38b64222e1c730376a2b084ff6bd7f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c843602d278a489f52282444efd5b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad953db00d8c2abdbfeaba1f774adf47&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32838d1c338418b6ba3de4f8e52015a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6ecb83005b0a3ed19af31b7dc7a307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6337d09fdc42bf43f4adbf33b0f37655&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b43139978dba5887d5c135e5174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77544c11bdeae685d5cc57de932d4153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1db711ffa750bb33d7442d11412d8e06&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-773c2e2557b92c3cb27281bf471ca290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9582d5fbcd0fec18f551d2401616b736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3842a58eeaf8cd4c18a171bd149f0da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5e144173f5e450941ba6b94f86ebf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e89417178bd5f0cae70e639617e8707&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e6e909540039e4b0a0732f451c6013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38627de21a3af1e2630b84098968d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d066fee844e2d8100274ab66d09c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7418d73aa79c7ecd1263d59ee184241b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa5380aaece7d51c8e33df868c8f3f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dceb1683460906a1f380e987a784c31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e2cb6922d0bff95becbc89209d302ce&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356f2ca641af882f4389e64c1cfe156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-203aa795181a9eb1397b2f84beb7f517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cacbf0b16743300060afa11c4c73b75&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-535538235eb01dfcd216bab7a901ead5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a77e7ac5150f49ecbdb4fdb4409a0642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d439770c0f7294bb2e112da933aca210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0461306cf04c98666dc40fbe77653113&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5221b49e5ededb6977aa59a29710dee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300d991e887f6e7a94ba6084446b534d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-628891acbda1427e7518f177398758d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2884565014208f9aafc19b0069db1c62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-489a23f49738517554abf2da01fc7862&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18db334173655996e9e3de660f3dfeb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1b65dcd4e5b65f014a78dfad395fdb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIGHT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The fight is a significant battle between the black men and the red men, noted for its ferocity and the involvement of John Carter.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-628891acbda1427e7518f177398758d5</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE JED OF ZODANGAN HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Jed of Zodangan Helium is a leadership role held by Zat Arrras, who exercises authority over military and judicial matters.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLAGSHIP">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A flagship is the leading ship in a fleet, used here to describe the primary vessel commanded by Zat Arrras in the battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Flagship is the lead vessel in the fleet, leading the descent into the depths towards the temple.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b53d74848fe61ebd58b7de25870cddf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e88229e411ecdc345e27bf0ded33876</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THERN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Thern is a character who is hostile towards Thuvia, becoming a victim of her revenge.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-58d979802dde723cae7cce270dec2ddf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RETRIBUTION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Retribution refers to the consequences or punishment expected as a result of the court's sentence, indicating a period of tension and anticipation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWIFT SCOUTS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Swift Scouts are a group of fast-moving crafts that are pursuing the narrator, representing a significant threat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b1014144b11d6bc9183b660092a58e1</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REVENGE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Revenge is a central theme, highlighted by Thuvia's actions against the thern after years of enmity.&lt;SEP&gt;Revenge is the new focus of the expedition, replacing the initial goal of rescue after the realization of the elapsed time.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-58d979802dde723cae7cce270dec2ddf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN MEASUREMENTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Martian measurements refer to units of time, distance, weight, and other scientific data specific to Mars, which are being translated into earthly equivalents.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f509fab32d9b0fbdcab80dfd87d54182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VALLEY OTZ">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Valley Otz is a geographic location described as a level valley with rolling hills and forests, situated near the ice barrier.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93e4b09129997fb7a91db72baa774cfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JULY 14, 2009">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">July 14, 2009, is the release date of 'The Gods of Mars' eBook version by Project Gutenberg.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a6f1cf4d481e792ef99973556a80dbc3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AUDIENCE CHAMBER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Audience Chamber is a location where Tars Tarkas is likely being taken to receive his sentence. It is an important setting for official proceedings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Audience Chamber is a location within the palace where important characters gather and make plans.&lt;SEP&gt;The Audience Chamber is the location where individuals are brought before Issus, the setting for the ceremonial entrance.&lt;SEP&gt;The audience chamber is a room in the palace where the council was held and where the body of the spy was brought.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-38bc5039b174d7262ba50a2721ad87c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7fa0605b3b0af3ae10bd81ff6ec0f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77692e6ffddee71d84df4019bdaed98d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43bfc44b4b8bc8f3727f57084e01925</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREAT HALL OF THE TEMPLE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Great Hall of the Temple is a significant location where events, such as the conduction of individuals by Zat Arrras' officers, take place.&lt;SEP&gt;The great hall of the temple is the location where the trial is taking place, described as having a broad Aisle of Hope and a platform in the center.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a11f0934cc5243985c1997fc23b28b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MANUSCRIPT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Manuscript is a document written by Captain John Carter, detailing his life and experiences, which has been pondered over by the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ae6ff778d2590cbe93dfbb660282da9a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OFFICERS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Officers are individuals who lead and command forces, and are expected to follow John Carter's lead in the face of challenges.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BARSOOMIAN TABLE OF TIME">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Barsoomian Table of Time is a system used by Martians to divide time into structured units, similar to Earth's time system but with different denominations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-52a11f0934cc5243985c1997fc23b28b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Mars is a planet associated with dreams and a sense of belonging for the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet in our solar system, characterized by its red appearance and ochre vegetation covering uncultivated areas.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet in our solar system, described as having red grasslike vegetation and great waterways where red Martians live.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet in our solar system, known for its red appearance and being the subject of exploration and scientific study.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet in the solar system, characterized here by having only one remaining sea and being associated with a fear of deep water among Martians.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet in the solar system, significant as the setting for the events described and the location of the narrator's first arrival.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet inhabited by different groups, including the Holy Therns and the red Barsoomians, as well as other creatures, all of which are part of a hierarchical society.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet that the Narrator believes they might have been transported to, but expresses doubt due to the un-Martian characteristics of the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet where John Carter spent ten years, engaging in battles with the green and red men of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is a planet with low gravity, influencing the speed of travel and the force required for movement.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is depicted as a celestial body, towards which the narrator turns and seems to have a connection with, indicated by the mention of its rays.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is depicted as the location where the events are occurring, specifically below its surface crust.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is described as a planet with lesser attraction and reduced air pressure compared to Earth, leading to unique physical experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is identified as the planet where the scene is set, populated by various wild hordes and deserted cities.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is referenced as a place John Carter has visited, indicating its importance in his experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is referred to as the mighty god of war, representing a powerful, compelling influence and a symbol of longing and aspiration for the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the celestial body that serves as the setting for "The Gods of Mars," featuring prominently in the Barsoom series.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun, characterized in this context by its surface and the unique conditions experienced by the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the fourth planet from the sun, characterized by its thin atmosphere, extreme temperature fluctuations, and unique celestial phenomena such as the sudden onset of darkness and its moons.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the outer world where water is scarce, indicating a challenging environment for its inhabitants.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet being explored, and the narrator has discovered multitudes of whites and blacks there, suggesting diverse inhabitants or visitors.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet mentioned as the location where the narrator expresses gratitude for Carthoris's survival.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet on which the narrative is set, providing a context for the appearance and behavior of the Figures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the Banth roams the low hills surrounding the dead seas, and is home to various Martian animals.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the battle takes place, illuminated by its two glorious moons.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, and the location of the door with a button.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, characterized by lesser gravity and air pressure compared to Earth.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, described as having gems far more beautiful than those on Earth.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, described with phenomena such as ice caps and clouds.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, home to the Supreme Deity Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events are taking place, known for its distinct culture and unique weaponry such as radium revolvers.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the events take place, known for its unique inhabitants and landscapes.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the narrative unfolds, featuring various Martian civilizations and cultures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the narrator has arrived, suggesting it is inhabited by a civilized people.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the story is set, described as having dead cities and lower worlds inhabited by ghoulish creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the story takes place, adding a science fiction context to the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the story takes place, known for its world of warriors and fierce battles.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where the story's events unfold, involving adventures and searches.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the planet where various races have battled for survival and where the amalgamation of races has occurred.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the setting of the narrative, where John Carter has been present for twenty years, engaging with its inhabitants and facing various challenges.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the setting of the narrative, where various creatures and characters, including plant men and great white apes, exist.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars is the setting where the Holy Therns view other inhabitants as inferior, akin to beasts of the field and forest.&lt;SEP&gt;Mars, also known as Barsoom, is the setting where the protagonist encounters various creatures, including the white apes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bb0e034aa1f544924ed3b64e528d808f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123b0f8300905c8e7557878480ae9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c8b6e33f9e011b6bce4f39de022bf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8dda25a1fdacdf60f611e0ff896350d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc05f5b96f50b7c9856d78db530d1d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba620ffc24b992c1aa22b35a87d8b250&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9da712a7c655f8901bdc9f3fb4a0cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6f5547e9fab47ba40a5a13be91087944&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-949dc44a1a314c18156adec10cd85e90&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d7ac97eeeec2ca5930ab7f0b8f51909&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34a9e3055f88da17653657badc062d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-730b68464524395dba3178e561c7c132&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bc7b3f5722e07fd67a65e8fb1be7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a293ca63ae749e20ee10ccd0b69b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abcb3e82d920234f2a3155202ab8cbdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38682fe044a197c2cdd15af662eef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6e1ce134374aa0fb25009cafd1bb18a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7418d73aa79c7ecd1263d59ee184241b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ec875fb286448c5a231b2e0b674613ff&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7407e663d0639c538204a4f83f2475d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da0399b1611c31391a38e23605c6a4cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0153c5f50c46a4640a510682675ea05&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0974acb08da1b4c1b92c316af33a88e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9327b914c391d3c6243870a0c7d7b802&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad91db0cfa902f227c8f42d4fc8ec3f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89debdc6b3600e41312c14e89346cdc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1cfa5959049998648fc259707cbe29c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be70a23f43613d282ab01428d5443025&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59d3f0f2009f3a1a1e552d208e3e428&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e1d860411b2b13228387bd01459577&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-92e23d759245c0e5c1794d6419e4a312&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3099f3fb64cc18307e48514cd1766183&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a412d7e62e543df749e5efad982ac680&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-300d991e887f6e7a94ba6084446b534d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a22e1ad1f3af901591bbdf5e3b5957aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77936b72f93fa19de1d9822b058c9022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cead3080c3879bc999f5b5b6ec863019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5090242f995a0ee5e8500bf6ef94eed3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98f38d06d8db25fac8950d2837736775&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0a229c550121312c4db9f9bbe4adbb4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7f78c9ccb74063a56ce56a2e1d5bafe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="POPULACE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Populace refers to the general population, which is expected to demand consequences for sacrilege, showing a collective mindset.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TRIAL">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Trial is an event where the protagonists are to be judged by an impartial body of nobles in the great hall of the temple.&lt;SEP&gt;The Trial is the event where nobles are being judged, and John Carter, his son, and the Great Thark are involved.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f509fab32d9b0fbdcab80dfd87d54182</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FLEET">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Fleet refers to a group of fighting-men assembled and stationed at Hastor, causing curiosity among the locals.&lt;SEP&gt;Fleet refers to a group of vessels, numbering five hundred, that are involved in a strategic maneuver against the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of battleships and troopships involved in a campaign against the Therns, aiming to achieve peace and return to the outer world.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of ships executing a strategic maneuver, characterized by speed and precision in an unexpected attack against the enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of ships traveling together, of which the battleship is a part, sailing thousands of feet above the ground.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fleet is a group of vessels moving toward Omean, under strategic command and coordination.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-efd3e0d93de6c86499fed72eef65713e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d663ab5c94c0659d8703cfef78b68e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4e88229e411ecdc345e27bf0ded33876&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81753f746888e783bd4e7e6d01676e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3076597b25663698d56a8907b5084439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89588704ee3cae64e0a062cefc137f80</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HORRID PLANT MEN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Horrid Plant Men are described as fearsome creatures, contributing to the nightmarish scenario envisioned by the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEROCIOUS WHITE APES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ferocious White Apes are depicted as threatening beings, adding to the narrator's fear for Dejah Thoris's safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE ICE BARRIER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Ice Barrier is a massive ice formation ending in a sheer wall, contributing to the geography of the Valley Otz.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-93e4b09129997fb7a91db72baa774cfd</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SURVIVAL OF THE FITTEST">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Survival of the Fittest refers to the principle by which the battle was fought, indicating a struggle for dominance and right to live.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-155a9ae6f189508e5e1a54b15041b72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMANCIPATION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Emancipation represents the goal of freeing the red men from the bondage of superstition through the battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-155a9ae6f189508e5e1a54b15041b72e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OUTER WORLD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Outer World signifies a place or realm that Thuvia and the Prince aim to reach, suggesting a goal or destination in their journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Outer World is mentioned as a place the protagonist hopes to reach in safety after escaping.&lt;SEP&gt;The Outer World refers to a realm outside the dominions of the therns, from which two individuals are at large.&lt;SEP&gt;The Outer World refers to the narrator's previous life and experiences, contrasting with his current existence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-21ff627f7e5d376dfb488b33baf21c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80eb9f50e883e48730129bb2c24b1228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a31ee982c8901b257ed1089244c5a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827fe0dc4cb1367d64ea93dc46b45f77</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BATTLESHIP">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Battleship is a large military ship involved in the pursuit of the protagonist's vessel, featuring giant propellers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battleship is a large ship with a watch that eventually detects the characters after they reach the flier.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battleship is a large vessel that is involved in a collision, leading to the boarding of the protagonist's deck by pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;The battleship is a disabled vessel to which the captives are transported, manned by a thousand black men who serve as its crew.&lt;SEP&gt;The battleship is a large warship stationed near the island, with a watch stationed in the upper works.&lt;SEP&gt;The battleship is a large, silent, unlighted vessel that looms close astern, causing apprehension for the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-452d661ef0dc01933f992e1f4cbb0181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c401d24eec318e7dd6ff9a98117d860&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c492fec7174d93acfd367ca61db0d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f2caea26e191ff7228ae666f043ee4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3572581c177d59bd25bf67c02d0373c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d43a98e16a4c8e37920ba8bd953e50b7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLAZING EYES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Blazing Eyes refers to a terrifying presence in the darkness, associated with fear and danger, and reminiscent of past traumatic experiences.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b96cba96db47085e2c6f519325397725</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ALTITUDE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Altitude in this context refers to the high elevation at which the characters are traveling, impacting their physical state and abilities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3535289447cafe1e19cf3c11eed02d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="UNCONSCIOUSNESS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Unconsciousness refers to the state that occurs quickly at high altitudes due to lack of oxygen, affecting those on the vessel.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c3535289447cafe1e19cf3c11eed02d6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CAPTAIN CARTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Captain Carter is a figure mentioned in relation to Martian measurements and scientific data, indicating his involvement in the exploration or study of Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Captain Carter is an individual who has documented the Barsoomian Table of Time, indicating their involvement in the study or exploration of Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Captain Carter is an individual whose story and scientific notes on Mars are being discussed, though some data is withheld to maintain reader interest.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-52a11f0934cc5243985c1997fc23b28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f509fab32d9b0fbdcab80dfd87d54182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b52a03d22e085e9687e45d371fea9629</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CORPSE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Corpse event recalls a traumatic moment when the protagonist encountered a dead body in the dungeons, leading to madness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b96cba96db47085e2c6f519325397725</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TEMPLE OF REWARD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Temple of Reward is a place where Martian justice is administered, and heroes are recognized, indicating its role in societal governance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9202971a6c9b597c032f8fde2a01d35a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="JUDGES">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Judges are individuals responsible for delivering justice and determining the reward for John Carter's actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The judges are a group of thirty-one individuals selected from the noble class to preside over the trial, though they appear to be predominantly Zodangans.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6ecb83005b0a3ed19af31b7dc7a307</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CHAMBER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Chamber is a large room carved from the material of the cliff, notable for its size and the dull gold material with a radium illuminator providing light.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is a large, ornate room hewn from a cliff, featuring dull gold surfaces, polished gemstones, and a smooth, hard floor, suggesting it is a place of significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is a location within the story where characters are situated and actions unfold, including secret panels and pathways.&lt;SEP&gt;The Chamber is a well-lighted room where prisoners and beasts are kept, and where the secret doorway is operated.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3842a58eeaf8cd4c18a171bd149f0da0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cce81745da273c6b721f4e683db4bc6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-83f0b3db706586131f9d3c45da8bba1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a648d5f699056f4919135718d634cd3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZODANGAN SOLDIERY">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Zodangan soldiery is a military force aligned with Zat Arrras, fighting against Heliumetic crews in the sky battles.&lt;SEP&gt;The Zodangan soldiery refers to the soldiers from Zodanga who are present in the hall, lining the aisle and providing security.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodangan soldiery are the armed forces present at the trial, maintaining order but unable to prevent Kantos Kan's intervention.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18baf96786d50da1cc2652ec45a9b1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b91c81842785853f1b7b9148297952</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HELIUM">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Helium is a multifaceted entity within the narrative, prominently situated on Barsoom (Mars). It serves as both a geographical location and a political powerhouse, central to the unfolding events and conflicts. As a city, Helium is marked by its mile-high scarlet tower and is known for its twin counterpart, indicating its significant stature and cultural importance. It is associated with key figures such as John Carter, Princess Dejah Thoris, and Tardos Mors, and holds a position of influence under the supreme command of Zat Arrras.

The city of Helium is a pivotal setting for political and military dynamics, with its powerful navy led by Kantos Kan and its people engaged in ongoing conflicts and allegiances. It is a starting point for expeditions and a destination of safety and refuge, playing a critical role in the narrative's strategic operations. Helium is characterized by its advanced technology, particularly its fast ships and unique gearing, and is a source of military might with its veteran fighting men and aerial forces.

Helium is deeply intertwined with the narrative's leadership struggles and political intrigue, requiring the selection of a new Jeddak and facing potential civil strife. It is a place where justice and fair treatment are demanded for its prince during trials, and where the populace holds a collective emotional connection to figures like Carthoris and the royal family. The city's people are described as kindly and magnanimous, representing a distinct cultural identity on Barsoom.

Throughout the narrative, Helium is depicted as a mighty nation experiencing calamities and sorrow, yet remaining a place of nobility and alliances. It is the backdrop for significant events, including battles against Zat Arrras and his forces, where loyalty to the Prince of Helium is paramount. Helium's influence extends to the decisions of the Thark council and the broader political landscape of Barsoom, cementing its role as a central and powerful entity within the story.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8920a88678918057bb141c7f9636c0d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18baf96786d50da1cc2652ec45a9b1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0051afe0d62a248a398dfeca58557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2689f06a45abd5998519fb85220b9bd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151c6925632d42abc6c6f08a41de7eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ce01b1948513d143cbcd4b1eddaaeda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebad39afb87513bd9b8bcf938fb8fd24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43237e8924c3e87e804cbb4a0e2df875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6311329816ffebf6e549cded38827ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3feecd7b55e6730b49c641bb5d5360b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddabfd0bd8bf6b02e156424ff9c407b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627d56e1e0e8e3e40a952f1e6c4de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c11cfbe8d63489be093b9a14d65fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6d66810adef7e94054186f17a12de861&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd6426cafa5e0838a5fd65d263895518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9202971a6c9b597c032f8fde2a01d35a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a221bcb1631084ef422a98443917c0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133710c37757094f24b32287cf6f3044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-495092be397283589740233519b5dcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95232bad6a3bef065f119152e4440ace&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e6c74f70eb14cd86afae56d8763706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81242062acf0dbf12fda459aa8de146d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0645e6d28537e5c8127826ee111f4dbf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eff6289e379a5bbb6ce19b0dc88aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b33af041481ac0fa8f2a1a4f22e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4ad2a6244781aedab72c9923705b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd702bb82bfdc458cb9b1d6020448ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6453946479e0e828e52424d453708f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43d3870029a94435f4a7808b5cc3561c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8b10db29c28315dcffcd42ec1182ba7a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab94c046d5beb01dc5019acc856391f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e7a2060e2c27b443e01d4c73c7f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-af5ed703fd05231acae40dc9a78f48c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b7e17d68c274e247f9a92e0dfa7535a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ad7db4f246beb4b819a8f0994ae7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abead0021cc1