      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Black warriors are a group of fighters engaged in a battle, forming a line across the gardens.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1e2bc04d789e0440373c080f9bdaedb9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SHADOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Shador is a geographic location mentioned in relation to the Sea of Omean, possibly a part of a larger narrative setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a geographical location near which several small craft and battleships are moored, playing a crucial role in the escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location from which the narrator and fellow prisoners were transported, indicating its role in the narrative setting.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location from which the narrator traveled, indicating a place of origin or departure.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location mentioned as a destination to which slaves are to be returned, indicating its role in the context.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location mentioned as a destination where individuals are ordered to be taken.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location mentioned as a place to which the narrator and Xodar are to return as part of their escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location mentioned as a place where the characters intend to return and potentially escape from.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location near which several small craft and two large battleships are positioned, indicating its strategic or significant importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location referenced as a place of imprisonment, indicating its significance in the narrative as a destination or fate for the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location to which the narrator is being taken back, indicating its significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location where the narrator and others are taken as prisoners, indicating its role as a place of confinement.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a location with a dome leading to the outer world, guarded by sentries with specific duties and customs.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a prison located on the Sea of Omean in the land of the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a prison location on Barsoom, associated with Carthoris's captivity.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is a specific position within Omean, relevant to the escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Shador is an island in the Sea of Omean, mentioned as a prison location.</data>
