    </node>
    <node id="SLAVES">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Slaves are depicted as followers of Issus, caught between fear and hope during the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves are individuals on Mars who consume the flesh of animals, indicating their lower status in the societal hierarchy.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves are individuals who are encouraged to rise against oppression, indicating a potential shift in power dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves are individuals who serve the First Born, drawn from the domains of the therns and from the outer world, indicating their subservient role in society.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves are laborers who were involved in the remodeling of the subterranean galleries and were taken to explore ancient corridors and chambers.&lt;SEP&gt;Slaves are present in the throne room, reclining near the throne of Issus, indicating their subservient status.&lt;SEP&gt;The slaves are individuals from the temples who come to the granaries and storerooms during the day.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed832c9005bcd6de678edadee8785ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ee174a5fe26d1ed437fbeaaf534da837&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38682fe044a197c2cdd15af662eef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6bbfb90b7b84328adaa1e46f68731fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202ae065926466ff564e922828d8ca62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ad91ced17fd76f9b7fb848f010f12b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a4237fb784eecdbed7be6c72ee4a8ee</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WARHOONS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Warhoons are a group of fearsome creatures characterized by their silence and terrifying presence, known for their baleful eyes that instill fear in others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are a group or faction fleeing from the battleship, suggesting conflict or fear.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are a group or horde known for their cruelty, specifically mentioned as the northern Warhoons, implying a significant presence and influence in the region.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are a group or tribe from the southern region, likely involved in conflict or warfare.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are a group or tribe that engaged in combat with Tars Tarkas, resulting in his presumed death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are an opposing group in the narrative, presenting a threat to the protagonist and their allies.&lt;SEP&gt;The Warhoons are portrayed as a pursuing threat, likely an organized group or tribe, gaining rapidly on the escaping party.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoons are a group from whom the characters are escaping, indicating a source of threat or conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoons are a group of hostile entities pursuing John Carter and Thuvia, presenting a threat to their safety.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoons are a group or faction mentioned in the text, possibly residing in or near the city being targeted for the mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoons are depicted as a group associated with dark dungeons and horrifying events, suggesting a fearsome and possibly cannibalistic nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoons are described as a group of howling devils, advancing in ranks and engaged in a charge against Carthoris and his allies.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8c843602d278a489f52282444efd5b26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-331b289581d2f7d15d72abd63236e614&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d708df29c7481f7f2727287063d43d2a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b33af041481ac0fa8f2a1a4f22e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-df11c982435f95e861fc0dd91fde9b5d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-307cb64b5b7a6a0c626a6d904683a8b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2417d5af6bb8ebfe1906e22eaeea4d53&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b96cba96db47085e2c6f519325397725&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87cf36f7152da08268ab8ec68bf17938&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593ac9d49ec07dc6c02dbd8f0ccab1a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e76d233bd322e66f43582e5859013c2</data>
    </node>
