    <node id="GUARDS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Guards are described as individuals who quickly overcame and killed the majority of the slaves during the rising event.&lt;SEP&gt;Guards are figures tasked with maintaining order, rushing across the sand towards the protagonist.&lt;SEP&gt;Guards are soldiers or protectors under Issus' command, sent into the arena to control or combat the prisoners.&lt;SEP&gt;Guards are tasked with patrolling the courts, temples, and gardens, ensuring the security of the location.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guards are a group of a dozen loyal protectors who follow the Princess on her journey, showcasing devotion and duty.&lt;SEP&gt;The Guards are responsible for patrolling Shador, with specific duties and customs during set hours, including slow-paced patrols.&lt;SEP&gt;The guards are figures responsible for maintaining security or control, and they are involved in a combat situation with the young red man and the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The guards are individuals who patrol the corridors and chambers during the day, ensuring order and security.</data>
