    <node id="PLANT MAN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plant Man is an opponent in the battle, whose sticky juice stains the protagonist's blade.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Man is the role of a pursuer characterized by bloodsucking mouths and claws, leading the chase against the protagonists.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Man refers to a creature with sucking lips, whose actions result in a death that makes human flesh suitable for the Therns to eat.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Man refers to another creature or adversary, suggesting a diverse range of threats faced by the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Man is a well-muscled, powerful creature engaged in a struggle with the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-abcb3e82d920234f2a3155202ab8cbdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5360ea6efbfef241b4593260b36361e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e33671946ad4f4f5b2e6f996f2c859cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdc7ca0ada626816a0c812ad9e1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369e6763ac9a08c733a8e0483dbb2cb</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PHOSPHORESCENT ROCK">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Phosphorescent Rock is a type of rock that emits light, encountered at the lower levels of the passageway, providing illumination in the darkness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2c1456d3d47a31765ea1a0f63e5efd3d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="YOUNG RED WOMAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Young Red Woman is a prisoner captured by the Black Pirates and considered important, as evidenced by the commander’s interview with her.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fae3b8c057c10806b8855546fa2a43e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TARS TARKAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tars Tarkas is a prominent character from Barsoom, known for his exceptional prowess as a Thark warrior and his strategic acumen as a leader. He holds the esteemed title of Jeddak of Thark, a position that highlights his significant influence and respect among the green warriors. Renowned for his bravery and formidable combat skills, Tars Tarkas has faced countless mortal combats with both men and beasts, often demonstrating a willingness to confront danger head-on. His leadership qualities are evident in his role in planning assaults, such as the attack on the Temple of Issus, and in strategic retreats to ensure the safety of his allies.

Despite his mighty bulk and enormous weight, which limit his ability to climb towering trees, Tars Tarkas is resourceful and determined, often collaborating with companions like John Carter in challenging situations. His loyalty to John Carter is unwavering, as he is willing to follow him into perilous circumstances. Tars Tarkas is not only a warrior but also a shrewd statesman and mighty general, respected by figures such as Tardos Mors and the narrator, who consider him a valuable ally in combat.

Throughout his adventures, Tars Tarkas experiences profound emotional moments, such as grieving the loss of his daughter, Sola. His human-like characteristics of love, friendship, and charity set him apart from other Martians. He is involved in complex situations, including being held prisoner and participating in daring escapes, showcasing his resilience and tactical skills.

In addition to his martial prowess, Tars Tarkas is known for his sense of humor and ability to engage in thoughtful conversations about belief and understanding, demonstrating his depth as a character. His attire, including a leather harness adorned with ornaments, reflects Martian customs and his status as a warrior. As a leader of the green warriors, Tars Tarkas commands significant troopships and convoys, indicating his strategic importance in military operations.

Overall, Tars Tarkas is a formidable and respected figure in the world of Barsoom, admired for his bravery, leadership, and the ability to unite different hordes for a common cause. His interactions with John Carter and others reveal his importance as a companion and ally, solidifying his role as a key character in the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a11c3e8c3e0a41f033f65d169562fb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e7c321f859a841ca0e55463f10ab39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0491417d3b1d17dbd4f6570ef17e2cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155a520841f1f147eaf186dab64b63b5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b94bb2efdd49e207c66c3b4856b42dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2a4c9a7e98c77fc85d55dd8c9465166&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec0c5c3f38231c4a87625db9626c95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e8ab518ccfc750df1afb7beaaf9e5279&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1403de9be5a8cd3ec91ce41c26a8925d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87b6b9321f4f05f0578fcd6c878db520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3feecd7b55e6730b49c641bb5d5360b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f37e3e8a7def60aa5153123fd40a4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7eab17c76d340b78e7d04b4ce3014258&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d0627d56e1e0e8e3e40a952f1e6c4de6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0c11cfbe8d63489be093b9a14d65fdd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3cdc7ca0ada626816a0c812ad9e1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-964af2aaf4acd0c3dce9fd7b11dc91ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9202971a6c9b597c032f8fde2a01d35a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-08eadcaf7e092280270c0aca7aaa5842&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1e735f04755bf97291c7e7ba215b41a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06aa4fa22af57c68012d4559518b9942&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9313680f9284277c6d0068f59907d106&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7889099df5359e57f62dd3d146b16efd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-32123b0f8300905c8e7557878480ae9c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f716bcab4e046c08c5eb05dd565ebb43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e3199ec3c47b077026b2d810b3a394f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eff6289e379a5bbb6ce19b0dc88aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4cac84688a88e1f331ac23bf1942580b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b33af041481ac0fa8f2a1a4f22e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c5360ea6efbfef241b4593260b36361e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b72dad86788b3397c84dad0327ae2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-63a07d95b31bd7f0773a4e70c95dad9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f43bfc44b4b8bc8f3727f57084e01925&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593ac9d49ec07dc6c02dbd8f0ccab1a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac26f47279e6517ca47662c906cd0dd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c62fc6c1b0c8d44a0b390114bb7ef329&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-abcb3e82d920234f2a3155202ab8cbdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2ec7cb3acbeed2ca8472a8e300df6f61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4df2b18cd189