    <node id="PHAIDOR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Phaidor is a character described as very beautiful, with a moment of embarrassment noted in her expression.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character expressing a desire to live in love and happiness despite a doomed fate, seeking understanding from the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character present during the situation and is in proximity to Thuvia and the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character present in the scene, presumably interacting with the narrator and observing the surroundings.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character referred to as the daughter of the therns, who reacts with anger and disbelief towards the notion of seeing the Temple of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who experiences amazement at the splendor of the Temple of Issus, indicating her presence and reaction within the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses affection towards the narrator, indicating a significant emotional involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses amazement upon seeing the Temple of Issus, indicating her sense of wonder and curiosity.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses curiosity and fear regarding the journey in the vessel, particularly due to her Martian heritage and the tradition of fearing deep water.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses fear and desperation in the face of danger, offering rewards in exchange for being saved.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses regret for her previous words and pleads to accompany the protagonist, showing vulnerability and a desire for companionship.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who expresses sorrow and seems connected to the events surrounding Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who has glorified another with her love and feels affronted by the rejection, seeking revenge.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who intervenes in a critical moment to save the narrator from being struck by an adversary's sword.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who is assertive and expects her questions to be answered, indicating her sense of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who is experiencing amazement at discovering a world beneath the surface of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who is presented to Issus and expresses doubts and fears, indicating vulnerability and uncertainty.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who is skeptical of the suggestion that the therns have been deceived by the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who is taken below decks and confined in a small compartment, sharing the space with the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who questions the protagonist's approach to dealing with enemies, suggesting a more ruthless method.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who reacts strongly to the command regarding Issus, showing fear and paleness.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who seems to have a more detached view of conflict, possibly valuing the spectacle of battle over its consequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who stands beside the narrator, indicating a level of companionship or shared experience.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a character who stands beside the rail with the narrator and expresses doubt about the truthfulness of certain information regarding the Temple of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a female slave, characterized by her white and trembling appearance, indicating fear or anxiety.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a girl who lags behind Issus's retinue and runs after the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is a girl who remains calm and composed at high altitudes, suggesting a level of experience or resilience in challenging situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is another individual present in the chamber with the Princess, suggesting a significant role in the events unfolding.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is described as a beautiful woman, experiencing strong emotions upon encountering Issus, the Supreme Deity of Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is described as a radiant beauty, the daughter of Matai Shang, indicating her noble lineage and significant presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is described as the daughter of Matai Shang and is also connected with John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is described as the daughter of the Master of Life and Death, indicating a significant lineage and association with concepts of mortality and immortality.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of Matai Shang, depicted with a fierce and malevolent disposition, commanding rather than supplicating.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of Matai Shang, described as having a penetrating gaze and associated with the Holy Therns on Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of Matai Shang, displaying malign hatred and jealousy towards Dejah Thoris, and threatening John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of Matai Shang, who expresses unrequited love for John Carter and shows jealousy towards Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of Matai Shang, who intervenes to save the narrator from an attack, showing bravery and concern for the Prince.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is the daughter of the Master of Life and Death on Barsoom, experiencing fear and doubt about the alliances of Issus, indicating her vulnerability and internal conflict.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-339c906257b62f16b009c25aebb93a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd54938ae10297f91951e3dc08c03318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80b3d1ec56db5ef8672ef886c7145598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc05f5b96f50b7c9856d78db530d1d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0844027fa3550189a9d270364e85674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f212e50e14d429100cb7544cff0cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d1f7421e24bb6db8db2cf43cce33eb2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3f392d47577a0f411eda285b198ebf39&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea85a61fc6af15c21b035b16ff189849&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827fe0dc4cb1367d64ea93dc46b45f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc67bf329b29478328d22700eef5657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c9ca80ffc66c0dd30d63d6dd2ad3f45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4bd851a51f2718867c4b20dce63ae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a6342d219ff9538b029d45a991c42a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf22396435379360201facb4abd270f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1ccf749f2b30c16f4cc985a93939e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9676c4c8b41ff0b49d14a71ae70361aa&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad069d3e03018513afb20c39dd315bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96eb2a40b66ea789f0a4cd3f2ec63e30&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a915a3180626dc866431172c413ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc537e2f3180437aa5790aa844ec7976&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89debdc6b3600e41312c14e89346cdc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510dc6fe133b57e406d839f11db76440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99ae3d51c8ed57d43c6b8f4465dfd95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbfd544a7666d71957424825d22b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0091b7eec20ccaadf8476aa83db095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ae9b01eadc7f407e1d5bca34640588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07cc24b9aeb58243bee79a445d667fd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6f2e1406ce8ebbe4ef2272e165d3aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f65b8a5a48d5153729a3de1ec4ca4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5207e2e583ab1153c0186e0f0fed81b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c77572865c7949fb289c8ad54e38a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3535289447cafe1e19cf3c11eed02d6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-979f880555ab53fcbf9eeb67a9056e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMMANDER OF THE FLEET">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Commander of the Fleet leads the fleet of battleships and holds significant interviews, such as the one with the captured young red woman.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8fae3b8c057c10806b8855546fa2a43e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIAN CREATURES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Martian Creatures are the savage denizens of the Martian wilds, attacking the protagonists.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a2a4c9a7e98c77fc85d55dd8c9465166</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MATAI SHANG">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Matai Shang is a character whose daughter is of interest to Issus, suggesting a connection to significant events or figures.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is a key figure associated with the principal temple and the messages from Issus, indicating a significant role in the religious hierarchy.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is mentioned as Phaidor's father, suggesting a position of influence or significance in her life.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is mentioned as the father of Phaidor, indicating a familial relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is mentioned as the father of Phaidor, suggesting a background of significance and influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is mentioned as the father of Phaidor, suggesting a familial connection to Phaidor's motivations and actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is mentioned as the father of the narrator and is a figure of authority within the Holy Therns, potentially offering protection and aid.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referenced as part of a court, suggesting a position of power or authority that might be significant to the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referenced as the father of Phaidor, suggesting his importance and possibly a position of authority or influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referenced as the parent of a significant character, the daughter of whom is of interest to Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referred to as the Father of Therns, indicating a position of high authority among the Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referred to as the Master of Life and Death upon Barsoom, indicating a significant role or authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is referred to as the father of Phaidor and is associated with a holy race with eternal life.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is the Holy Hekkador of the Holy Therns, a figure of authority on Barsoom, known as the Father of Therns and Master of Life and Death.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is the father of Phaidor, and while not directly involved in the scene, his mention signifies his importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Matai Shang is the father of Phaidor, though not directly involved in the scene, his presence is felt through Phaidor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f48c1d754d1ffb26016da528676dbc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-24c52f87672dabc9848d2a8d083a14c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a29095babe1a2ff500039fc4979ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ae9b01eadc7f407e1d5bca34640588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a4c2a87c1f4e9cc424db7febe61149a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-321bd48c691324503f9eb58bf49dbdcf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-827fe0dc4cb1367d64ea93dc46b45f77&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e6f2e1406ce8ebbe4ef2272e165d3aaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc05f5b96f50b7c9856d78db530d1d0b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0b6eb6f891f43fb7fcb46dec56bfd5cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7f212e50e14d429100cb7544cff0cb1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc67bf329b29478328d22700eef5657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c22e4d87550fcfbcdf0c1e0d337db45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510dc6fe133b57e406d839f11db76440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a</data>
