    <node id="THE GODS OF MARS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gods of Mars is a fictional narrative written by Edgar Rice Burroughs, involving themes of struggle and suspense.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gods of Mars is a novel by Edgar Rice Burroughs, available as an eBook through Project Gutenberg.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gods of Mars is a novel by Edgar Rice Burroughs, exploring themes of adventure and conflict on the planet Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gods of Mars is a science fiction novel by Edgar Rice Burroughs, part of the Barsoom series.&lt;SEP&gt;The Gods of Mars is the title of the story, indicating themes of adventure and mythology on Mars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3aa879e6dd4924ce82917533a3d4c573&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70a2237bd20399cfee1d7ac9f5534964&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f39bd08780868fa3aa1cb9896c0f66bf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6f1cf4d481e792ef99973556a80dbc3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-730b68464524395dba3178e561c7c132</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOLY THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Holy Therns are a fanatic and self-worshipping group who have eradicated broader humanitarian instincts and dictate the actions in a less accessible heaven.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns are a group involved in interactions with the silians, suggesting a religious or authoritative role within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns are a religious group on Barsoom who believe they receive divine messages from Issus, though they are unaware of the true nature of these communications.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns are regarded as gods on Barsoom, and are believed to have the divine right to consume human flesh.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns are sacred entities against whom John Carter has allegedly blasphemed.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns is a powerful and secretive organization with influence across Barsoom, possessing hidden temples in every community.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Therns is an organization or group associated with the gardens above the Golden Cliffs, implying a religious or mystical significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a group on Mars considered to be of high status, with their flesh being deemed suitable for consumption by the higher orders.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a group targeted by the First Born's military operation, indicating they are a significant opponent or enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a group that is guarded by a million warriors, indicating their significance and vulnerability to attacks by the black pirates of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a group whose domains are protected by a million warriors due to the threat posed by the black pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a powerful group that reside in luxurious palaces and control a network of passages, utilizing slaves and prisoners for their duties and sustenance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a religious group from whose temples the beauties for the Tribute to Issus are also taken.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a religious group previously considered holy, now viewed as no holier than others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a religious organization associated with ancient customs and the sacred precincts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are an organization that benefits from the voluntary pilgrimages of creatures, increasing their wealth and slave numbers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are an organization with the power to grant wishes or rewards, as suggested by Phaidor's promise.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are depicted as a group with a potentially cruel hospitality, yet they are considered as a possible refuge and hold religious significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are described as a powerful and possibly malevolent organization that conceived both Life and Death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are described as a race of cruel and heartless mortals who falsely claim holiness and knowledge about life after death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are described as the gods of Barsoom, indicating their revered status and religious significance in the society.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are portrayed as a cruel group whose lust poses a danger to the people of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns is an organization on Barsoom, associated with religious authority and leadership, with Matai Shang as their leader.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89113c4da6f11aefb8678fe8526edbf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-123857b6c478330f85bc333d9a7eeab9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e5e5b39a52fe718335f8e9d6edf39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec0c5c3f38231c4a87625db9626c95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5f38682fe044a197c2cdd15af662eef5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe729ce46c2462fad11275ee94493b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-449c06f1b6f91dee71f8c57cc5014980&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dceb1683460906a1f380e987a784c31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803a01fd429050acde727f1f5d0b80d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89debdc6b3600e41312c14e89346cdc9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-510dc6fe133b57e406d839f11db76440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5387a5bebe527b5c1302cedb859b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c2b778334955e9ced7c09bfb06c6e52&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f48c1d754d1ffb26016da528676dbc74&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a29095babe1a2ff500039fc4979ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75779c31636c7f365a9d05b913893782&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26a98669328fa30b8b7a975f4710c607&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3ab8dbfde418bf4917b6e144180ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f6ecb83005b0a3ed19af31b7dc7a307&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c1de3b9f0e7f1ea967106856be68ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca</data>
    </node>
