    <node id="THERN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">A Thern is a member of the Holy Thern, distinguished by unique attire and ornaments, including a significant circlet of gold.&lt;SEP&gt;A Thern is a role within a belief system that involves a cycle of reincarnation and spiritual immortality, central to the practices and rituals described.&lt;SEP&gt;The Thern is a group that has engaged in combat with the narrator's crew, indicating their opposition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Thern is a role held by an individual who confronts the narrator, wearing one of the rare jewels as a sign of their rank and position.&lt;SEP&gt;The thern are a group of individuals who seem to have power and control over the prisoners and the environment, but they live in constant fear of assassination.&lt;SEP&gt;The thern are a group or entity feared for their mysterious and superstitious nature, prompting heavy security measures.&lt;SEP&gt;The thern are a group or race that engage in combat with the narrator and their allies, suggesting they are adversaries in this context.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern is a character involved in a conflict, who finds themselves turning against a common enemy alongside others.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern is a race described as being bald from birth, with wigs being an important part of their apparel due to cultural reasons.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern is a term used to describe a group or individual, possibly with connotations of strength and respect, as indicated by the comparison to a Dator.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to a group or concept involved in warfare, presenting an obstacle to peace for the fleet near Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to a group or race distinct from the First Born of Barsoom, potentially adversarial to the narrator and others in the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to a group or race, whose harness and metal the narrator wears, indicating a connection to an enemy of the captors.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to a role or title associated with individuals who might guard the River Iss and protect voyagers.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to an ancient cult on Barsoom, believed to hold the secrets of life and death, yet are as ignorant as the speaker about the mysteries of life.&lt;SEP&gt;Thern refers to individuals who are part of a group that rarely traverse the underworld at night due to fear of the banths and potential attacks from prisoners.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are golden-haired, white-skinned warriors who fight with desperate courage against the Black Pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are individuals involved in a conflict, facing extermination and seeking safety in subterranean galleries.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are individuals known for disguising themselves as red men and infiltrating other groups, posing a threat to security.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-808ddbe6ccdd93bf254656679b522a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-202ae065926466ff564e922828d8ca62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da31980c5aadf67c1b4e0845e3002be9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-42f063e8c8fb8dc754a765041b551fbc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d56d13213c1e66414a1713c9fa5cfdfe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18ff701e90f02ebbdfe223f97c8789b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f6935c77e3f98e0a9662defff47ba72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81753f746888e783bd4e7e6d01676e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9502067fd0cb8fc03f8323bae38b4131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c374bf38b9e40f8bbeeea4db6dcc0472&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64474596228fc708f1e3fea89d9ec14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a6b409ade844047226580d5ff59b532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c71c37ac9aea9f53b4337fdbaf8493&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cebd2d10250f3f1708ab616c25dcf6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7747bf1bf113982bf92fc681219b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa38df0408d03dc87421f9da494e393f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215cc9a11b792d42bd9db23d7399186c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a59d3f0f2009f3a1a1e552d208e3e428</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE HOLY THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Holy Therns are a group that consumes human flesh, specifically from those who have died under the influence of plant men. They reside on the outer slopes of grim hills and are part of a cruel and hateful race.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Therns are a religious group associated with temples, providing individuals to serve in the retinue of Issus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-3356245cc78413b113811e37a4b2050b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5324db2140e850349d16bd6636e59321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PTARTH">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Ptarth is a geographic location, known as the court of Thuvia's father, the Jeddak, indicating its royal significance.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-07e93369af7ee026526581151dd43e2a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Black man is a character involved in the struggle, uniting with Thern against the common threat of the Banths.&lt;SEP&gt;The Black Man is an individual who provides detailed explanations about the genesis and characteristics of plant men, likely holding knowledge or authority on the subject.&lt;SEP&gt;The Black Man is described as the first creature to break through the shell on Barsoom, initiating the peopling of the planet.&lt;SEP&gt;The black man is a captive who is bound upon the deck and engages in conversation about the genesis of Barsoomian life, possibly as a distraction.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fd39baf5700bc8ce341598b693d045d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fa38df0408d03dc87421f9da494e393f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8f314a9085fecdc7786aee01217512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a54ae772b882a5b23dec9acd964a9f8b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE LESSER THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Lesser Therns are part of the same race as the Holy Therns, carrying out various duties through labyrinthine passages connected to the palaces of the Holy Therns.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5324db2140e850349d16bd6636e59321</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE SHAFT">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Shaft is a black and yawning opening in the glowing dome of the underworld, serving as a potential escape route.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a geographical feature or structure that must be navigated, presenting challenges due to its shape and the presence of pursuing scouts.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a passage that led the characters beneath the arena, playing a crucial role in their current situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a passageway from Omean's dome to the world above, crucial for escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a strategic location from which the navy of the First Born emerges, leading to a battle with the narrator's fleet.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a vertical passage that the characters are navigating, presenting both a physical obstacle and a potential means of escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Shaft is a vertical passage through which the characters are ascending at high speed.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9dd21470cebb00b207669a678b79f42d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8bb1e2efd94113cf087ebb11884aa04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6a4237fb784eecdbed7be6c72ee4a8ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f52f078afdf87c4aea647dd81d1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-543fb2ae09cc6db7d88bd7f2fef6f039&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1014144b11d6bc9183b660092a58e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-921a093a9894a3c734cae70309767381</data>
    </node>
