    </node>
    <node id="GREEN FOLK">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Green Folk are a group of individuals occupying a room that Tars Tarkas and his companion must navigate through, indicating their presence as a potential obstacle.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Folk are inhabitants or entities occupying a rear room, indicating their presence in the setting.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd03f2979188cf5a15b13474eca765de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a198e766ea844cac99bc89f040e161e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SELF-DEFENCE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Self-Defence is the principle followed by the protagonist, who claims to kill only in self-defence and not for murder.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5207e2e583ab1153c0186e0f0fed81b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARS' ONLY REMAINING SEA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Mars' only remaining sea is a significant geographical feature near which Phaidor was born, highlighting its rarity and influence on Martian culture.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-339c906257b62f16b009c25aebb93a6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TAN GAMA">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Tan Gama is a character associated with warriors and is mentioned in connection with Tars Tarkas' cell.&lt;SEP&gt;Tan Gama is a character who communicates with Tars Tarkas and is part of the group of men mentioned, indicating a role in the unfolding events.&lt;SEP&gt;Tan Gama is a character who was defeated by John Carter, displaying an expression of utter bewilderment. He is associated with the great Tharks, a group of fierce green warriors on Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Tan Gama is a character who was involved in a battle with the Thark and left a short-sword for repair, indicating a role in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Tan Gama is a warrior involved in a recent battle with the Thark, whose short-sword was broken and given for repair.&lt;SEP&gt;Tan Gama is a warrior who is summoned to take the Thark before Kab Kadja, indicating a role in the unfolding events.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5bc7b3f5722e07fd67a65e8fb1be7085&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8547e483bbd651bfa8dda4ee339da7ee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-261e6abe4a29dd3965c6c0ac95e9de36&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a198e766ea844cac99bc89f040e161e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd03f2979188cf5a15b13474eca765de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-026eb15bfc502ccc60ee3c2f2018ca57</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MURDER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Murder is the act that the protagonist refuses to commit, differentiating it from self-defence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5207e2e583ab1153c0186e0f0fed81b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEAR OF DEEP WATER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fear of deep water is a common cultural attribute among Martians, influenced by the long absence of seas on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-339c906257b62f16b009c25aebb93a6e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZAT ARRRAS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Zat Arrras is a character associated with the enforcement of harsh penalties for fugitives from the Valley Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character confronted by the protagonist, who hesitates between surrendering or fighting before ultimately deciding to flee.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character involved in the political affairs of Helium, seen as a traitor by John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character involved in the tribunal, responsible for charging the protagonist, suggesting a position of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character occupying a palace with guarded pits beneath it, suggesting a position of authority or power.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who accuses John Carter of being a coward and liar, leading to a physical confrontation.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who accuses John Carter of blasphemy and addresses the judges, influencing the verdict.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who challenges the speaker, warning against blasphemy and representing opposition to the speaker's appeal.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who commands soldiers and attempts to prevent John Carter from leaving the Throne of Righteousness.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who exercises caution in handling prisoners and returned wanderers, fearing public demonstrations of support.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who harbors animosity and hatred towards the speaker, with a desire to humiliate and kill them. He is portrayed as cold, haughty, and uncompromising, especially in his interactions with others.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who has taken John Carter's sword and interacts with the judges, showing a position of authority or influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who holds a position of authority, possibly a judge or ruler, and is involved in the sentencing of John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who holds authority and makes decisions, such as ordering someone to be taken to the pits, indicating a role of power.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who holds authority, commanding officers to seize another character, indicating his leadership role.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who holds power over John Carter, making threats and offering a magnanimous yet ominous alternative.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who is currently occupying a palace and has pits beneath it where guards are stationed.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who is cursed by Dejah Thoris, blamed for her cruel fate.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who is involved in a battle against the protagonist's fleet, engaging them with heavy fire.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who is involved in a potential conflict in Helium and is being offered a chance to avoid civil strife.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who may be holding the narrator and possibly Carthoris captive, indicating a position of power or antagonism.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who might be informed about the fleet's movements, indicating a potential threat or oversight.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who poses a threat to the speaker, indicating a position of influence or authority that could lead to severe consequences.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who questions John Carter about his return from the Valley Dor and the Land of the First Born, expressing pleasure at his confirmation but later accusing him of blasphemy and cowardice.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who receives a haughty sneer from Kantos Kan, suggesting opposition or disdain from the loyal group.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who sends a messenger to inform the protagonists about their trial by an impartial body of nobles.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who sends greetings and is aware of a plot to make the protagonist Jeddak of Helium. He has made an offer to the protagonist.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character who was at Helium when Dejah Thoris disappeared and commands a fleet searching for her.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character with a cold, haughty, and uncompromising attitude, questioning the status of certain individuals and requiring more information about their journey.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character with ambitions to become Jeddak of Helium and is described as having a cruel heart.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a character with authority, possibly a military leader, who commands officers and is associated with Zodanga.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a commander of a fleet searching for a missing individual named Dejah Thoris, indicating his leadership role in this quest.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a commanding figure in Helium, holding supreme authority and expressing animosity towards the narrator, with intentions to humiliate and possibly kill them.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a commanding figure leading a flagship in a naval battle, characterized by thin features and commanding a Zodangan crew.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a figure of authority who is opposed to John Carter and his supporters, showing frustration and helplessness.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a figure of authority, likely a leader or high-ranking officer, as their officers are responsible for conducting individuals to the great hall of the temple.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a figure of authority, possibly a judge, involved in a trial where he initially denies the defendant a fair hearing but is pressured by the public to allow it.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a figure whose biased judgment is mentioned, suggesting a role in the conflict within Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a leader commanding a fleet of ships, opposing the Prince of Helium, and engaging in battles with Heliumetic crews.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a man with ambitions to become the Jeddak of Helium, posing a threat to others who might stand in his way.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a person held responsible for the failure of the expedition, and there is a desire to confront him in battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a person to whom the character in the text is intensely loyal, indicating influence and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a person who is proposed to become the new Jeddak of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a person whom Parthak is loyal to, indicating a position of authority or influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is a representative of the government of Helium and is portrayed as a potential adversary who could influence political outcomes.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who commands officers and is involved in the events leading to the trial described in the text.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who had an audience with Dejah Thoris, which resulted in her mental distress and subsequent attempt to flee.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who is assured that the task involving the note will not harm him in any way.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who is aware of a plot to make the narrator Jeddak of Helium and has made an offer to the narrator regarding their freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who is described as white and trembling, indicating a state of fear or anxiety amidst his officers.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an individual who sends a surrender demand to Kantos Kan in the name of the Jeddak of Helium, suggesting a position of authority or command.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is an opposing leader whose ships are initially not aligned with the Prince of Helium, indicating a rival faction in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is associated with espionage, having spies who are identified by Hor Vastus.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is depicted as a person with spies and assassins, possibly holding prisoners in pits, indicating a position of power and influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is described as having a sardonic smile and cruel lips, and he is addressed as the Jed of Zodanga.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is described as the Jed of Zodanga, who meets his end by hurling himself into the depths below during a moment of hesitation.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is implied to be an individual who employs spies, as indicated by Hor Vastus's comment about the spy.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is implied to be the mastermind behind the spy, suggesting a role as an antagonist.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is likely a leader or authority figure within the Zodangan organization, responsible for holding the narrator prisoner.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is perceived as a cruel figure responsible for Dejah Thoris's distress and separation from John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is portrayed as a villain whose spies are a significant obstacle to the plans being executed.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is portrayed as ambitious, with aspirations for the title of Jeddak of Helium, indicating a political or power-driven role.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is someone in a position of authority, to whom Parthak might have sought to prove his loyalty by delivering a note.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is the Jed of Zodanga, who has been persistently pursuing Dejah Thoris for marriage.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is the Jed of Zodanga, who holds authority and makes decisions regarding the court's sentence, demonstrating power and political influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is the presiding magistrate who calls John Carter to be judged, indicating his role as a leader or authority figure in the event.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras is the representative of Tardos Mors, acting on his behalf.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras refers to a location associated with pits where the protagonist was held, contributing to the delay in their mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras refers to the location of the pits where the body of a guard was left behind during a journey.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-51c91641950b5371949cd00cb19ee78d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec090a1531505a82f52e76f197bd709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dad8def4f34b963a5737d3ed48d75d4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8920a88678918057bb141c7f9636c0d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e029e53f82ffdbeba2500285e859f464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-76eff6289e379a5bbb6ce19b0dc88aa4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18baf96786d50da1cc2652ec45a9b1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1ad7db4f246beb4b819a8f0994ae7c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5ec04b19f44e50aea83ee65f6472738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77692e6ffddee71d84df4019bdaed98d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-773c2e2557b92c3cb27281bf471ca290&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba6fe6e7d6d25df18260ffbf7692d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-150a32741024f15fa5faa16e08c5f878&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68f1a6e31899408aeeec6a28a06f7b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5e144173f5e450941ba6b94f86ebf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d992d50ff8d6d6a2e98bf2b0019642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fe97f250482c686ce435b237250ec83f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-19b91c81842785853f1b7b9148297952&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-57e6e909540039e4b0a0732f451c6013&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d77b7126508e140eb1d722ab80d440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-681e8c340ca9a7f2e14d3fcd3d71a3e4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3806151a083dd701c29455b3a3f12e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea33f874d5e3c117742eceb580ddf105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd702bb82bfdc458cb9b1d6020448ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60a9da7e3358ae80aa0dde32a451ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a68ab2d56f3a58dae0859abb96ba81f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b99744d09aa8c4015948f8dc5e7f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5611c5f62cf8eed6262c37dc2e3a029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e9d5b5bb51756648e7a02983977bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc3d412e05467116b42fd3c9af8d965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a0ba9e0d4459c3f9f24f06c81a870d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b53d74848fe61ebd58b7de25870cddf1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43237e8924c3e87e804cbb4a0e2df875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6453946479e0e828e52424d453708f6b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a356f2ca641af882f4389e64c1cfe156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ddabfd0bd8bf6b02e156424ff9c407b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e797ebb432bac2d42d4a50cdf4e2429&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38bc5039b174d7262ba50a2721ad87c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-290349b66f441c7882b44da1cd267609&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83fa3ad9e9d77a8f079c91c9d9b7717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8917f33ca9393e6e40d34847a0b96e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ab94c046d5beb01dc5019acc856391f5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f509fab32d9b0fbdcab80dfd87d54182&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99c39c37bc3b545fc1976766cc4848db&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f804d99b0560937dece663ce5c7f98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-52a11f0934cc5243985c1997fc23b28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-133710c37757094f24b32287cf6f3044&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebd37ffff0b33a7e235d87ed7805fbdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc762f5d59833da40830b39a8c156c55&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d663ab5c94c0659d8703cfef78b68e04&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-188e20abff12b91977ee19e7cec8de54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4bea953f1bd40bf6d9a85e314fdbeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0958c186ba3135c1e8cf7f85bf340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a03d32b4f129d8e3a6da9b664e8bae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01455886e310937a5b5e517c7050fde1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e6c74f70eb14cd86afae56d8763706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18db334173655996e9e3de660f3dfeb6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcf47f64aae75975f5f02f3ddf9a1b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b43139978dba5887d5c135e5174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1b65dcd4e5b65f014a78dfad395fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77544c11bdeae685d5cc57de932d4153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce7b4df675ffbd231e4dfa153bac440</data>
    </node>
    <node id="COMMAND">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Command refers to the leadership and decision-making authority held by the protagonist over Carthoris and Xodar.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-307cb64b5b7a6a0c626a6d904683a8b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE RED YOUTH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Red Youth is a young individual who is imprisoned in a cell and is part of a plan to escape, showing courage and determination.&lt;SEP&gt;The Red Youth is an individual mentioned in the context of being fetched, suggesting involvement in a larger plan or mission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Red Youth is described as a brave individual who is terrorized by deep water but possesses mighty skills in battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The red youth is a character who questions the reason for traveling to Helium and gives a peculiar look upon receiving an answer.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-d29b3deb40d1b6cb2b5a52d0f968e28b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd6426cafa5e0838a5fd65d263895518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed0051afe0d62a248a398dfeca58557b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0409b3cde140585f12f74a86142d05cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ZODANGA">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Zodanga is a city on Barsoom that was attacked by Tars Tarkas and his warriors to rescue Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a city on Barsoom, notable for its soldiers and the judges who are predominantly from there.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a geographical location where the events are taking place, known for its warriors and possibly its political climate.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a hostile city where the narrator and Kantos Kan once searched for Dejah Thoris, indicating its importance in past conflicts.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location associated with Zat Arrras, indicating a place of political or military importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location associated with Zat Arrras, indicating his authority and possibly his domain or jurisdiction.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location associated with Zat Arrras, indicating it is a place of significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location associated with Zat Arrras, likely a city or region in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location mentioned as a place where warriors are known to be handsomely accoutred.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location mentioned in the context of its men having a will with John Carter, indicating a conflict or power struggle.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location that was defeated by John Carter and the green hordes, resulting in its vassalage to Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location where Zat Arrras holds the position of Jed, appointed by Tardos Mors.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location whose soldiers are present and initially in control before being overwhelmed by the supporters of John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location whose soldiers are present within the temple and are commanded by Zat Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a location, possibly a city or region, where the events are taking place, and is governed by a Jed.&lt;SEP&gt;Zodanga is a naval organization associated with false identities and operations under Sab Than, the Prince.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a356f2ca641af882f4389e64c1cfe156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2666235d718f51c88b32ca9f3460dc4c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9b90dbaba8cc3ca973904a4cee3cf24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d77b7126508e140eb1d722ab80d440&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a5e144173f5e450941ba6b94f86ebf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea33f874d5e3c117742eceb580ddf105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01455886e310937a5b5e517c7050fde1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b99744d09aa8c4015948f8dc5e7f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68f1a6e31899408aeeec6a28a06f7b62&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd6426cafa5e0838a5fd65d263895518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1061c20e9da039c1ef6d01a5f9f830bd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc3d412e05467116b42fd3c9af8d965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1b65dcd4e5b65f014a78dfad395fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-40e7a2060e2c27b443e01d4c73c7f28c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b41c4f89a372b142a32bb11bf4f3a03f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOTHERHOOD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Motherhood refers to Dejah Thoris's role as a mother, providing her with solace and purpose despite her past suffering.&lt;SEP&gt;Motherhood refers to the duties and emotional impact experienced by the Princess after the loss of her son.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04adf1d3a5ce992fde59f92432650b96</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DEEP WATER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Deep Water is a concept representing fear and challenge for the red youth, due to the long absence of large bodies of water in their experience.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0409b3cde140585f12f74a86142d05cc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Therns are a group with a hierarchical structure, where Matai Shang holds a significant position of power.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are another group mentioned in the context of the narrative, possibly involved in conflict or pursuit.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group engaged in combat, equipped with rifles and shields, defending against attacks from pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group opposing the black pirates of Barsoom, engaged in efforts to rescue young women from their adversaries.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a group involved in a battle, fighting against the First Born, indicating their role in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a group on Barsoom, described as having evolved from the pure white ape of antiquity and considered a lower order.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a group or organization within whose dominions the events are taking place.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a group or society that do not practice marriage, indicating unique cultural norms and societal structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a group that claims the arms and ornaments of those who reach the Valley Dor and also assert ownership over individuals.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are a race on Barsoom who consider themselves gods and believe that all life on the planet exists to support them.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are an organization or group mentioned as being aware of John Carter's past actions, indicating their role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are an organization or group within whose dominions the events are occurring, potentially hostile towards outsiders.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are depicted as a group that worships plant men and apes, reverencing them as the abodes of departed spirits.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are described as a group that has harassed and persecuted the speaker, indicating a potential adversarial role.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are individuals or a group involved in a battle along a cruel frontier, suggesting conflict and territorial struggle.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are portrayed as a holy race that considers it an honor for lesser creatures to serve as slaves among them. They are involved in perpetuating superstitions and deceptions.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns are referred to as a group possibly involved in conflict or hostile activities, similar to the pirates.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns is a group or community on Mars, with Phaidor being a daughter of this group, indicating a cultural or religious background.&lt;SEP&gt;Therns refer to the white race that is part of the hybrid population in the underground world.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-339c906257b62f16b009c25aebb93a6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95e70c3e694c727832877be7ede74e80&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5cf99ba93703b4f07b83d74558ee9671&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d81037675f5b075ca39bbd7280bffb81&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940010d0056f8b8b43094bf27beeb53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fd4c188807a94298bfeb6bdc0fd055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7d4bd851a51f2718867c4b20dce63ae6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea33f874d5e3c117742eceb580ddf105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d066fee844e2d8100274ab66d09c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4946b446ccff9fda170ff24c30ed8581&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a6e3e6ec143a079a4d65379d29f1f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d22f942245f43a066705ca39e7afcb84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9a31ee982c8901b257ed1089244c5a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d3f1e23738091ab20178aeaf5ad79c85&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1f3ab8dbfde418bf4917b6e144180ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c22e4d87550fcfbcdf0c1e0d337db45&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-70df0f7b7c4334f4d8af1b1558e02707</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VALLEY">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Valley is a broad area surrounded by cliffs and a range of mighty mountains, creating a confined natural setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley is a geographical feature offering a magnificent view, indicating its expansive nature and significance in the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley is described as having a vivid scarlet carpet, located five hundred feet below the narrow ledge and cave.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley is described as unknown and hostile, presenting challenges and threats to those trying to navigate or escape from it.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley is the area from which the narrator considers launching a concerted attack on the Temple.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley is the setting where the characters are pursued, featuring level sward and scattered boulders.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0f37e3e8a7def60aa5153123fd40a4c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-95eb1259e0fa5d408ab67b004adbbeb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4a969533c3173ec88c8dc881084a5075&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-264ac3c16fad75dd9c5d97bf8e4b4ec5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c52ab8778aee4f0c53248a452d1143f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="&quot;PLAIN VANILLA ASCII&quot;">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">"Plain Vanilla ASCII" is a format used by Project Gutenberg-tm for distributing electronic copies of works. It is a simple text format that ensures accessibility and ease of distribution.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a1c59e6c561451677f9e9d7b7379f99</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIRST BORN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">First Born are an opposing group in the battle against the Therns, playing a key role in the ongoing conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is a group associated with the arena where Dejah Thoris would be fought over by wild beasts.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is a group or concept that is suggested to have lured the therns to a fate similar to that of the Barsoomians.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is a group or organization mentioned as having a potential reaction against their goddess.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is a group witnessing the downfall of Issus, influenced by John Carter's revelation of her true nature.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an elite group or race that Xodar was a part of, and they hold significant status and power.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an entity that appears to have knowledge of the principal movements of the protagonist and their men, suggesting a controlling or adversarial role.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an organization or group mentioned alongside Holy Thern, possibly with its own beliefs or customs.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an organization or group mentioned in the text, possibly with a hierarchical or elitist structure.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an organization or group that has captured Dejah Thoris, posing a threat.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born is an organization that appears to have knowledge of the principal movements and is capable of orchestrating attacks and other strategic actions.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a group described as devils who are aggressive and attack with swords.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a group of individuals or a status that involves being a prisoner under Issus's rule.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a group or civilization on Mars, known for being part of the land where significant events are remembered.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a group or community that the narrator describes as having a negative impact on those who live among them.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a group whose vessels are targeted for destruction by the fleet entering Omean.&lt;SEP&gt;First Born refers to a species or group of beings that are considered significant, and there is a desire to fight for them as an act of atonement for past ignorance.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group of individuals characterized by their aggressive actions and use of flying machines.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group previously believed to be holy, now considered no holier than other groups.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a group with a harbor at Omean, who are involved in a battle and have their ships used against them strategically.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are a non-productive race that relies on the labor and wealth collected by the Holy Therns. They occasionally raid the outer world for resources and people, priding themselves on luxury and idleness.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are depicted as wild beasts who are involved in fighting within an arena and dragging a bleeding corpse through the dirt and dust.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are described as either gods or mortals who are a powerful race, suggesting their control over others and the challenges in opposing them.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a fleet involved in the expedition, which was supposed to be contained in Omean, indicating its significant and possibly adversarial role.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a fleet that poses a threat to the expedition and is supposed to be confined in Omean, indicating their significance in the conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group associated with the Land of the First Born, known for their successful prevention of escapes from their region.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group of fighting-men on Mars, known for their prowess in battle, who attempt to stop the uprising.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group of individuals, of which Dator Xodar is a part, indicating a structured hierarchy or society.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or class characterized by having black hair, which distinguishes them from others in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or class that includes nobles whom Issus may choose to punish by imprisoning them in the Temple of the Sun.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or navy that guards the entrance to Omean, representing a formidable force.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or organization in whose power the characters find themselves and are wary of.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group or society from which the characters have escaped, known for their inability to keep prisoners from escaping.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that holds significant power and influence within the narrative, with ten thousand members mentioned within their domains.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that is likely responsible for holding Dejah Thoris, posing a significant threat to the narrator and his mission.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that possesses exclusive knowledge of a subterranean entrance to the Holy Land on Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group that previously held John Carter captive and is associated with Yersted.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a group whose members are considered divine and do not perform any work, relying on slaves for all tasks.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is a powerful group or organization with a significant fleet of battleships, involved in a strategic military operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born is an organization or group that patrols the outer valley, instilling fear in the inhabitants and preventing them from leaving their domains.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born of Barsoom is a race of black men who are the oldest on the planet, tracing their lineage directly to the Tree of Life.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born refers to a group or class that is observing the assembly, suggesting their status or authority within the context.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born refers to a group or race that has a connection with Omean and poses a threat that needs to be managed.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born refers to a group that has exclusive knowledge of the subterranean entrance to the Holy Land, indicating a revered status.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born refers to a privileged class on Barsoom, living lives of luxury and idleness, and fighting is their primary activity. They are distinguished by their long lives, not dying of natural causes.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-80eb9f50e883e48730129bb2c24b1228&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79c1b239e85ba6e45a8d3cfd5dd89d08&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68427a98a52f5c6bfa5aa4f4e34e079f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e0844027fa3550189a9d270364e85674&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47ff22de37061b202fbd099af0fca2dd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f06165f12faf40faec1cab62f00bb8fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-85e5e5b39a52fe718335f8e9d6edf39f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e678ea71ac9a1264539f43637bf2a809&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5bd91746b54706f1cdd87796a2646a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13123e8cc4e42bf2ebd1e6c36837aab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-910404a8e8ab7a8ecae676639f332071&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-55a19eca534e1c90722bcaba6bf0d0c9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fd4c188807a94298bfeb6bdc0fd055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea33f874d5e3c117742eceb580ddf105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b86cc68abfabb7895f5f31421d51d427&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f38627de21a3af1e2630b84098968d10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13a6342d219ff9538b029d45a991c42a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe729ce46c2462fad11275ee94493b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d0fb802276a52d0fbc7cbca2ed3cb4b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906dc67c04c5c3c54cafff91f6bf6a60&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-26ef0b24e731f9a32cfb495e4f895d9e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dceb1683460906a1f380e987a784c31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a027e972d7eb768695014c7c960f5758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae83a9d328abc751e8b03536497faf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b24d0bed8f7d9763208b3080b3ddeb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-803a01fd429050acde727f1f5d0b80d5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe8483a1bbc19b7757cade3ab93f3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f87b2173e6bc1dc31b41308980db1e72&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0fe46f35811b518242ee5704c45d9fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bc8ba319c10b95a0296d782317a73a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a29095babe1a2ff500039fc4979ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3964e585dee08446ad325587a718d0b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f65b8a5a48d5153729a3de1ec4ca4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77936b72f93fa19de1d9822b058c9022&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-07cc24b9aeb58243bee79a445d667fd1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c77572865c7949fb289c8ad54e38a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215cc9a11b792d42bd9db23d7399186c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a03d32b4f129d8e3a6da9b664e8bae&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3076597b25663698d56a8907b5084439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8c4010c210dcbb6da5ccd528fdf874&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89015e03c34ca60483685acd4b9fc408</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PITS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Pits are a location beneath the city of Helium where individuals are taken, possibly as a form of imprisonment or punishment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits are a location beneath the palace used as a place of imprisonment for those who refuse to provide information.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits are a location beneath the palace, reached via secret passageways known to the leader of the party.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits are described as a dangerous area that is about to be flooded, posing a threat to those within.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits are described as a trap that the narrator and his force have been drawn into, complicating their mission.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits are located beneath the structure and serve as the destination of the warriors and the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits refer to a location mentioned as burning, contributing to the urgency and danger of the situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits refer to a place of darkness and silence where John Carter may be imprisoned, symbolizing isolation and danger.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits refer to the underground locations in Helium where individuals are imprisoned, including Parthak and Hor Vastus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Pits refer to underground areas beneath various locations, significant for the hiding and movement of characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The pits are a location where Dejah Thoris was hidden by the narrator, indicating their importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The pits refer to a location where the narrator has been confined for three hundred days, indicating a place of captivity.&lt;SEP&gt;The pits refer to a location within the story, possibly a dangerous or significant area where the party was followed.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a43c41b4e0cc30def80a6039700a0bca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-38bc5039b174d7262ba50a2721ad87c3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ca06d2e5dc124b584060a61efedd5b65&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a9d992d50ff8d6d6a2e98bf2b0019642&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5a0ba9e0d4459c3f9f24f06c81a870d4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e6c74f70eb14cd86afae56d8763706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a88a169256ce5000de4b694a44baa4d8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d025c2fdd21d7a956f2705f12f6b69a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-410b3ad1e7dc881b5bb089cb806d3650&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba36c52515135b93e6cffab3871259ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5221b49e5ededb6977aa59a29710dee0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4ce58ae175da8c88d32eed4fe4dc295b</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PROJECT GUTENBERG-TM LICENSE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Project Gutenberg-tm License is a legal agreement outlining the terms of use for Project Gutenberg works, including refund policies and user obligations.&lt;SEP&gt;The Project Gutenberg-tm License outlines the terms and conditions for accessing, copying, and distributing Project Gutenberg-tm works. It specifies that works must be provided in their original format and prohibits charging fees unless certain conditions are met.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2a1c59e6c561451677f9e9d7b7379f99&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b83cdf44bb3173e3a4a5cffc5580d76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE TREE">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tree is a colossal structure with a large base, providing a potential hiding place for the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree is a large structure with an entrance at its foot and a stem that admits light, serving as a pathway for some creature.&lt;SEP&gt;The Tree is described as having its interior denuded of all possible means of ascent for a hundred feet, serving as a precaution against pursuit and attack.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b94bb2efdd49e207c66c3b4856b42dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c2ecd557268042ca8870f69d547b9b28&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-23432f8130c334a06bbe7cfa9957ad64</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BATTLE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Battle is the conflict occurring in the amphitheatre, involving the protagonist, apes, and other participants.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle involves a confrontation between the green warriors of Thark and the black warriors, initiated by Tars Tarkas.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle is a combat scenario where the Narrator and the Great Warrior confront the Green Martians, characterized by themes of courage and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle is a historic and ferocious conflict between the black men and the red men of Barsoom, determining the relative positions of these races.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle is a short and intense conflict between the fleet and the First Born, with an inevitable outcome due to the latter's carelessness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle is a significant conflict involving the Therns and the First Born, marked by strategic maneuvers and shifting alliances.&lt;SEP&gt;The Battle is the ongoing conflict involving multiple groups, including the green warriors and red men.&lt;SEP&gt;The battle is a chaotic and violent conflict between the black pirates of Barsoom and the therns, characterized by bloodlust and intense combat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91f54749765e904e286c340b8839282a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a6e3e6ec143a079a4d65379d29f1f2b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ea33f874d5e3c117742eceb580ddf105&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-acbe80414646c50a040ed7d24329e8df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-155a9ae6f189508e5e1a54b15041b72e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3076597b25663698d56a8907b5084439&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0700c43fe3a98521053c4539ff16e766&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165af99021c79dc0a6c523935a6d7b6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CORRIDOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Corridor is a dark passage leading towards the water of Omean, symbolizing a journey or transition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corridor is a geographical location where the protagonist encounters the Green Warriors and experiences a moment of unconsciousness.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corridor is a location that the narrator is forced to move through due to smoke, leading towards surging waters.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corridor is a passageway within the setting where the characters move, indicating a location relevant to the events unfolding.&lt;SEP&gt;The Corridor is a winding path through cliffs, leading to the surface from a lower level.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-6433c97b44b6a8dfc3da799e49e9017b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baab614831fc9ef34506ececd779922c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a3eae58bb1b31a20484bd7491decba&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-041ca20ade0f8736efede5678e381751&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06aa4fa22af57c68012d4559518b9942</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MARTIANS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Martians are a species from the ancient planet described in the text. They are generally poor climbers and prefer circuitous routes to climbing.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians are described as a higher race with a light reddish copper color, indicating their extraterrestrial origin and distinct physical attributes.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians are referenced as the discoverers of the ray of repulsion, a technology that enables navigation in the thin atmosphere of Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians refer to beings from Mars, indicating the setting of the event involving the attack on the Green Warriors.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians refer to the inhabitants of Mars, depicted as wearing silk capes and robes for protection from the cold.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians refer to the inhabitants of Mars, who wear leather harnesses, silk capes, and robes for protection against the cold, indicating a unique cultural attire.&lt;SEP&gt;Martians refer to the red and green Martians who are part of the hybrid population in the underground environment.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5e7c321f859a841ca0e55463f10ab39c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-940010d0056f8b8b43094bf27beeb53d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a066689ab8b7599bbec5a36e42af40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8b72dad86788b3397c84dad0327ae2f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e74a2f200cf0cf297917132a91806ef2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f6c0e8de7d0e31c3876fd0e24f7fc265&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bda2626ac1c54553dbd42e5bbc18073a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LESSER THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Lesser Therns are a group confronting the narrator and their companions, armed with rifles and initiating an attack.&lt;SEP&gt;Lesser Therns are individuals within the hierarchy of the Therns, responsible for carrying out various duties within the labyrinthine passages.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a8ef909cf6cea9004f4cf2ca39dc840</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE CLIFF">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Cliff is a geographical feature that the narrator approaches via a branch that leads to a narrow ledge and cave entrance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliff is a natural formation that becomes a breathtaking spectacle as sunlight reveals its rich veins and patches of precious metals and gemstones.&lt;SEP&gt;The Cliff is a stern and forbidding natural feature that runs across the head of the valley and towers about five thousand feet, with various colors including dusky red, green, and white quartz.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b94bb2efdd49e207c66c3b4856b42dee&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baf097d75b2e15406baf64c8aff8191f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c52ab8778aee4f0c53248a452d1143f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BEASTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Beasts are described as new foes that appear stealthily, causing rage and pain, and are believed to enter through concealed doorways rather than supernatural means.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5e7c321f859a841ca0e55463f10ab39c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SLAVES AND PRISONERS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Slaves and prisoners are individuals kept within the underworld to serve the Therns, never seeing the light of day.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEAR OF WATER">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fear of Water is a common attribute among Martians, indicating a cultural or inherent trait related to the Martian environment.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-89debdc6b3600e41312c14e89346cdc9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PLANT MEN">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Plant Men are a part of the black man's story, presumably creatures or beings related to the Barsoomian life.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are beings that appear towards the end of the text, potentially involved in the events described.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are beings that graze in circles around the sward, indicating they are herbivorous and part of the ecosystem.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are beings that inhabit the Valley Dor and prey on those who reach it, serving as guardians of the area.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are beings with limited intellectual capacity, characterized by their bisexual reproduction and instinct-driven behavior. They consume vegetation and animal blood and are fearless due to a lack of self-preservation instincts.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures believed by the therns to be the reincarnated forms of those who die before their allotted time, considered sacred within their belief system.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures described as mingling with the crowd and are familiar to the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures on Barsoom that evolved from the Tree of Life, capable of reproducing themselves like true plants.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures on Mars, described as having mighty tails and talons, feeding on the leaves and twigs of the trees.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures that grow from buds on fruit trees, remaining attached by stems from the tops of their heads.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are creatures that guard the Temple of Issus, playing a role in the capture of pilgrims.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are described as a herd-like group, aggressive in nature, and capable of causing significant harm with their tails.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are described as gruesome entities on Barsoom, known for their remarkable and effective attack methods, unfamiliar to the green warriors.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are described as hideous entities that the narrator would seek to exterminate.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are fierce and powerful creatures with great tails and razor-like talons, characterized by a green and sticky syrup that serves as their blood.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant Men are likely creatures or entities to whom the bodies are suggested to be thrown, indicating a potentially hostile or dangerous nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant men are beings held sacred by the therns, believed to be the form taken by those who die before their allotted lifespan is complete.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant men are described as a group surrounding green men and women, indicating their presence on Mars.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant men are described as agile and powerful adversaries with great tails, adding to the dangers faced by the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant men are described as creatures with a sucking embrace, posing a danger to individuals on Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Plant men are described as terrifying beings, contributing to a wave of snarling, snapping, screaming, and purring rage. Their horrid purring sound is noted as particularly hideous.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Men are a terrifying group involved in the attack, known for their indescribable purring.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Men are creatures that graze in circles, maintaining the grass like a well-kept lawn, suggesting a unique ecological behavior.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Men are described as creatures with cruel fangs, keen talons, and cold, sucking lips, indicating their predatory nature and the threat they pose.&lt;SEP&gt;The Plant Men are described as repulsive creatures that attack and drain the blood of their victims.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-68a066689ab8b7599bbec5a36e42af40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1bdc154afb97906f6c0d9be300b69e67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd39baf5700bc8ce341598b693d045d2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f214d1753c4d082073bfcf19b7280732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-04a161c56dbcea4ad6b336308a46ba34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-196465999312ca6d83f3f81d85944eb2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd96469a4962b32b193a14b2cae95e8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ff8f314a9085fecdc7786aee01217512&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf3b513cfbd001de6d80b59a09154df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c67b69095d5fb4eb3dbe97daae753305&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9502067fd0cb8fc03f8323bae38b4131&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a4fe2b5df5b2ed0fabd95ff2a65a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c865b073d24996a602f890b25765e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c1cfa5959049998648fc259707cbe29c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a6b409ade844047226580d5ff59b532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34611705ea5e04e7955dfd1248aed028&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17e1d860411b2b13228387bd01459577&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8d012f8241c4f059ba0b43b92cfad0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-207f5996f61ac31a201fa962ab092a5c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd597b4a21e1b8303b052d390d036cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1e735f04755bf97291c7e7ba215b41a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WARHOON">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Warhoon refers to a group or society, possibly a tribe or clan, of which Tars Tarkas is a chief, indicating a hierarchical structure.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoon refers to a group or tribe that the narrator and Tars Tarkas have fought against in the past.&lt;SEP&gt;Warhoon refers to a horde or group that the narrator and the young red man are fighting against, symbolizing a formidable adversary.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-2ad91ced17fd76f9b7fb848f010f12b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ed832c9005bcd6de678edadee8785ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-98242f5ba56160f01ff92873f61bfe8a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREAT WHITE APES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Great White Apes are brutal beasts that move among the crowd and are treated like pet dogs.&lt;SEP&gt;Great White Apes are creatures on Barsoom, mentioned by John Carter as part of his surroundings.&lt;SEP&gt;Great White Apes are creatures that guard the Temple of Issus and prey on individuals in the Valley Dor.&lt;SEP&gt;Great White Apes are described as horrible companions of the Plant Men that the narrator would seek to exterminate.&lt;SEP&gt;Great White Apes are fierce beasts that guard the Temple of Issus, involved in the capture of pilgrims.&lt;SEP&gt;Great White Apes refer to creatures that are part of a planned vindictive event, representing danger and destruction.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great White Apes are a fearsome and hostile group that participates in the attack, characterized by horrid growling.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great White Apes are creatures that arrive after the plant men have attacked, presumably to consume the remains left behind.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great White Apes are creatures that devour the remains of Tars Tarkas' former companions, indicating their ferocity and danger.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great White Apes are depicted as fearsome creatures with gleaming fangs, offering a swift end to suffering.&lt;SEP&gt;The Great White Apes are revered by the Therns, believed to be abodes of departed spirits, indicating their significant religious and cultural role.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f1de80424c9643aa139d17b7a371aed4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89113c4da6f11aefb8678fe8526edbf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-732154b0f5db90ca8982ebe025221f6c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd597b4a21e1b8303b052d390d036cf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1e735f04755bf97291c7e7ba215b41a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a6b409ade844047226580d5ff59b532&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-378619143a33f83383e8a418b9f9c820&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a7a4fe2b5df5b2ed0fabd95ff2a65a4e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4fd96469a4962b32b193a14b2cae95e8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE YOUNG RED MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Young Red Man is a character who actively participates in the battle, wielding a sword and fighting alongside the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;The Young Red Man is a participant in the battle, fighting alongside the narrator and exhibiting skill with a sword.&lt;SEP&gt;The young red man is a character fighting alongside the narrator with great ferocity and purpose.&lt;SEP&gt;The young red man is a participant in the battle, fighting alongside the narrator towards the throne.&lt;SEP&gt;The young red man is noted for his extraordinary speed, unmatched by any Martian the narrator has seen.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ed832c9005bcd6de678edadee8785ea2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-79bfaa16b39934f8800e01535bdd4dac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b513f985e87889370807eaddbed6a7b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8e73ce07604d42f9c6e9b21c0f5f3b1c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-96b7627f226c0cffd3d7951ab5750969</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MY PRINCESS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">My princess is a character who shows tender-hearted regret for the necessity of conflict, indicating a compassionate nature.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-9e0091b7eec20ccaadf8476aa83db095</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE GATE">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Gate is a physical location in the arena, where the monstrous white apes are released.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e678ea71ac9a1264539f43637bf2a809</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Man is the narrator who considers revealing himself to the herd but is deterred by the wail from the bluffs, indicating his cautious nature.&lt;SEP&gt;The man is a bound individual on the deck, described as handsome and intelligent, and possibly an enemy or prisoner.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b274f937a3dc2f41dc46c714db0e1c59&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0091b7eec20ccaadf8476aa83db095</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MONSTROUS WHITE APES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Monstrous White Apes are creatures that are released into the arena to attack the frightened maidens, symbolizing terror and frenzy.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e678ea71ac9a1264539f43637bf2a809</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREEN HORDES">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Green Hordes are groups that occupy the deserted cities, specifically around the central plaza, and typically travel across the dead sea bottoms.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Hordes are a group of tribesmen led by the Great Thark, who overran Zodanga.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5abead0021cc11fa9cdb0e164538e6f3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25b54582b37bd689e9944f79dbc5d866</data>
    </node>
