    </node>
    <node id="ROYALTY PAYMENTS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Royalty Payments refer to the financial payments that are required to be made to the Project Gutenberg Literary Archive Foundation, as specified in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b83cdf44bb3173e3a4a5cffc5580d76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORS KAJAK">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mors Kajak is a character associated with Helium and mentioned alongside Mors and Dejah Thoris, indicating involvement in important events or decisions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is a person mentioned in relation to not returning to Helium as part of the conditions for reprieve.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is a royal figure whose return to Helium is awaited, affecting political decisions and actions.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is another individual whose safety is a concern, suggesting a significant role or connection to leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is mentioned alongside Mors as a character who is no longer present and will not return.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is mentioned alongside Tardos Mors, suggesting a connection to leadership in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is the father of the Princess who leads an expedition in search of her lost son, showing determination and leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak is the son of Tardos Mors, whose return is also awaited for resolving the dispute, signifying his potential role in leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors Kajak, also known as Tardos Mors, is a central figure with authority in Helium, commanding respect and loyalty from others.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-203aa795181a9eb1397b2f84beb7f517&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-888217eade35a66c1dd712e0e3da230d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21b99744d09aa8c4015948f8dc5e7f67&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5611c5f62cf8eed6262c37dc2e3a029&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c623b43139978dba5887d5c135e5174&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2689f06a45abd5998519fb85220b9bd0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-43237e8924c3e87e804cbb4a0e2df875&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9cd72b265d18f8c068fcc7cb760ce09f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE STRANGE SHAFT">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Strange Shaft is a vertical passage with a ladder of horizontal bars, explored by the narrator and leading to a large flat limb.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c2ecd557268042ca8870f69d547b9b28</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SELF-PRESERVATION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Self-preservation is the instinct to protect oneself from harm or death, even in dire situations.&lt;SEP&gt;Self-preservation is the instinctive drive to survive, even in the face of inevitable death.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-975c90c687850d2c03b5c57fe3acbb46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-17a3eae58bb1b31a20484bd7491decba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TORITH">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Torith is a character who emerges from his office to address a commotion involving armed guards and a message addressed to him.&lt;SEP&gt;Torith is a character who questions others about the rising of slaves and appears to be in a position of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Torith is an individual who emerges from his office to investigate a commotion and is involved in verifying the authenticity of a message.&lt;SEP&gt;Torith is the officer in charge of the guards patrolling the island about the pool, responsible for maintaining security.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ad51ac4fc1824f7d9fecff7b3b450743&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da4a2f8784f599bc94defce14beef7f0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f61dacafb7778f4b0ffdd11993b73432&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f11bf730f5cfa3d77405e7d734e74488</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MY MEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">My Men are individuals accompanying the narrator, who have taken the last torch, leaving the narrator in darkness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-17a3eae58bb1b31a20484bd7491decba</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DATOR YERSTED">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dator Yersted is a person whose whereabouts are questioned, implying involvement in a significant event or operation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f11bf730f5cfa3d77405e7d734e74488</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOLY THERN">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Holy Thern is a character standing on a balcony, wearing a scarlet robe of office, and anticipating the cold that comes with darkness.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern is a high-ranking position within the infernal cult, indicating religious and possibly political authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern is a religious group or organization referenced in the text, possibly associated with spiritual or ritualistic practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern is a title associated with a religious or spiritual order on Barsoom, marked by distinctive golden hair and jeweled circlet.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern is a title indicating a religious or spiritual leader among the Therns, associated with significant status and authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern is an organization or religious group mentioned in relation to beliefs about life and death.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern refers to a religious figure or priest within an infernal cult, whose physical appearance resembles that of the Prince.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern refers to a religious or spiritual leader, symbolized by a priceless diadem.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern refers to a religious or spiritual role, possibly of significant authority or reverence in the context of the story.&lt;SEP&gt;Holy Thern refers to the role or position within the thern society, characterized by specific apparel and cultural significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Thern is a character with long flowing, yellow locks, whose presence offers a potential means of escape and hope in a dire situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Thern is a figure of authority, likely holding a religious or ceremonial role on Mars, distinguished by a scarlet robe of office and a duty to watch over his surroundings.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Thern is a religious figure who is responsible for watching over the river and has the authority to claim individuals as their own.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Thern is a role associated with individuals who watch over the valley and claim victims as their own, often using foul means if necessary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Holy Thern is a secretive organization with a wide reach across Barsoom, known for its hidden temples and influence over various communities.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-f651ea5c605f9f3d54a95f1c90c89a0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-21ff627f7e5d376dfb488b33baf21c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-808ddbe6ccdd93bf254656679b522a03&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-682cfb3dc6d02c7c2e7994c7caa7c551&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-88f65b8a5a48d5153729a3de1ec4ca4f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8444ad2509b1d2679504e820feabb704&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e51e1d8477880f7c52ccf46556e3c955&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a0ff17997572867abd4f76f4d654adda&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0f9da712a7c655f8901bdc9f3fb4a0cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3c1c1de3605517ea048c08675a03df17&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91388cfb9b19f81432eafb4bca1d653b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cebd2d10250f3f1708ab616c25dcf6b8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c818231005769615743d6e44cf0d9b33&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a</data>
    </node>
