    <node id="MIGHTY FIGHTER">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mighty Fighter is a strong combatant who was overwhelmed by the Green Warriors and was last seen being taken to a deserted city, wounded and bleeding.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-99a999462c51c933f54b7da03b7f1fa7</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PERILOUS TRIP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Perilous Trip is the dangerous journey that the narrator and his companions are about to undertake.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0a705f5ca3ac7586de6280ecff5dabe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE EXPEDITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Expedition is a doomed mission involving a fleet that is being pursued by hostile forces, highlighting its perilous nature.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expedition is an event aimed at rescuing Dejah Thoris, showing its significance to the narrator and Carthoris.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expedition refers to a group of individuals attempting to navigate through a passage, facing the danger of rising waters from Omean.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-22eaf50af48826cca311a84b8da73b0e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5ec04b19f44e50aea83ee65f6472738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c3a03d32b4f129d8e3a6da9b664e8bae</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWORDS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Swords represent a necessary tool for protection and survival on the perilous trip.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0a705f5ca3ac7586de6280ecff5dabe</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHINA">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">China refers to fine, clear, and white porcelain, used to describe the appearance of some trees in the forest.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f9949a0bb82e20d49be0609ca8878e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PERSON OR ENTITY">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The person or entity refers to the individual or organization responsible for providing the defective work and handling its replacement or refund.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE VALLEY DOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Valley Dor is a geographical area that is part of the religious doctrine of the Therns, influencing pilgrimages and religious beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley Dor is a geographical location mentioned as a place from which the protagonist and his companion are attempting to escape, associated with a certain death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Valley Dor is perceived by the outer world as a place similar to the Temple of Issus, representing an ultimate haven of peace and happiness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-085e618431c5f450074853c08198b71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b70f3d124e6dbcf1fbf9180293d455f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REPLACEMENT COPY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">A replacement copy is an alternative copy of the work provided in lieu of a refund when the original work is defective.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="TEN YEARS' RESIDENCE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ten Years' Residence refers to the narrator's long-term stay on Mars, during which they have explored only a small area.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a412d7e62e543df749e5efad982ac680</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REFUND">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">A refund is the return of money paid for the defective work, offered if the replacement copy is also defective.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREEN WARRIORS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">Green Warriors are a group of fearsome fighters participating in the battle, led by the Thark.&lt;SEP&gt;Green Warriors are a group of fighters led by Tars Tarkas, stationed at Thark with a large number of troopships.&lt;SEP&gt;Green Warriors are a group of individuals seen carrying a torch and moving through the corridors, indicating they might be a military or exploratory group.&lt;SEP&gt;Green Warriors are a group on Barsoom skilled in science and combat, but unprepared for the unique attacks of the plant men.&lt;SEP&gt;Green Warriors are mentioned as a multitude from another horde who overwhelmed Tars Tarkas, suggesting a group involved in conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Green Warriors are the victims of an attack by a frightful herd, experiencing terror and confusion.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Warriors are a group of fighters from a different horde who overwhelmed a mighty fighter and took him to a deserted city.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green Warriors are a group of four individuals, presumably part of a larger organization, who are encountered in a corridor and carry a torch.&lt;SEP&gt;The Green warriors are a group of fighters astride mighty thoats, forcing the Black warriors back in the battle.&lt;SEP&gt;The green warriors are a large force attacking the temples of the therns and engaging in combat with their soldiery.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-eaf7dc1903c32a72610791b1667df6b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-68a066689ab8b7599bbec5a36e42af40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d37d0a9a9b921ab61d9d45cce2805441&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f214d1753c4d082073bfcf19b7280732&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-72812560e1ff7542f6388b33de0b70d3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1e2bc04d789e0440373c080f9bdaedb9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-baab614831fc9ef34506ececd779922c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-99a999462c51c933f54b7da03b7f1fa7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1403de9be5a8cd3ec91ce41c26a8925d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-165af99021c79dc0a6c523935a6d7b6c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELECTRONIC COPY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">An electronic copy is a digital version of the work provided to the recipient, with the possibility of receiving a second electronic copy if the first is defective.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EBONY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ebony refers to a type of wood that is black in color, used to describe the wood of some trees in the forest.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e1f9949a0bb82e20d49be0609ca8878e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="WARRANTIES">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Warranties refer to assurances provided regarding the quality and functionality of the work, which are disclaimed in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FLOOD">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The flood is a critical event characterized by rising water levels, posing a threat to the men and necessitating a strategic retreat to safety.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96546a836d85558a443f79415ac1818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STATES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">States refer to regions or jurisdictions within a country that may have specific laws regarding disclaimers and warranties.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-206ecd0ddef85356e60a60f9e88ce85d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ARMED SAILORS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Armed Sailors are part of the crew surrounding the protagonists, indicating their role in maintaining security and order.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0461306cf04c98666dc40fbe77653113</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LIFE AND DEATH">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Life and Death are presented as fundamental concepts, evoking a sense of existential power and the inevitability faced by mortal beings.&lt;SEP&gt;Life and Death refers to the existential concepts that Matai Shang is associated with as the Master on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-49f2816b2fa66aa235a34337ce63c50a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0dfc9370da9b7473c6ffb2b187d36968</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EXPEDITION">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Expedition refers to the missions led by Mors Kajak and Tardos Mors to search for the Princess's lost son in the northern hemisphere of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expedition initially intended to rescue Dejah Thoris, but now seeks revenge and aims to reveal the truth to the people of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expedition is a mission undertaken by the narrator and a hundred fighting-men to rescue Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;The Expedition refers to a planned military endeavor involving warriors from various communities and hordes, organized by the Thark under the leadership of the Jeddak.&lt;SEP&gt;The expedition is a group of people undertaking a journey or task, currently facing a life-threatening situation.&lt;SEP&gt;The expedition is a journey undertaken by the narrator, which has faced a series of misfortunes and disasters.&lt;SEP&gt;The expedition is a planned mission aimed at preserving Dejah Thoris and countering the therns' threat.&lt;SEP&gt;The expedition is an effort to teach the people of Barsoom about the cruel deception they have suffered and to open the Valley Dor to the red men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-495092be397283589740233519b5dcac&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80db35b61d87fdd761868678f27e8d38&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bea6eb93c07d5de217e100ae883e0c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5b919dd2dc7793aafb7f18ad97d8cb61&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-215cc9a11b792d42bd9db23d7399186c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef83a1bb59d0a6160845638665b9ef6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-906dc67c04c5c3c54cafff91f6bf6a60</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ETERNAL OBLIVION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Eternal Oblivion refers to the concept of a final state of non-existence, portrayed as a desirable eternity for mortal man.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0dfc9370da9b7473c6ffb2b187d36968</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GREAT RIVER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Great River is a significant geographical feature in the narrative, characterized by its grandeur and inspiring presence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-be70a23f43613d282ab01428d5443025</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUBTERRANEAN VAULT">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The subterranean vault is a small underground chamber where the submarine is docked, characterized by rock-lined walls and a low roof.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cd2dc607190379cdec50d1c32f9a6cdc</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE OFFICER">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Officer is a character responsible for escorting individuals to the audience chamber of Issus, indicating a role in the ceremonial process.&lt;SEP&gt;The Officer is a character who follows Issus' commands, demonstrating authority and duty in enforcing the deity's orders.&lt;SEP&gt;The officer is a person in a position of authority within the military or organized group, responsible for ensuring the execution of commands and the safety of the men.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96546a836d85558a443f79415ac1818&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc67bf329b29478328d22700eef5657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1fb7fa0605b3b0af3ae10bd81ff6ec0f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE DROP">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Drop is an event involving a descent of about ten feet into a dark pit, requiring careful maneuvering.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cb36162aba338e66b3b93a517a51f9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE FIRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fire is a catastrophic event occurring at the Temple of the Sun, causing chaos and prompting evacuation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fire is a conflagration described as a seething hell of chemicals, posing a significant danger and obstacle to the protagonist.&lt;SEP&gt;The Fire is a dangerous event involving flames and smoke, causing chaos and requiring evacuation to avoid harm.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-348a17955f915d0d8c7721c28a9da5c1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5c800b530f2a9aa4ac941241f419bdaf&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b86cc68abfabb7895f5f31421d51d427</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PANIC">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Panic is a feeling experienced when facing the unknown depths during the descent into darkness.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4cb36162aba338e66b3b93a517a51f9f</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DJOR KANTOS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Djor Kantos is a red man and padwar of the fifth utan who warns others about the temple being on fire.&lt;SEP&gt;Djor Kantos is the son of Kantos Kan and a padwar of the fifth utan, who joins efforts to save soldiers during a crisis.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-cead3080c3879bc999f5b5b6ec863019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b1cd3d37a3444603507b9a474cfa473</data>
    </node>
    <node id="LEADERSHIP SELECTION">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Leadership Selection refers to the process by which the people of Helium will choose their next Jeddak, emphasizing democratic principles.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-203aa795181a9eb1397b2f84beb7f517</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE RIVER">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The River appears to break from the base of the cliffs, contributing to the natural features of the valley.&lt;SEP&gt;The River is a geographical feature on Mars, originating from the base of the cliffs and serving as a pathway for the herd.&lt;SEP&gt;The River is broad, placid, and majestic, flowing between scarlet banks into the sea, adding to the natural grandeur of the scene.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91e86645b0989df5782a6688160c1d8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c52ab8778aee4f0c53248a452d1143f8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f09a293ca63ae749e20ee10ccd0b69b9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FOUNDATION">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Foundation is involved in the management and oversight of Project Gutenberg-tm, ensuring compliance with legal agreements and liability protection.&lt;SEP&gt;The Foundation is involved in the production, promotion, and distribution of Project Gutenberg-tm electronic works, and holds trademark rights.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-796965d281b54a5d433ef73d41710652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a4f9feaf0a05843a17bccdae6cc3fa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIRE">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fire is an event causing chaos and danger in the pits, requiring evacuation and posing a significant threat to those involved.&lt;SEP&gt;Fire is an event taking place at the Temple of Issus, causing smoke and a tumult among different groups of men.&lt;SEP&gt;The cry of "fire" indicates a potential danger or threat faced by the group during their escape.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a8c9fa2f165189b2177ca5c0e4a0b033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a5068f52c923549934726130060ee89e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="STATE LAW">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">State Law refers to the legal framework applicable to the agreement, influencing the interpretation of disclaimers and limitations.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a4f9feaf0a05843a17bccdae6cc3fa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE LAST TWENTY-FIVE UTANS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The last twenty-five utans refer to a group of units or divisions of men within a larger force, potentially indicating a military structure or organization.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e96546a836d85558a443f79415ac1818</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGENT">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">An Agent is a representative or individual acting on behalf of the Foundation in the distribution of Project Gutenberg-tm electronic works.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a4f9feaf0a05843a17bccdae6cc3fa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DOR">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Dor is a concept referring to a false hereafter that John Carter aims to save people from.&lt;SEP&gt;Dor is a geographical location where the fleet remains, and its proximity is linked to the conflict with the Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;Dor is a location associated with religious beliefs and considered a place of sacrilege by some officers on the _Xavarian_.&lt;SEP&gt;Dor is a location from which Tars Tarkas has returned and is assessing his people's sentiments about this return.&lt;SEP&gt;Dor is described as both a beautiful and hideous valley on Barsoom, indicating its complex nature.&lt;SEP&gt;Dor is referred to as a false hereafter, implying it is a deceptive or misleading concept of an afterlife.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-71af797a3da71bfc14e67053629a5b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-81753f746888e783bd4e7e6d01676e26&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebad39afb87513bd9b8bcf938fb8fd24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fd1b65dcd4e5b65f014a78dfad395fdb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a221bcb1631084ef422a98443917c0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="EMPLOYEE">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">An Employee is a person working for the Foundation and involved in the distribution of Project Gutenberg-tm electronic works.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8a4f9feaf0a05843a17bccdae6cc3fa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="PADWAR">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A padwar is a rank or role, possibly akin to a military or leadership position, who assists in guiding the group through the passage.&lt;SEP&gt;Padwar is a rank or role held by Djor Kantos within the fifth utan, likely a military or leadership position.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5068f52c923549934726130060ee89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cead3080c3879bc999f5b5b6ec863019</data>
    </node>
    <node id="VOLUNTEERS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">Volunteers are individuals who assist in the production, promotion, and distribution of Project Gutenberg-tm electronic works.&lt;SEP&gt;Volunteers are individuals who contribute their efforts to support Project Gutenberg-tm, playing a crucial role in achieving its goals.&lt;SEP&gt;Volunteers play a crucial role in the production, promotion, and distribution of Project Gutenberg-tm electronic works, contributing to its mission of free access.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-7b87840a620a3fd3be02b4f0d4ec3dd7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-796965d281b54a5d433ef73d41710652&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8a4f9feaf0a05843a17bccdae6cc3fa0</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kan is a character involved in leading a group through a challenging situation, likely displaying leadership and bravery.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5068f52c923549934726130060ee89e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ELEVATOR CARS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Elevator Cars are transportation devices operated by magnets, used to move people or objects through shafts on Barsoom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c06efaf0405e791fc4f6f9af3b7624b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="OATH OF FEALTY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Oath of Fealty is a pledge of complete loyalty and obedience, signifying that one's life, body, and soul are dedicated to serving and protecting a leader.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1a5c94f3b5e290f5c1cd4a83a590d5a6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MAGNETS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Magnets are used in Barsoom to operate elevator cars by regulating the magnetic volume to control speed.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c06efaf0405e791fc4f6f9af3b7624b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHAINED PRISONERS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The chained prisoners are individuals who are observing the combat, indicating their captive status and lack of freedom.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-4d326ad7454f10313352505bb827bb89</data>
    </node>
    <node id="ISS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Iss appears to be a concept or belief related to the lifecycle or destiny of certain beings, possibly linked to their cultural or spiritual practices.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is a cold sea mentioned in the text, connected to the Temple of Issus and guarded by plant men and great white apes.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is a location associated with the voluntary pilgrimage of Barsoomians, where they are believed to go at or before their thousandth year.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is a river emerging from the base of cliffs, playing a significant role in the scene described.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is a river on Mars, emerging from the base of cliffs and observed to carry a canoe laden with lost souls.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is a subterranean passage that flows for a thousand miles before entering Valley Dor, possibly playing a role in the journey of victims.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is described as an icy bosom, potentially a location associated with the voluntary pilgrimage of Dejah Thoris and her servants.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is described as the mighty messenger of Issus, who carries individuals to the Valley Dor at their own behest.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss is referred to as the River of Mystery, suggesting a significant and mystical location.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss refers to a doctrine or religious belief held by some officers on the _Xavarian_, influencing their attitudes and behaviors.&lt;SEP&gt;Iss refers to a place or entity associated with the Valley Dor and the Land of the First Born, from which John Carter has returned.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ebad39afb87513bd9b8bcf938fb8fd24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bc1af42c648e773e967ffc620ac03772&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-77544c11bdeae685d5cc57de932d4153&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9582d5fbcd0fec18f551d2401616b736&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c60a9da7e3358ae80aa0dde32a451ee8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25f6195017cf2ed0308d928aeccda715&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4b5bd91746b54706f1cdd87796a2646a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91388cfb9b19f81432eafb4bca1d653b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5bf3b513cfbd001de6d80b59a09154df&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bc8ba319c10b95a0296d782317a73a9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GRAVITY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Gravity on Barsoom is described as being weak, affecting the movement and speed of elevator cars.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c06efaf0405e791fc4f6f9af3b7624b3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THARKS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Tharks are a group or organization led by the Jeddak, indicating a structured community or tribe.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b70f3d124e6dbcf1fbf9180293d455f8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THABIS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Thabis is described as someone who selects individuals for Issus, suggesting a role as a servant or assistant in carrying out Issus's commands.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-5075c6c6334565039e84371f24903659</data>
    </node>
    <node id="GUR TUS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Gur Tus is a valorous soldier and the dwar of the 10th utan, who assists in maintaining order and rescuing soldiers during a dangerous situation.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-1b1cd3d37a3444603507b9a474cfa473</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MORS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Mors is a character who, along with Mors Kajak and Dejah Thoris, will not return to Helium, indicating their absence is significant to the political dynamics of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Mors is mentioned as a character who, along with Mors Kajak, is no longer present and will not return.</data>
