    </node>
    <node id="BLACK MEN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Black Men are described as the race of true and immortal humans on Barsoom, representing purity and superiority in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Black Men are participants in the rites of Issus, judged by their ability to survive combat, which is tied to their loyalty and purity.&lt;SEP&gt;Black Men are participants in the rites of Issus, where they attempt to wash sins from their souls through bloodshed, indicating their role in the ritual.&lt;SEP&gt;Black Men are portrayed as a dominant group whose sufferance allows the therns to live, indicating a power dynamic.&lt;SEP&gt;The black men are described as antagonists in the gardens of the cruel therns, posing a mortal threat to the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bcc97b8466964e5aa69bc08566713a40&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-64474596228fc708f1e3fea89d9ec14b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-31d9d856d8607b6185783a1c035ed7f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe8483a1bbc19b7757cade3ab93f3d9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b852a9d3367f81e14d5fe18d854c6494</data>
    </node>
