    </node>
    <node id="THE GIRL">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Girl is a character who communicates silently and offers aid, indicating a complex and potentially strategic role in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who led her savage companions through a panel, indicating her role in guiding or influencing their actions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who possesses a commanding presence, able to control banths and is kept by Sator Throg to train and handle these creatures.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who reflects on the importance of truth and expresses a willingness to sacrifice herself to save others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who swoons but later regains consciousness and engages in a conversation about mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is a character who warns about the dangers within the territory of the therns and assists in the escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is depicted as a character who is involved in a combat situation, using a revolver to assist in a fight against attackers.&lt;SEP&gt;The Girl is linked to the narrator by a rope, indicating a shared captivity or predicament.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a captive who is bound alongside the narrator and draws attention due to her beauty, eliciting comments from the captors.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a character who actively participates in a combat situation, using a firearm to aid the narrator in reducing the number of opponents.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a character who appears to have a different perspective on conflict, possibly contemplating the necessity of dispatching an enemy.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a character who interacts with the narrator, providing information about the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The girl is a stealthy and strategic individual who is attempting to flank the attackers to assist in reducing their numbers during a battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-b90195666d478ccee815cdee51c1fb10&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dda2ba13c7497352bcb94f3e493f8def&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0070ef1f1167082da565bcee6e79fbca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9e0091b7eec20ccaadf8476aa83db095&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d68959082a690bb8c58c37751492f86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c865b073d24996a602f890b25765e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d4a0eb7e5b53ec81773729f65fca8a27&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8065467da8bd3c84208f3c43a5f1bf76&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-be809390aed5cbcb14d9c180568ae323&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ae1ccf749f2b30c16f4cc985a93939e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d43a98e16a4c8e37920ba8bd953e50b7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8ae29e0662e7c7df5e1c335a0ba53d41</data>
    </node>
    <node id="RECEDING SEAS">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Receding Seas is an event that led to the abandonment of fortified cities and caused races to adopt a nomadic lifestyle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e7f78c9ccb74063a56ce56a2e1d5bafe</data>
