    <node id="THE _XAVARIAN_">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The _Xavarian_ is a battleship involved in rescuing a party and transporting them.&lt;SEP&gt;The _Xavarian_ is a craft or vessel that serves as a location where the rescued party is brought and where Kantos Kan is present.&lt;SEP&gt;The _Xavarian_ is a location associated with Hor Vastus' fliers and the arrival of a message from Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;The _Xavarian_ is a vessel involved in the journey to Helium, serving as a central setting for the events described.&lt;SEP&gt;The _Xavarian_ is a vessel with officers divided into factions based on their beliefs and loyalties.&lt;SEP&gt;The _Xavarian_ is likely a ship or vessel that holds significance for the characters, especially the Prince of Helium.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e029e53f82ffdbeba2500285e859f464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0ba6fe6e7d6d25df18260ffbf7692d4a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d439770c0f7294bb2e112da933aca210&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ebad39afb87513bd9b8bcf938fb8fd24&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8656b4b6a355643abf13c112ecbaf810</data>
    </node>
    <node id="XODAR">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Xodar is a multifaceted character within the narrative set on Mars, embodying roles ranging from leadership to servitude. As a member of the First Born of Barsoom, Xodar holds the title of Dator, which is equivalent to a prince, indicating his authoritative position and commanding presence. Despite this, he experiences a fall from grace, becoming a degraded slave due to disgrace, yet he maintains composure and stoicism in the face of adversity.

Xodar is deeply involved in numerous aspects of the unfolding story, from planning and executing escape plans to engaging in tense situations. He demonstrates resourcefulness, agility, and strategic thinking, notably during prison escape attempts and navigating vessels with quick reflexes and control. His leadership and loyalty are evident as he volunteers to join stealth missions and aligns with other characters, such as Carthoris and Tars Tarkas, to face threats like the advancing Warhoons.

In his interactions, Xodar shows respect and familiarity with figures such as John Carter, acknowledging their accomplishments and strength. He advises on strategy during escapes, suggesting high ascents to avoid enemy fire, and collaborates with the narrator to plan escapes, utilizing his knowledge of the south polar regions and guard duties. His involvement in conversations reveals skepticism, surprise, and inner conflict, particularly regarding the commands of Issus and the divine beliefs associated with her.

Despite being faithful to Issus, Xodar confronts the idea that she may not be as divine as believed, leading to contemplation and despair. He is a complex character, experiencing degradation and mistreatment, yet he is also depicted as a fiend for subtle craftiness, devising plans to extract information and refit battleships for navigation in Omean.

Xodar's interactions with others range from expressing gratitude and willingness to aid the narrator to challenging beliefs and teaching about the Temple of Issus. He provides valuable insights into the geography and infrastructure of Barsoom, including the River Iss, the navy of the First Born, and the sea beneath Barsoom. His technical proficiency is evident as he works alongside Carthoris to repair the vessel and remodel battleships for future missions.

Overall, Xodar is a character marked by complexity and depth, navigating a world of danger and intrigue with a blend of leadership, resourcefulness, and contemplation, contributing significantly to the narrative's progression and the safety of key characters like Dejah Thoris and Thuvia.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a0a705f5ca3ac7586de6280ecff5dabe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f0c492fec7174d93acfd367ca61db0d1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f3a6677c685c5edfb6994caf71b433ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c9470c83ddd8e7e1b1a012ece31cb589&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-80b3d1ec56db5ef8672ef886c7145598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6fb847572b8f4cd9bcb5e21934d38337&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8888a7351a2f9284fdc4f2cc1a25d395&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-921a093a9894a3c734cae70309767381&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151c6925632d42abc6c6f08a41de7eb8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a1fd4c188807a94298bfeb6bdc0fd055&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2cc67bf329b29478328d22700eef5657&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c780b2690f7d5702006bb65b02e4811b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9269232f99d91f950b2e2e1efcd036d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-553265af22155e878e0c762c2ea5c1fb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a6311329816ffebf6e549cded38827ab&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cf32459bda0d3c3a0f4656dfded76108&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cd2dc607190379cdec50d1c32f9a6cdc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd6426cafa5e0838a5fd65d263895518&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9202971a6c9b597c032f8fde2a01d35a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-828c13a969a4680fba443b671dee21b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65cbfd544a7666d71957424825d22b07&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d7ae9b01eadc7f407e1d5bca34640588&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac21fdcaba1072d7aae816bc5a5b7e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fcf47f64aae75975f5f02f3ddf9a1b21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d378cc6dcca5a19ea2b10af50a96bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-457f113a7e0cee5a28f3a33cab3fe887&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-452d661ef0dc01933f992e1f4cbb0181&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5fb37188960dc17c3a250c133cc1d830&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e7b33af041481ac0fa8f2a1a4f22e9d0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d5c0c969b2aa049ae080527d08909391&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-593ac9d49ec07dc6c02dbd8f0ccab1a8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9f4ad2a6244781aedab72c9923705b95&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-25b54582b37bd689e9944f79dbc5d866&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e6b2df8db3209d64539ab2e7119498&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9dd21470cebb00b207669a678b79f42d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-885bf7dbe26f685a917110c8c81cfc01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a251acf5b0228bf1f96d5672fe3db216&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cc097954bb2f6ee125ba13ade198a9f1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-93e4b09129997fb7a91db72baa774cfd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-44530add08352