hunk-6c1de3b9f0e7f1ea967106856be68ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e03da8ccb26edbf8fde791db77d403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ba36c52515135b93e6cffab3871259ca&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3e58012e53ec92e40f7c47c8c3805771&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b836fd8868218c6690ae5715294518c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7a74e531db6278d5b04b13ea92e66032</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MYSTIC JEWEL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Mystic Jewel is a significant object that seems to provide relief and has mystical properties, central to the narrative.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-8065467da8bd3c84208f3c43a5f1bf76</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUNSET">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Sunset marks the time by which the fleet has successfully gathered away from the ongoing battle.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-29e1a71b135e5ee730cfeb499b981e36</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE PRINCE">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">The Prince is a character who is mentioned as leading the men of Helium, indicating a leadership role in the conflict or rescue.&lt;SEP&gt;The Prince is the main character who is married to the Princess of Helium. He tries to gently but firmly disengage from Thuvia's affections, acknowledging the danger and hardships she has been through.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-fe5cf45af5e3799da900db83fcb3ff56&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fbe2b8a94bb223962e9bd344d6ec1889</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE MIRROR">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Mirror is a small reflective object worn by Martians, used in this context to observe unexpected movements.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mirror is used by the narrator to watch the section of the wall, serving as a tool for observation and strategy.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bda2626ac1c54553dbd42e5bbc18073a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-10fb47e6e94d1a79b8238f79b15d45c8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="CHAMBER OF HORRORS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Chamber of Horrors is a grim and perilous location where dangerous encounters take place, including the fight involving Tars Tarkas.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63a07d95b31bd7f0773a4e70c95dad9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE WALL">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Wall refers to a section of the structure that can pivot and move, indicating a hidden or mechanical aspect of the environment.&lt;SEP&gt;The Wall refers to a section of the structure that is capable of rotating on pivots, revealing hidden elements behind it.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-bda2626ac1c54553dbd42e5bbc18073a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6885d08319ecf502c70443aab4891a50</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SWORD">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">The Sword symbolizes the protagonist's means of defense and potential escape from the threatening creatures, representing strength and survival.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sword symbolizes the responsibility and duty to uphold truth and justice, given by John Carter to Hor Vastus.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32838d1c338418b6ba3de4f8e52015a3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f54e6e134d03ff91769cb5e4edbaeba6</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE THERNS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Therns are a group engaged in a fierce conflict with powerful creatures, distracted by their assailants, creating an opportunity for escape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group or society that has domains within the Otz Valley, from which the narrator recently escaped.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group or society that is associated with a territory containing dangerous places and ancient superstitions.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group that monitors others on Barsoom, expecting individuals to take a pilgrimage, and are associated with the consumption of human flesh.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group that uses a race for their own purposes, collecting tolls in arms, ammunition, and prisoners, and living under the threat of black battleships.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group who fear the banths and rarely venture below ground due to their presence.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group whose fire has ceased, indicating they were involved in a conflict or battle but have chosen to disengage.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a group whose members were stripped of their weapons by the narrator and Tars Tarkas. They are associated with ancient superstition.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a race characterized as mental giants and moral pygmies, who revere the Temple of Issus as their ultimate sanctuary after life.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are a religious group with temples across the civilized world, collecting wealth and labor through the doctrine of the Mysterious River Iss, the Valley Dor, and the Lost Sea of Korus.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are an organization with an impregnable fortress on Barsoom, fearing the black pirates of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are individuals or a group whose land is being approached, suggesting they are the opposing force or target in this operation.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are responsible for the fatal marksmanship that resulted in the death of companions, hindering the group's chance of gaining freedom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Therns are the defending forces engaged in combat against the Black Pirates of Barsoom, utilizing temple guards and soldiery.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group characterized by a physical structure similar to the red men and the narrator, but they are distinct in their cultural or social identity.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group mentioned in the text, likely with religious or cultural significance, whose beliefs are in conflict with the narrator's experiences.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group of beings in Barsoom, revered by the people and believed to have a lifespan of one thousand years.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group of people whose land the protagonist and their team are approaching.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group or organization on Barsoom, associated with a storehouse where the narrator once slept.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group whose temples and soldiers are under attack by green warriors and battleships.&lt;SEP&gt;The therns are a group with deadly marksmanship, posing a significant threat to the protagonists and capable of demanding scrutiny from higher powers.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-ebc4c43245688964f6b9cde60fa1b9a0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1c0106b92cb6f20d3c3acb7b5cdb78cd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dc4a67f1f5f95ea1ba51770bfae3761&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-71af797a3da71bfc14e67053629a5b6d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f4953262a187c7f088ce754bc536a798&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-65e8b4e5cb9fe7b6998ce2d6e059f797&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-108a9127dde1b2e1f9fc62c0742c62de&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6716a4317005ca2adb5fd451d6df6352&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eaf7dc1903c32a72610791b1667df6b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e9df9ebc1b25dd4de139a9defc734208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e32f64cbf961c7ebe05d9308a82211c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9c865b073d24996a602f890b25765e4d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-085e618431c5f450074853c08198b71e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-90f4870643c7b80fc79a5ab9ab123487&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3369e6763ac9a08c733a8e0483dbb2cb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-33f4de7021681b138c6572d77b66c4fe&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83143cdd9a1d0eb60c6e662a220df1b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-920a46aa7ab7990a8fd14507517ad0c8&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c768a4ea224d8da779e3818ab95c45f2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cb13d519a0b4f895198cfc2c98df8b98&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-16b92520aa86cd4fddd2580eca2b853a</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FIFTH UTAN">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">The Fifth Utan appears to be a military or organized group involved in the evacuation through the corridor.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5068f52c923549934726130060ee89e</data>
    </node>
    <node id="BLACK BATTLESHIPS">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Black Battleships refer to the formidable forces that circled the Mountains of Otz, attacking the Therns and demonstrating their power and influence.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9df9ebc1b25dd4de139a9defc734208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="FEALTY">
      <data key="d0">CONCEPT</data>
      <data key="d1">Fealty refers to the oath of loyalty and allegiance paid to a leader, demonstrating a strong bond and commitment.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-32838d1c338418b6ba3de4f8e52015a3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="MOUNTAINS OF OTZ">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Mountains of Otz are geographical features described as the impregnable fastnesses of the Thern cult on Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are a formidable mountain range that contains the Golden Cliffs and impregnable fortresses.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are a geographic feature that hosts a fortified stronghold, characterized by a continuous line of impregnable fortifications.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are a geographical feature on Barsoom, marking the boundary of the Land of Lost Souls.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are a geographical location that was targeted by black battleships during a conflict with the Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are described as having impregnable fortifications, indicating their strategic importance and difficulty to breach.&lt;SEP&gt;The Mountains of Otz are the outer slopes surrounding the Valley Dor, part of the strategic landscape involved in the conflict.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9df9ebc1b25dd4de139a9defc734208&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89113c4da6f11aefb8678fe8526edbf0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c94071ebf05790657895dd5a92350321&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1b02017949859ea016f59b43ad5eeda2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ad5387a5bebe527b5c1302cedb859b9a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2d7747bf1bf113982bf92fc681219b66&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a36134f2c86fa620f5fc1afeb5c999e3</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE DEAD CUSTODIAN">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">The Dead Custodian is the former keeper of the chamber, whose keys are used to unlock various mechanisms.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-63a07d95b31bd7f0773a4e70c95dad9d</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SUBTERRANEAN GALLERIES">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Subterranean Galleries are underground areas where the Therns sought refuge from the attacks by black battleships.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9df9ebc1b25dd4de139a9defc734208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="THE BLUFFS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">The Bluffs are mighty perpendicular formations rising up from the river, enhancing the majestic nature of the landscape.&lt;SEP&gt;The Bluffs is a geographical location mentioned as the direction from which a strange shrieking wail emanates, influencing the actions of the herd.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-91e86645b0989df5782a6688160c1d8b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b274f937a3dc2f41dc46c714db0e1c59</data>
    </node>
    <node id="AGES AGO CONFLICT">
      <data key="d0">EVENT</data>
      <data key="d1">Ages Ago Conflict refers to a historical attack on the Therns by black battleships, which led to significant destruction and forced the Therns to retreat.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-e9df9ebc1b25dd4de139a9defc734208</data>
    </node>
    <node id="DWARS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Dwars are roles associated with giving commands during the crisis, indicating their position of authority or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;The dwars are individuals or a group being commanded to take action to avoid the flood.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a8c9fa2f165189b2177ca5c0e4a0b033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a2bea6eb93c07d5de217e100ae883e0c</data>
    </node>
    <node id="SEA OF OMEAN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Sea of Omean is a body of water where the Isle of Shador is located.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a body of water on Mars, in the land of the First Born, where the prison of Shador is located.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a body of water where the Cruiser ultimately sinks after the collision.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a geographical feature mentioned as being near the Isle of Shador.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a geographical feature on Barsoom, mentioned in relation to Shador.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a geographical location from which Carthoris, Kantos Kan, and the narrator plan to lead a smaller force.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a geographical location mentioned in the context of escape, suggesting it as a barrier or boundary.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a geographical location where the vessel is traveling, contributing to the setting of the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a location mentioned as part of the journey, suggesting its importance in the setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is a significant geographical location mentioned as part of the journey described, involving a descent and subsequent travel through a tunnel.&lt;SEP&gt;The Sea of Omean is described as an abysmal sea, suggesting it is a significant geographic feature within the story.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-64c0b713387801e1b22b06d3b9a3cc46&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-06c8b6e33f9e011b6bce4f39de022bf6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd54938ae10297f91951e3dc08c03318&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da397bcf9850c3ba624363a75bf205f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8f52f078afdf87c4aea647dd81d1df01&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f2c78a61cc0a501b49bd10b98af39acd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-47d378cc6dcca5a19ea2b10af50a96bb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1a5e676349eca8df4634b467d2aef249&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-935472cc7fa86ac74d68d6972f9a98b9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13123e8cc4e42bf2ebd1e6c36837aab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad069d3e03018513afb20c39dd315bf</data>
    </node>
    <node id="HOUSE OF TARDOS MORS">
      <data key="d0">ORGANIZATION</data>
      <data key="d1">House of Tardos Mors is a noble family or organization that John Carter is affiliated with, indicating lineage and status.&lt;SEP&gt;House of Tardos Mors is a noble house associated with John Carter, indicating his royal lineage.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Tardos Mors is a noble lineage associated with John Carter, suggesting a background of leadership and influence.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Tardos Mors is a noble lineage or organization with which John Carter is affiliated, suggesting royal or aristocratic connections.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Tardos Mors is a royal family, embodying tradition and reputation within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The House of Tardos Mors is a royal lineage to which the narrator belongs, associated with the leadership of Helium.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-c5360ea6efbfef241b4593260b36361e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-0e1589e9bc10a530649c9633fc000a9d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7d066fee844e2d8100274ab66d09c32&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-34e6c74f70eb14cd86afae56d8763706&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dbd0fd5cca73331a533757f7f594757&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b41c4f89a372b142a32bb11bf4f3a03f</data>
    </node>
