    <node id="PRINCE OF THE HOUSE OF TARDOS MORS">
      <data key="d0">ROLE</data>
      <data key="d1">A Prince of the House of Tardos Mors holds a significant position and is expected to uphold family and national honor.&lt;SEP&gt;A royal title indicating a position of nobility within the societal hierarchy of Helium, associated with leadership and governance.&lt;SEP&gt;The narrator holds the rank of Prince within the house of Tardos Mors, implying a high social status and expectation of courtesy and protection.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-0974acb08da1b4c1b92c316af33a88e1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-1ec0c5c3f38231c4a87625db9626c95a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-151c6925632d42abc6c6f08a41de7eb8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="KANTOS KAN">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Kantos Kan is a character accompanying the speaker and others to Zat Arrras' flagship, interacting with Zat Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character involved in a search and is tasked with bringing prisoners before Zat Arrras, indicating his role within the fleet and his interactions with authority figures.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character involved in the search for Dejah Thoris and Thuvia, receiving a message from Arrras.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character leading a group of red men into the throne room, indicating a role of leadership and support for the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character mentioned towards the end of the text, implying involvement in the situation at the coliseum.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character present at the gathering, sitting to the right of the narrator, indicating a position of significance or friendship.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who advises Prince and is concerned about the fleet's purpose being questioned by the people of Hastor.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who advises restraint to prevent mutiny and potential revolution, showing loyalty to Tardos Mors and Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who appears to be an ally or advisor to John Carter, providing whispered advice during the confrontation.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who awaits important information on the forward deck of the flagship.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who desires the rescued party to be brought to the deck of the _Xavarian_. He is portrayed as holding a significant position, possibly a leadership role.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who expresses deep affection for Carthoris and provides insight into the emotional state of Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who interacts with the Prince, indicating a role in military or strategic operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who is hesitant to discuss certain experiences, indicating a conflict between personal loyalty and deeply ingrained beliefs.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who is involved in the events surrounding the return to the _Xavarian_. He is contemplative about potential future calamities.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who is responsible for escorting John Carter and his party, indicating a role of authority or trust.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who observes the battle and is in a position to issue orders, indicating a role of leadership or authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who provides information about the date, impacting the protagonist's understanding of their mission's timeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who speculates about the identity and intentions of the spy, indicating his experience and insight.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a character who works alongside Carthoris and the narrator, leading a force towards the Temple of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a companion in the expedition, involved in the mission to enter the Temple of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a companion of John Carter, showing interest and anticipation in the potential leadership of John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a high-ranking officer in the navy of Helium, a brave comrade who has shared significant experiences with the narrator, including surviving a Warhoon dungeon and participating in the Great Games.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a key planner of the campaign, responsible for organizing the details of the air battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a leader of a group of a thousand red men who are involved in an assault on the temple.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a leader or commander of the ships engaged in Barsoomian naval warfare, orchestrating the tactical maneuvers and delivering broadsides.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a leader or commander overseeing the movements of Helium's battleships during the battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a leader who plays a strategic role in rallying support for the Prince of Helium by issuing a decisive signal during a naval battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a loyal supporter of Mors Kajak, remaining with him on the Throne of Righteousness and showing allegiance.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a loyal supporter who stands with others on the Throne of Righteousness and escorts the protagonist and his allies to their palace.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is a red noble accompanying the narrator on the journey to the Temple of the Sun.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual known for teaching a specific trick of gearing, indicating expertise in naval technology.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual who advocates for justice and fair treatment, intervening in a public trial setting to demand impartiality for the Prince of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual who communicated information about Sola to the narrator, impacting Tars Tarkas.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual who is aware of Zat Arrras' ambitions and the threat they pose to others.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual who is involved in a situation where they receive a radio-aerogram, indicating a significant role in the unfolding events.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an individual who is responsible for delivering instructions and overseeing the formation of battleships, indicating a leadership role in the campaign.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an officer concerned about the potential calamity that might befall Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an officer who defends the status of certain individuals, stating their noble connections and alliances.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is an officer who orders the rescued party to be brought to the deck of the battleship _Xavarian_.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is another member of the group with John Carter, suggesting a connection to the unfolding events.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is associated with receiving a radio-aerogram, indicating involvement in communication or navigation during a critical moment.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is involved in discussing and planning the details of the expedition, particularly in equipping a fleet.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is involved in executing plans laid nearly a year ago, facing challenges due to the need for secrecy and the presence of spies.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is involved in leading a smaller force alongside Carthoris and the narrator, indicating a leadership role in the operation.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is mentioned as a potential victim or prisoner of Zat Arrras, involved in discussions about selecting a new Jeddak and rescuing Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is one of the individuals awaiting the return of the protagonist in the audience chamber.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is responsible for remodelling the ships as part of a strategic plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is responsible for taking the vessels into dock and overseeing their preparation for entering Omean, indicating leadership and strategic planning abilities.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is the commander-in-chief of the navy, responsible for ordering battleships to be remodelled and overseeing the fleet's management.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is the father of Djor Kantos, indicating a familial connection and possible legacy of military involvement.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is the head of the navy of Helium and shows loyalty and leadership by defending John Carter and his party.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is the head of the navy of Helium, displaying leadership and defiance by rejecting the tribunal's verdict publicly.</data>
