    <node id="HOR VASTUS">
      <data key="d0">PERSON</data>
      <data key="d1">Hor Vastus is a character accompanying Kantos Kan, participating in the support of the narrator's group with a contingent of red men.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character present in the scene, who identifies the fallen individual as one of Zat Arrras' spies.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character responsible for recruiting a million veteran fighting men from Helium to man battleships, transports, and convoys, ensuring their loyalty and secrecy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who discovers the location of a cell and navigates the complex pits beneath Helium to reach it.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who dispatches air scouts to search for Thuvia, indicating a role in coordinating search efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who expresses trust in John Carter and has previously offered his blade in service.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who has a plan to thwart Zat Arrras' ambitions and intends to reveal it publicly one day.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who identifies a potential intruder and suggests pursuing them, showing initiative and alertness.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who identifies another character as one of Zat Arrras' spies.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who interacts with Carthoris and John Carter, showing surprise and concern upon seeing John Carter.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who is alert to suspicious activity and responds quickly to potential threats.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who laughs and discusses plans related to a new Jeddak and the rescue of Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who sits in a place of honor on Carthoris' side of the table, indicating a role of respect or authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a character who suggests John Carter as Jeddak of Helium, indicating support and recognition of his leadership qualities.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a follower of John Carter who receives a sword as a token of fealty and is trusted to use it in the cause of truth and justice.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a leader of red men, involved in the assault on Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a noble Martian who demonstrates loyalty and honor by unbuckling his scabbard and flinging his sword at the feet of the narrator, signifying his fealty and devotion.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a noble character who offers his sword to John Carter as a gesture of honor and loyalty.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a person of honor, sitting at the side of Carthoris, suggesting a role of importance or leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is a red noble who is part of the group led by the narrator to the Temple of the Sun.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is also present in the audience chamber, suggesting a role in the ongoing plans.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is an officer who recognizes and greets Carthoris with surprise and pleasure, suggesting familiarity and respect.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is another character traveling with Carthoris and Tars Tarkas to Thark.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is another leader of a group of a thousand red men participating in the temple assault.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is associated with fliers returning to the _Xavarian_, indicating his involvement in the search efforts for Thuvia.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is included in the group with John Carter, indicating involvement in the current crisis.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is mentioned as a potential victim or prisoner of Zat Arrras, involved in discussions about selecting a new Jeddak and rescuing Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is part of the group discussing the expedition details, suggesting a role in leadership or strategy.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is portrayed as a noble individual who infiltrates Parthak's cell to gain his trust and extract information.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is responsible for organizing a secret force of fighting men sworn to follow John Carter, tasked with assembling over a million men for a significant military mission.&lt;SEP&gt;Hor Vastus is responsible for organizing a secret force of fighting-men sworn to follow John Carter.</data>
