    <node id="TEMPLE OF ISSUS">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Temple of Issus is a location towards which the protagonist is advancing, implying its importance in the plot.&lt;SEP&gt;Temple of Issus is a significant location that the protagonist hopes to enter, linked to the mission's objectives.&lt;SEP&gt;Temple of Issus is a strategic target for the assembled horde and fleet.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a destination accessible through a passageway connected to the Sea of Omean, indicating its importance in the journey.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a destination or significant location that the group aims to reach through the upper pits.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a golden structure on Mars, adorned with various precious stones and currently on fire.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a key location targeted for assault by the combined forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location associated with the Goddess Issus, from which John Carter claims to have returned.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location guarded by plant men and great white apes, serving as a site from which pilgrims might drift to the Therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location mentioned as being near the upper pits, indicating its significance in the narrative setting.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location mentioned as central to Xodar's country, believed by Phaidor to be associated with Life Eternal, but potentially a place of torture and death.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location of significance, potentially a destination or objective within the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location on Barsoom that is significant to the plot, potentially where Dejah Thoris is held.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location on Barsoom where unthinkable atrocities are heaped upon fair women.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location that must be reached secretly before an impending assault by Tars Tarkas's forces.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a location where a great tumult involving black, red, and green men is occurring, and it is on fire.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a magnificent structure described with burnished gold and intricate designs, contributing to the scene's splendor.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a mysterious organization with gilded walls, holding secrets that have never been revealed since the beginning of time.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a sacred location guarded by plant men and great white apes, associated with religious significance.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a significant location on Barsoom, associated with the deity Issus and considered sacred by the therns.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a significant location that the expedition aims to enter, associated with the fate of Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a significant location where a critical event is set to occur, specifically the rescue of a Princess.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is a significant location within the narrative, described as having a complex structure with an inner court and a little temple that raises a thin spire above the larger surrounding temple.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is an organization that holds significant power or reverence, causing fear or respect in others.&lt;SEP&gt;The Temple of Issus is referenced as a significant and potentially powerful institution feared or respected by the character in the text.</data>
      <data key="d2">chunk-a5068f52c923549934726130060ee89e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4d326ad7454f10313352505bb827bb89&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-9ac788a7f0b0f7041a03297b242b6cad&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-923f3704592d0c1131d92378ee957a21&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-46817f0e5364d880844af125e330b888&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ef83a1bb59d0a6160845638665b9ef6f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2bf22396435379360201facb4abd270f&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a8c9fa2f165189b2177ca5c0e4a0b033&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d2ea7458d8583dfbde88866c8e4d86e2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-87b6b9321f4f05f0578fcd6c878db520&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-d9d4dcc65f8faed5a3466318ce785313&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-03a915a3180626dc866431172c413ae7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c17bb33df2ff9d9289d6824b20a85169&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-da397bcf9850c3ba624363a75bf205f9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-214f06aa11fe94cd8053753efc32c5f7&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7dbcafdba492eee56a86676200e0270b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c323bce2bc6dde08ce8080a58eccc7b0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-cead3080c3879bc999f5b5b6ec863019&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-29d75a8b07d711ce1eff0a8d3d37c746&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-89015e03c34ca60483685acd4b9fc408&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8c77572865c7949fb289c8ad54e38a34&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e68c808037e36d2554d82e6adc14f58d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-91388cfb9b19f81432eafb4bca1d653b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01c317929db219c46232f998050022ca</data>
