    </node>
    <node id="OMEAN">
      <data key="d0">GEO</data>
      <data key="d1">Omean is a body of water encountered in the dark corridor beneath the temple, representing a physical and metaphorical barrier.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a body of water mentioned in the text, possibly a significant geographical feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a body of water that the characters are swimming in, located beneath a rocky dome.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a body of water that the narrator dives into to escape, indicating its geographical significance in the scene.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a destination that the battleships are guarding the way to, indicating strategic importance in the campaign.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a geographic location that is the target destination of the fleet, indicating its strategic importance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a geographical feature described as having a dome structure, with rising waters that pose a threat to an expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a geographical location mentioned as the chapter title, potentially significant to the story's setting or events.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a geographical location with an opening leading to the outer world, and its map is studied for the escape plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a geographical location, possibly a body of water, where specific cultural or ritual activities occur, such as the marking of day-end with a call and the spreading of silks.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location associated with a significant event involving hostile fleets and is mentioned as a place where the First Born fleet should have been contained.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location associated with phosphorescent rock that provides illumination, suggesting it is an important geological feature.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location associated with pumps that have been stopped, causing the water level to rise and posing a threat to the characters.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location characterized by a glowing dome, suggesting a distinct or possibly technologically advanced environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location characterized by phosphorescent radiance, serving as a point of reference for steering during a high-speed journey through a shaft.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location described as having lax discipline, and it is the secret base of a fleet on Barsoom, unknown to enemies.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location mentioned as a significant place related to John Carter, implying some future events or changes.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location mentioned as a strategic point that needs guarding, possibly a crucial site in military operations.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location mentioned by Yersted where the fleet is expected to return, indicating its strategic importance.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location mentioned in relation to the stopping of pumps, indicating its significance in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location on Mars, described as lying two miles below the surface crust of the planet.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location that is being blocked by vessels and is significant in the context of the First Born's activities.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location that is central to the mission, requiring a large force to man battleships and transports.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location that requires specialized equipment for navigation, suggesting it is a challenging or unique environment.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location where significant events, including a massacre, are taking place. It is connected to the amphitheatre and the submarine pool.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location where the events are taking place, characterized by the absence of conventional compass directions and a chaotic environment during a conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a location where the fleet of the First Born was supposed to be contained, implying its strategic importance in the expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a region accessible via the water shaft, potentially leading to a sea with many islands.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a sea through which a smaller force led by Carthoris, Kantos Kan, and the narrator plans to advance towards the Temple of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a subterranean location where the sun does not penetrate, illuminated by phosphorescent rocks and characterized by rolling billows.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is a subterranean vault characterized by rocks that emit light and a windless sea with rolling billows.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is described as a buried sea, where a fleet of vessels rests, indicating a hidden or protected location.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is described as a location where every direction is due north, and it features a dome with a shaft leading to the world above.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is described as a rocky dome under which ships are stationed, and an alarm is a rare occurrence here.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is described as a significant location where the battle takes place and where the First Born have their harbor.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is the destination where the fleet is being prepared to go, indicating its importance as a location in the expedition.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is the geographical location that the protagonist and their team are progressing towards, characterized by a cone-like summit.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is the location where the fleet plans to enter and destroy the vessels of the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Omean is the target location for a future mission involving a remodelled fleet of battleships.</data>
