    <edge source="ISSUS" target="JOHN CARTER">
      <data key="d3">65.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Issus is fearful of John Carter, indicating a conflict or threat posed by him.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter challenges the mightiest of Issus's fighting-men, indicating a direct confrontation with Issus's forces.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter exposes Issus as a false deity, refusing to kill her, thus sparking a shift in perception among the people.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter has allegedly blasphemed against Issus, the Goddess of Death and Life Eternal.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is determined to protect the people from the falsehoods associated with Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is intensely focused on finding Issus within the temple, suggesting a strong desire for confrontation or resolution.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter's ideas have led the speaker to question the divinity and authenticity of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter's mission involves confronting Issus, who holds Dejah Thoris captive.</data>
      <data key="d5">conflict, religious belief&lt;SEP&gt;conflict, rescue&lt;SEP&gt;confrontation, challenge&lt;SEP&gt;fear, threat&lt;SEP&gt;influence, skepticism&lt;SEP&gt;protection, ideology&lt;SEP&gt;revelation, moral stance&lt;SEP&gt;search, confrontation</data>
