    <edge source="ISSUS" target="FIRST BORN">
      <data key="d3">64.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Issus and the First Born are part of a religious hierarchy that is now being questioned for authenticity and holiness.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus and the First Born are related as forces of control, with Issus possibly being a deity or authority figure influencing the First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus is associated with the First Born, as the narrator confronts her within their domains, indicating a relationship of power and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus maintains prisoners under the status of First Born.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus may choose to punish nobles of the First Born by imprisoning them in the Temple of the Sun.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are fighting to protect Issus and maintain her authority, indicating their allegiance.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born are protected by Issus, who has lived for countless ages, signifying her importance to them.&lt;SEP&gt;The First Born serve Issus by fighting and dying for her, which is considered a sacred duty.</data>
      <data key="d5">hierarchy, religious doubt&lt;SEP&gt;imprisonment, power dynamics&lt;SEP&gt;loyalty, defense&lt;SEP&gt;power dynamics, control&lt;SEP&gt;protection, reverence&lt;SEP&gt;punishment, authority&lt;SEP&gt;sacred duty, divine service</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-04a29095babe1a2ff500039fc4979ce0&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a027e972d7eb768695014c7c960f5758&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-eae83a9d328abc751e8b03536497faf5&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dbe729ce46c2462fad11275ee94493b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-13123e8cc4e42bf2ebd1e6c36837aab2&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2dceb1683460906a1f380e987a784c31&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-7bc8ba319c10b95a0296d782317a73a9&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac8c4010c210dcbb6da5ccd528fdf874</data>
    </edge>
