    <edge source="ISSUS" target="XODAR">
      <data key="d3">110.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Issus and her retinue had passed before Xodar is seen surrounded by a hostile crowd, indicating a possible connection or preceding event.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus commands Xodar to serve as a slave, indicating her authority over him.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus gives commands that directly affect Xodar, placing him in a position of potential persecution and humiliation.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus has degraded Xodar, indicating a relationship of authority and subjugation.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus holds power over Xodar, dictating that he be subjected to mistreatment and degradation.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus punishes Xodar by demoting him from a Dator to a slave due to disgrace, demonstrating authority and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar acts under the command of Issus, indicating a hierarchical relationship of authority and obedience.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar believes in Issus's omnipotence and omniscience and fears her wrath.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar has previously bested Thurid in the secret councils of Issus, indicating strategic or political success.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar has served Issus by delivering messages, revealing the manipulative nature of Issus over Barsoomian society.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar is a faithful follower of Issus, but his beliefs are challenged by the Speaker who reveals Issus's mortality.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar is affected by the belief in Issus, which the speaker challenges, indicating a conflict between personal beliefs and external influence.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar presents prisoners to Issus, indicating a connection or duty towards Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Xodar was once powerful under Issus's favor but now faces persecution, indicating a fall from grace.</data>
      <data key="d5">authority, command&lt;SEP&gt;authority, degradation&lt;SEP&gt;authority, disfavor&lt;SEP&gt;authority, obedience&lt;SEP&gt;authority, power dynamics&lt;SEP&gt;authority, punishment&lt;SEP&gt;belief system, ideological conflict&lt;SEP&gt;deception, servitude&lt;SEP&gt;faith, belief challenge&lt;SEP&gt;faith, fear&lt;SEP&gt;favor, persecution&lt;SEP&gt;political strategy, success&lt;SEP&gt;power dynamics, subjugation&lt;SEP&gt;service, duty</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-3964e585dee08446ad325587a718d0b1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-a292b6d7aae5528de2d633ec624a151c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac21fdcaba1072d7aae816bc5a5b7e84&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-ac274835cf15fd4d19a41f986b75a81a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-099b24e2ed3a239625f97efd0db9934c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f9269232f99d91f950b2e2e1efcd036d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dd1602bdc35e6e17999a40b105c63f6e&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6c1de3b9f0e7f1ea967106856be68ebb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4638e15286baadf00497251d2c1faa42&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-09e03da8ccb26edbf8fde791db77d403&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f7a22c0c45b96f211a7e6f3fec2419c6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b6936386cb94820c7f5a584ca537f27d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-979f880555ab53fcbf9eeb67a9056e54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-aad069d3e03018513afb20c39dd315bf</data>
