    <edge source="ISSUS" target="DEJAH THORIS">
      <data key="d3">65.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Dejah Thoris is remembered by Issus as the wife of John Carter and mother of another rebel, highlighting her indirect role in opposing Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Dejah Thoris participates in the rites of Issus and is potentially at risk due to the actions of her family against the Goddess.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus controls the fate of Dejah Thoris, whose life and death are dictated by its rules.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus has control over Dejah Thoris and intends to prevent her rescue.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus has placed Dejah Thoris under guard, indicating a position of power or authority over her.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus has the power to choose individuals like Dejah Thoris, who live only for a single year, influencing her fate.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus is believed to have chosen Dejah Thoris to serve her, creating a direct conflict in the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;Issus is blamed for the death of Dejah Thoris, which deeply impacts the narrator.</data>
      <data key="d5">authority, tension&lt;SEP&gt;captivity, conflict&lt;SEP&gt;captivity, control&lt;SEP&gt;causality, vengeance&lt;SEP&gt;control, fate&lt;SEP&gt;divine interaction, risk&lt;SEP&gt;opposition, divine conflict&lt;SEP&gt;power, fate</data>
