      <data key="d3">67.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Issus has control over Phaidor's fate, as Phaidor is presented to Issus and may be selected as a slave.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor claims immortality through Issus, indicating a belief or cultural connection.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor experiences a profound emotional response upon encountering Issus, indicating Issus's powerful presence.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor fears the alliance of Issus, indicating a relationship of fear and doubt towards the potentially sinister influence of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor has looked upon Issus, indicating a shared experience or understanding with the narrator.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is one of the female slaves surrounding Issus, indicating a power dynamic and subjugation.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor is seen reacting emotionally to Issus, indicating a relationship or significant interaction between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor lags behind Issus's retinue, indicating her connection and possibly lesser status.&lt;SEP&gt;Phaidor reacts fearfully to the command involving Issus, indicating a relationship of fear and reverence.</data>
