      <data key="d3">147.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Dejah Thoris and John Carter are married, forming a royal family that includes Carthoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Dejah Thoris loves John Carter, which connects them emotionally.&lt;SEP&gt;Dejah Thoris provides emotional support and urges John Carter to save himself, indicating a close relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter and Dejah Thoris are connected through past experiences or interactions, likely significant in nature.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter and Dejah Thoris share a deep connection, with Dejah Thoris longing for John Carter's return.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter and Dejah Thoris share a deep emotional bond, highlighted by their reunion and expressions of love.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter and Dejah Thoris share a deep love and devotion, which is central to the narrative.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter has a deep affection for Dejah Thoris, the Martian Princess, indicating a strong emotional connection.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is approaching to demand accountability for the imprisonment of Dejah Thoris.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is concerned about Dejah Thoris' fate and is determined to act in a way that honors her values.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is deeply concerned about Dejah Thoris's health and safety.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is married to Dejah Thoris, and their relationship is significant due to his escape from Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is on a mission to rescue Dejah Thoris from the clutches of Issus.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter remains devoted to Dejah Thoris, expressing his love despite the circumstances.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter won Dejah Thoris as his wife, indicating a strong personal relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter's loyalty and devotion to Dejah Thoris are central to the narrative, impacting her emotionally.</data>
