    <edge source="JOHN CARTER" target="HELIUM">
      <data key="d3">165.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Helium's actions or stance influence the decisions regarding John Carter within the Thark community.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter addresses the people of Helium, indicating his influence and importance in their lives.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter addresses the people of Helium, indicating his influence and leadership in the location.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter holds the title of Jeddak in Helium, indicating his authority and leadership.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter holds the title of Jeddak of Helium, indicating his leadership and connection to this location.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is Jeddak of Helium, indicating his leadership and authority over this location.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is a leader in Helium, attempting to prevent civil strife by addressing the crowd and calling for peace.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is associated with Helium as its Prince, indicating a leadership role within this location.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is being judged by the people and judges of Helium, where he was once a Prince.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is committed to ensuring a fair election for the next Jeddak of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is considered a traitor to Helium, suggesting a conflict or betrayal.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is referred to as Jeddak of Helium, indicating his leadership or rule over this region.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is referred to as the Prince of Helium, indicating a significant relationship with this location, possibly as his place of origin or authority.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is the Prince of Helium and has returned to the nation after a period of absence.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter is traveling to Helium, which is the destination of his journey.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter references Helium as he charges into battle, showing his allegiance and motivation.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter was a prince in the house of Tardos Mors, indicating a political role in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter's actions led to Zodanga becoming a vassal to Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter's leadership garners loyalty and could sway the political balance in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;John Carter, as a prince of the House of Tardos Mors, is involved in the political and leadership dynamics of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;The people of Helium wanted the narrator's son to be named after John Carter, indicating their respect for him.</data>
