      <data key="d3">113.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Tars Tarkas aims to communicate with Thark to assess his people's sentiments and potentially gather support.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas exemplifies the warrior traits and physical prowess associated with the Thark race.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is a member of the Thark race, demonstrating his cultural and racial identity.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is a member of the Thark, a group known for seeking death rather than life, which contrasts with his current actions of fleeing.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is associated with Thark, a group or race that he belongs to.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is identified as a Thark, highlighting his role and societal standing among Martians.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is the Jeddak, or leader, of Thark, showcasing his leadership and status among the green men of Barsoom.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is the leader of Thark, commanding its warriors in a historic event.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is the leader of Thark, demonstrating his leadership and influence within the organization.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas is the leader of Thark, indicating a hierarchical relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas leads the Thark warriors, showing his role as their commander in battle.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas may be associated with the Thark, as there is an intent to learn about his prison in the context of Thark being taken before Kab Kadja.&lt;SEP&gt;Tars Tarkas mentions leaving his short-sword in the Thark's cell, indicating a connection or previous encounter with the Thark.&lt;SEP&gt;Thark and Tars Tarkas share a bond of friendship, and Thark urges Tars Tarkas to retreat for strategic reasons.</data>
