    <edge source="ZAT ARRRAS" target="KANTOS KAN">
      <data key="d3">111.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Kantos Kan challenges Zat Arrras's authority by demanding justice and fair treatment for the Prince of Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan discusses the protagonist's time in the pits of Zat Arrras, influencing the mission timeline.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is aware of Zat Arrras' ambitions and perceives them as a threat to Dejah Thoris and Carthoris.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is commanded by Zat Arrras to bring prisoners before him, indicating a hierarchical relationship and the execution of authority.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan is worried about the actions Zat Arrras might take against fugitives in Helium.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan opposes Zat Arrras by rallying support for John Carter, leading to a conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan receives a message from Zat Arrras, indicating communication regarding the search efforts.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan speculates that Zat Arrras is behind the spy's actions, indicating suspicion and historical context.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan's actions result in some of Zat Arrras' ships switching allegiance to the Prince of Helium, indicating a shift in the battle dynamics.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan's efforts to execute plans are hindered by Zat Arrras' spies, creating a conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Kantos Kan's sneer towards Zat Arrras suggests disdain and opposition.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras commands officers to seize someone, while Kantos Kan intervenes to prevent conflict, showing opposing approaches to authority and conflict.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras might have Kantos Kan as a prisoner or victim, indicating a conflict or threat between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras questions Kantos Kan about the disarming of prisoners, indicating a direct interaction concerning authority and control.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras sends a surrender demand to Kantos Kan, indicating a conflict or confrontation between their respective groups.</data>
      <data key="d5">authority, command&lt;SEP&gt;authority, conflict prevention&lt;SEP&gt;authority, interrogation&lt;SEP&gt;awareness, threat&lt;SEP&gt;challenge, authority&lt;SEP&gt;communication, coordination&lt;SEP&gt;conflict, authority&lt;SEP&gt;conflict, espionage&lt;SEP&gt;conflict, imprisonment&lt;SEP&gt;disdain, conflict&lt;SEP&gt;fear, potential conflict&lt;SEP&gt;opposition, conflict&lt;SEP&gt;strategy, conflict&lt;SEP&gt;suspicion, historical context&lt;SEP&gt;time misreckoning, location significance</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-a356f2ca641af882f4389e64c1cfe156&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fec090a1531505a82f52e76f197bd709&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-6e2515053cf8b27bec37582a93f80564&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c093b23e9b64e59d4454ce39258f9d86&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-e029e53f82ffdbeba2500285e859f464&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-5e4bea953f1bd40bf6d9a85e314fdbeb&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-18baf96786d50da1cc2652ec45a9b1cc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8de0958c186ba3135c1e8cf7f85bf340&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-3806151a083dd701c29455b3a3f12e94&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01455886e310937a5b5e517c7050fde1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-c83fa3ad9e9d77a8f079c91c9d9b7717&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e9d5b5bb51756648e7a02983977bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8dd702bb82bfdc458cb9b1d6020448ed&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-fc0af3b312b7ff86a8268a91122bb6fc&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f804d99b0560937dece663ce5c7f98</data>
    </edge>
    <edge source="ZAT ARRRAS" target="CARTHORIS">
      <data key="d3">48.0</data>
      <data key="d4">Carthoris acts against Zat Arrras by freeing the narrator and slaying a guard, indicating opposition to Zat Arrras's occupation of the palace.&lt;SEP&gt;Carthoris is involved in delivering a note that is assured to be harmless to Zat Arrras, indicating a link through the planned task.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras does not acknowledge or greet Carthoris, showing a lack of recognition or friendliness.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras fears the public's love for Carthoris, which could lead to demonstrations against the charges.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras may also be holding Carthoris captive, suggesting an antagonistic relationship.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras might have Carthoris as a prisoner or victim, indicating a conflict or threat between them.&lt;SEP&gt;Zat Arrras sees Carthoris as an obstacle to his goal of becoming Jeddak, as Carthoris is another contender for power.</data>
      <data key="d5">animosity, indifference&lt;SEP&gt;captivity, antagonism&lt;SEP&gt;conflict, imprisonment&lt;SEP&gt;opposition, resistance&lt;SEP&gt;public sentiment, fear&lt;SEP&gt;rivalry, power struggle&lt;SEP&gt;task involvement, assurance</data>
      <data key="d6">chunk-188e20abff12b91977ee19e7cec8de54&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b5ec04b19f44e50aea83ee65f6472738&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-01455886e310937a5b5e517c7050fde1&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f5e9d5b5bb51756648e7a02983977bdd&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8917f33ca9393e6e40d34847a0b96e2d&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bfc3d412e05467116b42fd3c9af8d965&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-69f804d99b0560937dece663ce5c7f98</data>
    </edge>
